      "name": "DestroyCallbackQueue",
      "signature": "void DestroyCallbackQueue(CallbackQueue * pQueue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Destroys a callback queue by freeing all nodes and deleting the critical section.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock via Ordinal_10050\n2. Get list head pointer from pQueue+0x1c\n3. While list is not empty:\n   a. Save next node pointer (node+0x4)\n   b. Free current node via Ordinal_10043\n   c. Update list head to next node\n4. Clear list head (0x1c) and count (0x20) fields\n5. Delete critical section via DeleteCriticalSection\n\nParameters:\n- pQueue (CallbackQueue*): Pointer to queue structure containing critical section and linked list\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nStructure Layout:\n| Offset | Size | Field           |\n|--------|------|-----------------|\n| 0x00   | 4    | dwUnknown       |\n| 0x04   | 24   | criticalSection |\n| 0x1c   | 4    | pListHead       |\n| 0x20   | 4    | nCount          |",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
