      "name": "EnqueueSocketMessage",
      "signature": "void EnqueueSocketMessage(void * pSocket, byte * pbData, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Allocates a message node and enqueues it to the socket's message queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate size is non-zero (assert on failure)\n2. Enter critical section at pSocket+0x4\n3. Allocate message node: size + 8 bytes (2-byte size + 4-byte next + data)\n4. Store size as ushort at node[0], set next pointer to 0\n5. Copy data to node+8 using DWORD then BYTE copy loops\n6. Link node to queue: if empty, set head/tail; else append to tail\n7. Leave critical section\n\nParameters:\n- pSocket (void*): Pointer to socket context structure\n- pbData (byte*): Source data buffer to copy\n- dwSize (uint): Size of data (lower 16 bits used, max 0x1FFF)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMessage Node Layout (0x8 + dwSize bytes):\n- 0x0: ushort wSize - message size\n- 0x2: 2 bytes padding\n- 0x4: void* pNext - next node pointer\n- 0x8: byte[] data - message payload\n\nSocket Queue Fields:\n- +0x04: CRITICAL_SECTION\n- +0x1C: pHead - queue head pointer\n- +0x20: pTail - queue tail pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
