      "name": "SendNetworkData",
      "signature": "bool SendNetworkData(int nConn, char * szBuffer, ushort wLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Sends data over a network connection with thread-safety.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate connection pointer and socket structure at offset 0x110\n2. Acquire critical section lock via Ordinal_10010\n3. If buffer valid and length > 0, send data via Ordinal_10009 (WinSock send)\n4. Release lock via Ordinal_10011\n5. Return true if all bytes sent, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- nConn (int): Connection object pointer (socket struct at +0x110)\n- szBuffer (char*): Data buffer to send\n- wLength (ushort): Number of bytes to send\n\nReturns:\n- true if wLength bytes sent successfully, false on error or invalid params\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x110: Offset to socket structure within connection object",
