      "name": "SpawnStormWorkerThread",
      "signature": "dword SpawnStormWorkerThread(void * pWorkerCtx)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Thread procedure that spawns a Storm worker thread via Ordinal_10003.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Storm Ordinal_10003 with context sync object, priority, thread proc, and name\n2. Store returned thread handle in context structure at offset 0x110\n3. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pWorkerCtx (void*): Worker context structure containing sync object at +0x8,\n  thread priority at +0x10C, and thread name at +0x124\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset   Field\n  +0x008   Critical section or sync object\n  +0x10C   Thread priority parameter\n  +0x110   Storm thread handle (output)\n  +0x124   Thread name string",
