      "name": "SignalResourceStop",
      "signature": "void SignalResourceStop(void * pResource)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Signals a resource to stop by setting termination flags and releasing critical section.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pResource is non-NULL\n2. Get inner control block at pResource+0x110\n3. Check if control block exists and is active (offset 0x24 != 0)\n4. Set termination flag at pResource+0x120 to 1\n5. Enter critical section at control block+0xc (via Ordinal_10050)\n6. Set stop flag at control block+0x2c to 1\n7. Leave critical section\n\nParameters:\n- pResource (void*): Pointer to resource context structure\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x110: Offset to inner control block pointer\n- 0x120: Offset to termination pending flag\n- 0x24: Offset to active state flag in control block\n- 0x2c: Offset to stop request flag in control block\n- 0xc: Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION in control block",
