      "name": "EncodeVarInt2Byte",
      "signature": "void EncodeVarInt2Byte(byte * pbOutput, uint dwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Encodes a value into 2-byte variable-length integer format with continuation bits.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Takes lower 7 bits of dwValue, sets bit 7 (0x80), stores at pbOutput[0]\n2. Shifts dwValue right by 7, takes lower 7 bits, sets bit 7, stores at pbOutput[1]\n\nParameters:\n- pbOutput (byte*): Destination buffer, must be at least 2 bytes\n- dwValue (uint): Value to encode (up to 14 bits, 0-16383)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x80: Continuation bit flag (indicates more bytes follow in VLQ encoding)\n- 7: Bits per encoded byte (standard VLQ uses 7 data bits per byte)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d8f75e5bed8df576bcfaf542858e6c54",
