      "name": "InitBitBuffer",
      "signature": "void InitBitBuffer(dword * pBitBuffer, byte * pbSource, int nByteCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a BitBuffer structure for bit-level read/write operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pBitBuffer is not null (assertion)\n2. Set source pointer (offset 0x0)\n3. Set total bit count (nByteCount * 8) at offset 0x4\n4. Clear current bit position (offset 0x8) to 0\n5. Clear state flags (offset 0xC) to 0\n\nParameters:\n- pBitBuffer (dword*): Pointer to 16-byte BitBuffer structure\n- pbSource (byte*): Source data buffer pointer\n- nByteCount (int): Number of bytes in source buffer\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout:\n| Offset | Size | Field          |\n|--------|------|----------------|\n| 0x0    | 4    | Source pointer |\n| 0x4    | 4    | Total bits     |\n| 0x8    | 4    | Current pos    |\n| 0xC    | 4    | State/flags    |\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10128: WriteBits - writes bits to buffer\n- Ordinal_10130: ReadBits - reads bits from buffer\n- Ordinal_10135: PackString - packs string using bit buffer\n- Ordinal_10136: UnpackString - unpacks string from bit buffer",
