      "name": "WriteBitsFromTable",
      "signature": "void WriteBitsFromTable(int * pBitBuf, int * pBitTable, int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Writes bits from indexed entry in a bit descriptor table to a bit buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate offset into pBitTable using nIndex * 8 (8-byte stride)\n2. Read dwValue from pBitTable[nIndex].offset_0\n3. Read nBitCount from pBitTable[nIndex].offset_4\n4. Call WriteBitsToBuffer(pBitBuf, dwValue, nBitCount)\n5. Return (void function)\n\nParameters:\n- pBitBuf (int*): Pointer to bit buffer structure for output\n- pBitTable (int*): Pointer to array of 8-byte bit descriptors\n- nIndex (int): Zero-based index into the bit descriptor table\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout (BitTableEntry, 8 bytes):\n| Offset | Size | Field     | Description          |\n|--------|------|-----------|----------------------|\n| 0x0    | 4    | dwValue   | Bit value to write   |\n| 0x4    | 4    | nBitCount | Number of bits       |\n\nRelated Functions:\n- WriteBitsToBuffer (0x6ff620f0): Core bit writing implementation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
