      "name": "PackStringToBitBuffer",
      "signature": "void PackStringToBitBuffer(int * pStrPack, char * szString, byte * pbBuffer, int nBufferSize, int nNullTerminate)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Packs a string into a bit buffer using variable-width character encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate inputs: pStrPack, szString, pbBuffer must be non-null\n2. Validate pStrPack->nPackedBits is non-zero\n3. Initialize bit buffer with pbBuffer and nBufferSize\n4. Calculate max chars: (nBitCount * nBufferSize + 7) >> 3\n5. If nNullTerminate, decrement max by 1 to reserve space for null\n6. Loop: for each char in szString until null or max reached\n   - Look up packed value via pStrPack[char + 1] lookup table\n   - Write nBitCount bits to buffer\n7. If nNullTerminate or chars remain, write null terminator (0 bits)\n\nParameters:\n- pStrPack (int*): String pack structure with nPackedBits at offset 0\n                   and char-to-packed lookup table at offset 4\n- szString (char*): Null-terminated input string to pack\n- pbBuffer (byte*): Output buffer for packed bit data\n- nBufferSize (int): Size of output buffer in bytes\n- nNullTerminate (int): If non-zero, write null terminator at end\n\nReturns:\n- void (asserts on invalid input)\n\nStructure Layout (pStrPack):\n| Offset | Size | Field           |\n|--------|------|-----------------|\n| 0x0    | 4    | nPackedBits     |\n| 0x4+   | 256  | Char lookup tbl |\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitBitBuffer: Initializes BitBuffer for writing\n- WriteBitsToBuffer: Writes bits to buffer\n- UnpackString: Reverse operation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:aec2395dc44f2705e2c97e819c3c6f42",
