      "name": "ClearAllBucketLists",
      "signature": "int ClearAllBucketLists(void * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Clears all bucket lists and frees their nodes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return early if bucket count is 0\n2. For each bucket index:\n   a. Acquire critical section lock\n   b. Capture head node from bucket array\n   c. Clear bucket head and tail pointers\n   d. Release critical section lock\n   e. Walk linked list, freeing each node via Ordinal_10043\n3. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (void*): Context structure with bucket arrays at:\n  - +0x854: CRITICAL_SECTION for synchronization\n  - +0x870: Array of bucket head pointers\n  - +0x874: Array of bucket tail pointers\n  - +0x87c: Bucket count\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5bc: Offset to next node pointer in linked list\n- 0x854: Critical section offset in context\n- 0x870: Bucket head array offset\n- 0x874: Bucket tail array offset\n- 0x87c: Bucket count offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:c49e429976faabc43d86aeeceef72c20",
