      "name": "QSrvAddClient",
      "signature": "dword * QSrvAddClient(dword * ptServer, dword dwSocket, dword dwAddr)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new client structure for the QServer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x644 byte TQCLIENT structure via Fog heap (Ordinal_10042)\n2. Zero-initialize all 0x191 dwords of the structure\n3. Lock server critical section and increment client ID counter\n4. Store socket handle, IP address, and initial state values\n5. Initialize per-client critical section at offset 0x2c\n6. Link client into ID hash table at server offset 0x14\n7. Link client into IP hash table at server offset 0x20\n8. Update or create IP address reference count node\n9. Increment server total client count at offset 0x880\n10. Log client addition with inet_ntoa for IP string conversion\n\nParameters:\n- ptServer (dword*): Pointer to TQSERVER structure\n- dwSocket (dword): Socket handle for this client\n- dwAddr (dword): Client IP address as in_addr\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to newly allocated TQCLIENT structure (never NULL)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x644: TQCLIENT structure size\n- 0x191 (401): TQCLIENT size in dwords\n- 0x854: Server main critical section offset\n- 0x880: Server total client count offset\n- 0xc: IP reference node size (addr, count, next)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
