      "name": "ProcessTimerTick",
      "signature": "void ProcessTimerTick(int nTimerCtx)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Processes timer tick events, decrementing timeout counters and recycling expired entries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize lastTickCount if unset (-1)\n2. Check if 1000+ ms elapsed since last tick\n3. Enter critical section via Ordinal_10050\n4. Iterate through all timer buckets\n5. For each timer entry: decrement delay/timeout by elapsed seconds\n6. If entry fully expired, unlink from bucket list\n7. Move expired entry to free list at offset 0x88c\n8. Decrement active count at offset 0x890\n9. Leave critical section via LeaveCriticalSection\n10. If entries expired and 2000ms since last cleanup, call NullStubProc\n\nParameters:\n- nTimerCtx (int): Pointer to timer manager context structure\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x888: lastTickCount offset in context\n- 0x88c: freeList head offset\n- 0x890: activeCount offset\n- 0x894: criticalSection offset\n- 0x8ac: bucketArray pointer offset\n- 0x8b0: bucketCount offset\n- 0x78 (120): Default timeout in seconds\n- 1000: Milliseconds threshold for processing\n- 2000: Cleanup callback throttle interval (ms)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:44e1de2e8adb85b98c05499e3a65ec6f",
