      "name": "AddIpToBlockCache",
      "signature": "void AddIpToBlockCache(void * this, uint dwIpAddr, uint dwContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Adds an IP address to the server's blocked IP cache with timeout.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if server is initialized (offset 0xbd0)\n2. Check allowlist: iterate server's IP/mask pairs at +0x48 against g_adwCidrNetmasks\n3. If IP matches any allowlist entry, return without blocking\n4. Invoke optional callback at +0xbb8 with dwContext\n5. Enter critical section at +0x894\n6. Hash IP by modulo bucket count at +0x8b0\n7. Search hash chain at +0x8ac for existing entry\n8. If found: reset timeout to 0x78 (120) and return\n9. If not found: allocate 16-byte node from free list at +0x88c or via Ordinal_10042\n10. Insert node into hash bucket, increment count at +0x890\n11. Leave critical section\n12. Throttle logging: call NullStubProc if >2000ms since last log\n\nParameters:\n- this (ECX): QServer instance pointer\n- dwIpAddr: IP address to block (network byte order)\n- dwContext: Context value passed to callback\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x78 (120): Block cache entry timeout in ticks\n- 0x10 (16): Size of cache entry node (4 DWORDs)\n- 0x7d0 (2000): Log throttle interval in milliseconds\n\nStructure Offsets (QServer):\n- +0x48: Allowlist IP array base\n- +0x4c: Allowlist mask index array\n- +0x848: Allowlist entry count\n- +0x88c: Free list head pointer\n- +0x890: Active entry count\n- +0x894: Critical section\n- +0x8ac: Hash bucket array pointer\n- +0x8b0: Hash bucket count\n- +0xbb8: Block callback function pointer\n- +0xbd0: Server initialized flag",
