      "name": "HashTableCheckEntryThreshold",
      "signature": "bool HashTableCheckEntryThreshold(void * pHashTable, uint * pdwKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Checks if a hash table entry's value meets or exceeds the threshold.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates hash table is initialized (offset 0x884 >= 0)\n2. Computes bucket index: key % bucketCount (offset 0x10)\n3. Acquires critical section (offset 0x854) via Ordinal_10050\n4. Walks linked list at bucket looking for matching key\n5. If found, compares entry value against threshold (offset 0x884)\n6. Releases critical section and returns result\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTable (void*): Hash table structure pointer\n- pdwKey (uint*): Pointer to key value to look up\n\nReturns:\n- true if entry found AND entry value >= threshold\n- false if table invalid, entry not found, or value below threshold\n\nStructure Layout (HashTable):\n- 0x10: dwBucketCount (modulo divisor)\n- 0x40: ppBuckets (array of linked list heads)\n- 0x854: CriticalSection (48 bytes)\n- 0x884: nThreshold (validity/threshold value)",
