      "name": "CheckConnectionRateLimit",
      "signature": "void CheckConnectionRateLimit(void * pServer, int * pnConnectionId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Checks if connection from given ID exceeds rate limit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return success if rate limiting disabled (offset 0x884 <= 0)\n2. Get current time and rate limit threshold\n3. Lock critical section and purge stale entries (>15000ms old)\n4. Search linked list for existing record matching connection ID\n5. If found within window: increment count, reject if > (limit*2+3)\n6. If not found or expired: create/reset record with count=1\n7. Return 1 (allowed) or 0 (rate limited)\n\nParameters:\n- pServer (void*): Server context containing rate limit config and record list\n- pnConnectionId (int*): Pointer to connection identifier\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Connection allowed\n- 0: Connection rate limited (exceeded limit*2+3 attempts in 15 seconds)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x884: Rate limit threshold field offset\n- 0x84c: Head of rate record linked list\n- 0x850: Tail of rate record linked list\n- 0x854: Critical section offset\n- 15000 (0x3A98): Rate window in milliseconds\n- 0x10: Size of rate record structure (16 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
