      "name": "ValidateIpAgainstAllowList",
      "signature": "int ValidateIpAgainstAllowList(void * pCtx, in_addr * pAddr)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates an IP address against the allowed CIDR networks list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract IP address from in_addr structure\n2. Enter critical section and lookup IP in hash table\n3. Iterate through CIDR allow list checking if IP matches any network\n4. If match found, return success (1)\n5. If no match, log unauthorized access and disconnect client\n\nParameters:\n- pCtx (void*): Server context containing hash table and CIDR list\n- pAddr (in_addr*): IP address to validate\n\nReturns:\n- 1 always (logs/disconnects on unauthorized access)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc: Hash mask offset in context\n- 0x20: Hash table pointer offset\n- 0x28: Critical section offset\n- 0x848: CIDR entry count offset\n- 0x4c: CIDR list start offset\n- 0x18: IP address offset in entry (puVar3[6])\n- 0x1c: Next entry pointer offset (puVar3[7])",
