      "name": "DequeueBufferAndCopy",
      "signature": "dword DequeueBufferAndCopy(void * pManager, int nPriority, byte * pbDestBuf, dword dwMaxSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Dequeues a buffer from a priority queue and copies its contents to destination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nPriority is within bounds (< manager+0x87c)\n2. Clamp dwMaxSize to max buffer size 0x5b4 (1460 bytes)\n3. Enter critical section at manager+0x854 via Ordinal_10050\n4. Get head buffer from queue array at manager+0x870[nPriority]\n5. If no buffer available, leave critical section and return -1\n6. Unlink buffer from queue, update head pointer to next in chain\n7. Clear tail pointer at manager+0x874[nPriority] if this was last buffer\n8. Leave critical section\n9. Copy min(dwMaxSize, bufferSize+4) bytes to pbDestBuf\n10. Zero the entire 0x5c0-byte buffer (0x170 dwords)\n11. Re-enter critical section\n12. Link buffer to free list at manager+0x878\n13. Leave critical section and return original data size\n\nParameters:\n- pManager (void*): Pointer to buffer manager structure\n- nPriority (int): Priority queue index to dequeue from\n- pbDestBuf (byte*): Destination buffer for copied data\n- dwMaxSize (dword): Maximum bytes to copy to destination\n\nReturns:\n- Data size on success (value from buffer offset 0x5b4)\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) if nPriority out of bounds or queue empty\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5b4 (1460): Max data payload size and offset to size field\n- 0x5bc: Offset to next pointer in buffer node\n- 0x5c0 (1472): Total buffer size (0x170 * 4 bytes)\n- 0x854: Critical section offset in manager\n- 0x870: Queue head array offset\n- 0x874: Queue tail array offset\n- 0x878: Free list head offset\n- 0x87c: Max priority count offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:01ea08240fc2c95f093f1cac50e874e3",
