      "name": "GetPeerIPAddressByID",
      "signature": "void GetPeerIPAddressByID(FogHashTable * pHashTable, DWORD dwPeerID, char * szIPBuffer, DWORD dwBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Looks up a peer entry by ID in a hash table and returns its IP address as a string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute bucket index: dwPeerID & mask (offset 0xC)\n2. Enter critical section for that bucket (stride 0x18)\n3. Walk linked list at bucket looking for matching ID\n4. If not found, set output buffer to empty string\n5. If found, convert IP at offset 0x18 via inet_ntoa, copy to output\n6. Leave critical section\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTable (int): Pointer to peer hash table structure\n- dwPeerID (DWORD): ID of peer to look up\n- szIPBuffer (char*): Output buffer for IP address string\n- dwBufferSize (DWORD): Size of output buffer\n\nReturns:\n- void (result written to szIPBuffer; empty string if not found)",
