      "name": "DisconnectClientByAddress",
      "signature": "void DisconnectClientByAddress(void * pServerContext, in_addr addrClient, uint dwUnused1, uint dwBlockDuration)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Disconnects a client by IP address and adds IP to block cache.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if server not accepting connections (offset 0xBD0 == 0)\n2. Look up client in address hash table using IP as key\n3. If not found, log and add IP to block cache\n4. Lock client list critical section, find client by ID\n5. Mark client as disconnecting (offset 0xC = 1)\n6. Close client socket via Ordinal_10000\n7. Decrement reference count via InterlockedDecrement\n8. If refcount reaches 0, remove from both hash tables and destroy context\n9. Add IP to block cache with specified duration\n\nParameters:\n- pServerContext (void*): Server context structure\n- addrClient (in_addr): Client IP address to disconnect\n- dwUnused1 (uint): Unused parameter\n- dwBlockDuration (uint): Duration to block IP in cache\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout (pServerContext offsets):\n- 0x0C: Hash table mask\n- 0x14: Client list hash table pointer\n- 0x1C: Client list critical sections array\n- 0x20: Address hash table pointer\n- 0x28: Address hash critical section\n- 0x854: Global client lock critical section\n- 0x880: Active client count\n- 0xBC8: Optional callback function pointer\n- 0xBD0: Server accepting connections flag",
