      "name": "RemoveClientByIpAddress",
      "signature": "void RemoveClientByIpAddress(void * pServerCtx, in_addr addrClient)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Removes a client connection from the server by IP address.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Find client in IP address hash table using hash bucket lookup\n2. Get client ID and locate in client ID hash table\n3. Mark client as disconnecting (flag = 1)\n4. Close socket via Ordinal_10000 and invalidate handle\n5. Decrement reference count via InterlockedDecrement\n6. If ref count reaches zero, remove from both hash tables\n7. Call callback at +0xBC8 if registered for cleanup notification\n8. Destroy client context structure\n\nParameters:\n- pServerCtx (void*): Server context containing hash tables and locks\n- addrClient (in_addr): IP address of client to disconnect\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xC: Hash mask offset in server context\n- 0x14: Client ID hash table pointer offset\n- 0x18: Lock size for hash bucket (24 bytes)\n- 0x1C: Hash bucket locks array offset\n- 0x20: IP address hash table pointer offset\n- 0x28: IP hash table critical section offset\n- 0x854: Global client lock critical section offset\n- 0x880: Active client count offset\n- 0xBC8: Cleanup callback function pointer offset",
