      "name": "QueueReceivedMessage",
      "signature": "int QueueReceivedMessage(int nServerCtx)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves and queues a received network message from the server context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call vtable function at offset 0xBC0 to retrieve message data\n2. Return 0 if result is not 1 or 2 (no message available)\n3. Allocate or recycle a message buffer (0x5C0 bytes) from free list\n4. Copy message data to buffer using MOVSD/MOVSB\n5. Store message size at offset 0x5B4, timestamp at 0x5B8\n6. Link buffer into per-queue linked list at queue index\n\nParameters:\n- nServerCtx (int): Server context structure pointer containing vtable and queue arrays\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (message queued)\n- 0 if no message available\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xBC0: Vtable offset for message retrieval callback\n- 0x5C0: Message buffer allocation size (1472 bytes)\n- 0x854: CRITICAL_SECTION offset in server context\n- 0x870: Queue head array offset\n- 0x874: Queue tail array offset\n- 0x878: Free list head offset\n- 0x87C: Max queue count",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:b850d2d4521ed789fb21fd9bfb49d4d3",
