      "name": "CreateListenerSocket",
      "signature": "int CreateListenerSocket(void * pNetCtx, ushort wPort)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Creates and binds a TCP listening socket, then spawns an accept thread.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set network context init flag at offset 0x884\n2. Create AF_INET SOCK_STREAM socket\n3. Set TCP_NODELAY (level 6, opt 1) and SO_REUSEADDR (level 0xFFFF, opt 8)\n4. Set non-blocking mode via FIONBIO ioctlsocket\n5. Bind to INADDR_ANY on specified port\n6. Listen with backlog of 25 connections\n7. Create event handle and spawn listener thread at LAB_6ff66560\n\nParameters:\n- pNetCtx (void*): Network context structure\n- wPort (ushort): Port number to listen on\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success\n- 0 if socket() or bind() fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x884: Network context init flag offset\n- 0xb90: Socket handle offset in context\n- 0xba0: Port storage offset in context\n- 0xbd4: Event handle offset\n- 0xbd8: Thread handle offset\n- 0xbe8: Thread ID offset\n- 0x19 (25): Listen backlog size\n- FIONBIO (0x8004667E): Set non-blocking mode",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:dea117cd6b6323762c26511ce9165a87",
