      "name": "ServerListenerThread",
      "signature": "void ServerListenerThread(FogHashTable * pServerContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Server Listener Thread - Main network I/O loop for accepting new connections and receiving client data\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize bucket tracking state (dwBucketIndex=0, nBucketOffset=0)\n2. Enter infinite server loop\n3. Call ProcessTimerTick to handle time-based events\n4. Initialize fdReadSet and fdExceptSet fd_sets with count=0\n5. Lock server critical section (param_1+0x854)\n6. Add listener socket (param_1+0xb90) to both fd_sets if not already present (max 64)\n7. Iterate through client hash table (up to 64 clients per select cycle):\n   a. Navigate to current bucket position using nBucketOffset skip count\n   b. For each client entry, lock client critical section (entry+0x2c)\n   c. Add client socket (entry+0x10) to read and except fd_sets\n   d. Advance to next entry in linked list (entry+0x4)\n8. Calculate select timeout: tv_usec = 100000 / ((clientCount / 64) + 1)\n9. Release server critical section\n10. Call select() with readfds, NULL writefds, exceptfds, and timeout\n11. On timeout (select returns 0):\n    a. Check shutdown flag (param_1+0xbf8), if set call ExitThread\n12. On success (select returns > 0):\n    a. Process exception fd_set (currently just decrements count)\n    b. Process read fd_set from end to beginning:\n       - Listener socket: Accept new connection\n         * Validate IP against cache (RefreshCacheEntryTimer)\n         * Check connection threshold (HashTableCheckEntryThreshold)\n         * Check rate limit (CheckConnectionRateLimit)\n         * If all pass, add client via QSrvAddClient\n         * Otherwise reject and close socket\n       - Client socket: Receive data\n         * Find client in hash table (FindHashTableEntryById)\n         * Read into client buffer at offset pClient[0x22]\n         * On error/disconnect: call DisconnectClient\n         * On success: update buffer size, ProcessClientMessages, signal event\n13. Loop forever until shutdown\n\nParameters:\n  pServerContext (FogHashTable *): Server state structure containing:\n    - ppBuckets: Hash table buckets for client tracking\n    - dwUnknown18: Number of hash buckets\n    - +0x854: Critical section for server synchronization\n    - +0x880: Total connected client count\n    - +0xb90: Listener socket handle\n    - +0xbc4: Optional callback function pointer\n    - +0xbd4: Event handle for signaling\n    - +0xbf8: Shutdown flag\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function runs indefinitely until ExitThread called\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - EWOULDBLOCK (0x2733): Accept retry up to 100 times\n  - Accept failure: FogFatalError then ExitWithCode(-1)\n  - Buffer bounds check: nSize in [0, 0x5b3] or assert failure\n  - Invalid client: recv to temp buffer and log warning\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x40 (64): Max sockets per fd_set (FD_SETSIZE)\n  - 0x5b4 (1460): Read buffer size (TCP MTU)\n  - 0x90 (144): Offset to client read buffer\n  - 0x88 (136): Offset to client buffer size field\n  - 0x10b (267): Block reason code\n  - 0x2733 (10035): WSAEWOULDBLOCK",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:36f78b1ac2fe1a5b1ed3c4490e4cc96e",
