      "name": "FogMemAlloc",
      "signature": "void * FogMemAlloc(dword nSize, char * szFile, int nLine)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from Fog's global memory pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls internal pool allocator FUN_6ff68140 with NULL context (uses default pool)\n2. If allocation fails, logs error via Ordinal_10028 with source location\n3. Returns allocated pointer or NULL\n\nParameters:\n- nSize: Number of bytes to allocate\n- szFile: Source file path for error logging (e.g., __FILE__)\n- nLine: Source line number for error logging (e.g., __LINE__)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated memory on success\n- NULL on allocation failure (error logged)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f91ad661a0954fc291a8cef163c6f456",
