      "name": "PoolReallocate",
      "signature": "byte * PoolReallocate(byte * pbExisting, int nNewSize, char * szFile, int nLine)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Reallocates memory from the default memory pool with debug tracking.\n\nWrapper around the internal pool reallocation that uses the default pool\n(DAT_6ff87044) and logs allocation failures for debugging.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6ff68ac0 with NULL pool context (uses default pool)\n2. Pass existing pointer, new size, and debug info (file/line)\n3. If reallocation fails (NULL result), log error via Ordinal_10028\n4. Return reallocated pointer (or NULL on failure)\n\nParameters:\n- pbExisting (byte*): Existing allocation to resize, or NULL for new alloc\n- nNewSize (int): Requested new size in bytes\n- szFile (char*): Source file name for debug tracking\n- nLine (int): Source line number for debug tracking\n\nReturns:\n- byte*: Pointer to reallocated memory on success\n- NULL: On allocation failure (error logged via Ordinal_10028)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
