    "fog.dll_RemoveMemPoolHashEntry": {
      "addresses": {
        "LoD/1.07": "0x6FF67FF0"
      },
      "rvas": {
        "LoD/1.07": "0x7FF0"
      },
      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.07": 122
      },
      "name": "RemoveMemPoolHashEntry",
      "signature": "void RemoveMemPoolHashEntry(MemPool * pMemPool, uint dwAllocAddr)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Removes an allocation from the memory pool's hash table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute hash node pointer from allocation address (dwAllocAddr - 4)\n2. Calculate hash bucket index using modulo 0x3ff (1023 buckets)\n3. Lock critical section at pMemPool->critSection\n4. Traverse linked list at calculated bucket to find matching node\n5. If found, unlink node from chain (update prev->next or bucket head)\n6. Unlock critical section via Ordinal_10051 (LeaveCriticalSection wrapper)\n7. Free the node memory via FUN_6ff72982\n\nParameters:\n- pMemPool (MemPool*): Memory pool structure containing hash table\n- dwAllocAddr (uint): Address of user data to remove (actual node is at dwAllocAddr - 4)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:c620bdceae5c103035f37b50b375055a",
      "basic_block_counts": {
        "LoD/1.07": 8
      },
      "loop_counts": {
        "LoD/1.07": 0
      },
      "mnemonic_hashes": {
        "LoD/1.07": "8a30716c1b371376c2345582a962d6e8"
      }
    },
    "fog.dll_PoolHashReallocEntry": {
      "addresses": {
        "LoD/1.07": "0x6FF68070"
      },
      "rvas": {
        "LoD/1.07": "0x8070"
      },
      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.07": 195
      },
      "name": "PoolHashReallocEntry",
      "signature": "byte * PoolHashReallocEntry(void * pMemPool, byte * pbOldData, int nNewSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Reallocates a hash table entry with a new size.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert user pointer to entry header (pbOldData - 4)\n2. Enter critical section for thread safety\n3. Compute hash bucket index: entry % 0x3ff\n4. Walk hash chain to find and unlink old entry\n5. If entry not found, release lock and return NULL\n6. Call FUN_6ff72a6b (realloc) with new size + 4 for header\n7. Link new entry into its hash bucket\n8. Release critical section and return user data pointer\n\nParameters:\n- pMemPool (void*): Memory pool with hash table at offset 0x30\n- pbOldData (byte*): Pointer to user data of existing allocation\n- nNewSize (int): New requested size for user data\n\nReturns:\n- byte*: Pointer to reallocated user data (entry + 4), or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: Header size before user data\n- 0x30: Offset to hash table array in memory pool\n- 0x3ff (1023): Hash table bucket count for modulo operation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:8be7550a9ab4a57dee4841cf85b154a9",
      "basic_block_counts": {
        "LoD/1.07": 10
      },
      "loop_counts": {
        "LoD/1.07": 0
      },
      "mnemonic_hashes": {
        "LoD/1.07": "315ec45da97d4954e48430c8ae88a239"
      }
    },
