      "name": "FindFirstFreeBitInBitmap",
      "signature": "int FindFirstFreeBitInBitmap(uint * pdwBitmap, uint nStartIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Finds the first zero bit in a bitmap array starting from nStartIndex.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute DWORD index from nStartIndex (divide by 32)\n2. Switch-case falls through DWORDs 7->0 checking for free bits\n3. For each DWORD: NOT value then BSF to find first zero bit\n4. If >8 DWORDs needed, advance by 8 DWORDs (256 bits) and retry\n5. Handle partial DWORD at start using g_adwPartialBitMasks lookup\n\nParameters:\n- pdwBitmap (uint*): Pointer to array of DWORDs forming the bitmap\n- nStartIndex (uint): Starting bit index (0-based)\n\nReturns:\n- Bit index of first zero bit (>=0), or -1 if all bits are set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Bits per DWORD\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for bit-within-DWORD\n- 0x100 (256): Bits per 8-DWORD chunk",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
