      "name": "InsertPoolBlockSorted",
      "signature": "void InsertPoolBlockSorted(int * pPool, uint * pPoolBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Inserts a pool block into the pool's sorted block array using binary search.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock pool critical section\n2. Check if block count is at capacity - fatal error if overflow\n3. Update pool's total allocated memory tracking\n4. Binary search for correct insertion position by block address\n5. Shift existing entries if not inserting at end\n6. Store block pointer and address key at insertion position\n7. Increment block count and unlock\n\nParameters:\n- pPool (int*): Memory pool structure\n- pPoolBlock (uint*): Pool block to insert (first DWORD is address key)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nStructure Layout (8-byte stride):\n| Offset | Field          | Description                    |\n|--------|----------------|--------------------------------|\n| 0x00   | pBlock         | Pointer to pool block          |\n| 0x04   | dwAddressKey   | Block address for sorting      |\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (pPool+9): Current block count\n- 0x28 (pPool+10): Maximum block capacity\n- 0x2c (pPool+11): Pointer to block array\n- 0x102c (pPool+0x40b): Total allocated memory counter",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
