      "name": "CreatePoolBlock",
      "signature": "uint * CreatePoolBlock(int * pPool, uint * pBucket)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new PoolBlock, then inserts it into the pool's sorted block array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify pool has capacity (nBlockCount < nMaxBlocks)\n2. Calculate bitmap size: (nMemBlocks + 31) / 32 dwords\n3. Allocate header+bitmap (0x18 + bitmap bytes) and data buffer\n4. Zero-initialize header (6 dwords) and bitmap\n5. Set pData pointer, pBitmap pointer, pBucket backref\n6. Increment bucket's block count\n7. Binary search for insertion position (sorted by pData address)\n8. Shift existing entries and insert new block\n9. Update pool totals and block count\n\nParameters:\n- pPool (int*): Memory pool context\n- pBucket (uint*): Size-class bucket requesting new block\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to new PoolBlock on success\n- Does not return on failure (fatal error logged)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18 (24): PoolBlock header size (6 dwords)\n- 0x1f (31): Rounding for bitmap dword count\n- 8: Block entry stride in sorted array (ptr + base addr)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:97eee2c04a3bf183fc814c962aadcd55",
