      "name": "ReleasePoolChunkSlot",
      "signature": "void ReleasePoolChunkSlot(MemPool * pMemPool, uint * pdwAllocAddr)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Releases a memory slot back to the pool by clearing its allocation bit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Use default pool if pMemPool is NULL\n2. Lock pool critical section, binary search chunk array for matching chunk\n3. Calculate slot index within chunk: (allocAddr - chunkBase) / slotSize\n4. If slot index exceeds chunk capacity, use hash table fallback\n5. Lock chunk critical section and clear allocation bit in bitmap\n6. Decrement chunk allocation count\n7. If chunk has free slots and meets threshold, add to free list\n8. Unlock critical sections and return\n\nParameters:\n- pMemPool (MemPool*): Pool to release from, NULL uses default\n- pdwAllocAddr (uint*): Pointer to allocation address to release\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2c: Offset to pBuckets in MemPool\n- 0x24: Offset to chunk count in MemPool\n- 0x1f: Bit index mask (31, for 32-bit word)\n- 5: Bit shift for word index (divide by 32)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:a6657ef2b5152fc1e513f9c07ca37927",
