      "name": "DestroyMemPool",
      "signature": "void DestroyMemPool(MemPool * pPool)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Destroys and deallocates a memory pool and all its allocations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check memory subsystem is initialized and pool is valid\n2. Use default pool (g_pDefaultMemPool) if NULL passed\n3. Enter pool's critical section\n4. If pool has allocation buckets:\n   a. Iterate each bucket (0x30 stride), free allocation linked lists\n   b. Delete each bucket's critical section\n5. Free the bucket array (offset 0x20) and pBuckets (offset 0x2C)\n6. Iterate 0x3FF hash buckets (offset 0x30), free each linked list\n7. Delete pool's main critical section\n8. Zero the entire pool structure (0x414 dwords = 4180 bytes)\n9. Free the pool structure itself\n10. If this was the default pool, clear globals and delete global critical section\n\nParameters:\n- pPool (MemPool*): Pool to destroy, or NULL to destroy default pool\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x30 (48): Bucket stride size\n- 0x3FF (1023): Hash bucket count\n- 0x414 (1044): Pool structure size in dwords (4176 bytes)\n- 0x28 (40): Offset to allocation list head in bucket",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:76fc04bc1a6df020e9349917b52f9900",
