      "name": "InitializeMemoryPool",
      "signature": "int InitializeMemoryPool(uint * * ppPool, char * szPoolName, int nMaxPools, int nMaxThreads)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initializes a memory pool structure with size-class buckets for allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate pool structure (0x1050 bytes)\n2. Zero-initialize structure (0x414 DWORDs)\n3. If ppPool is NULL, set as default pool and init global critical section\n4. Initialize pool's critical section and enter it\n5. Copy pool name if provided (max 0x20 chars)\n6. Calculate number of buckets using BSR (bit scan reverse) for log2\n7. Validate bucket count < 0x29 (D2POOL_MAX_POOLS)\n8. Allocate bucket array (nBuckets * 0x30 stride) and thread array (nMaxThreads * 8)\n9. Initialize each bucket's critical section and compute sizes:\n   - Block size = 1 << bucketIndex\n   - Block count = min(0x100, 0x40000 / blockSize)\n   - Total bytes = blockSize * blockCount\n10. Zero-initialize tracking table (0x3ff DWORDs)\n11. Leave critical section and return success\n\nParameters:\n- ppPool (uint**): Output pointer to pool, or NULL for default pool\n- szPoolName (char*): Pool name for debugging (max 0x20 chars)\n- nMaxPools (int): Max allocation size hint (bucket count derived via log2)\n- nMaxThreads (int): Max concurrent threads for tracking array\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success (never returns on failure - calls FUN_6ff71ca1)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1050 (4176): Pool structure size\n- 0x414 (1044): DWORDs to zero in pool structure\n- 0x30 (48): PoolBucket stride\n- 0x29 (41): D2POOL_MAX_POOLS limit\n- 0x3ff (1023): Tracking table size (hash mask)\n- 0x40000 (262144): Max total block allocation per bucket\n- 0x100 (256): Default block count per bucket",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:c1822e3997ce3fa84368daf76070724c",
