      "name": "BinarySearchTable",
      "signature": "int BinarySearchTable(int * pTable, uint dwKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Binary searches a sorted table for a key and returns associated value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pTable is not NULL (assert otherwise)\n2. Extract count from pTable[0] and data pointer from pTable[2]\n3. Validate data pointer is not NULL if count > 0 (assert otherwise)\n4. Binary search: compare key at midpoint, narrow range until found\n5. Return value at offset +4 from matching key, or -1 if not found\n\nParameters:\n- pTable (int*): Pointer to table structure [count, ?, dataPtr]\n- dwKey (uint): Key to search for\n\nReturns:\n- Associated int value if key found, -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) if not found\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field\n  0x0     4     nCount (number of entries)\n  0x4     4     (unused/reserved)\n  0x8     4     pData (ptr to entry array)\n\nEntry Format (8 bytes each):\n  0x0     4     dwKey (search key)\n  0x4     4     nValue (associated value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
