      "name": "InsertSortedIndexEntry",
      "signature": "int InsertSortedIndexEntry(int * pIndex, uint dwKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Inserts a key into a sorted index table using binary search.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pIndex is not NULL\n2. Check pIndex[3] == 0 (table is not readonly string table)\n3. If array is full (count >= capacity), grow by 64 entries\n4. Binary search to find insertion point\n5. Shift elements right via FUN_6ff72470 (memmove)\n6. Insert key and current count as entry pair\n7. Increment count and return original index\n\nParameters:\n- pIndex: Sorted index structure:\n  - [0]: entry count\n  - [4]: capacity\n  - [8]: pointer to entry array (8-byte entries: key + index)\n  - [12]: string table flag (must be 0)\n- dwKey: Key value to insert\n\nReturns:\n- Index position where entry was inserted (original count before increment)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x40 (64): Growth increment for array capacity\n- 0x80 (128): DWORD count for zeroing new entries (64 entries * 8 bytes / 4)\n- 8: Entry stride (key:4 + index:4)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
