      "name": "FindIndexByKey",
      "signature": "int FindIndexByKey(StringIndex * pIndex, char * szKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Searches a binary tree index for a key and returns associated value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pIndex is not NULL (assert on failure)\n2. Copy szKey to local buffer (max 32 bytes) via SStrCopy\n3. Convert buffer to uppercase via ToUpperInPlace\n4. Get root node from pIndex->pRoot\n5. Traverse binary tree comparing uppercase key to each node\n6. If match found, return value at node+0x20\n7. If key < node key, go left (node+0x24), else go right (node+0x28)\n8. Return -1 if key not found or empty tree\n\nParameters:\n- pIndex (StringIndex*): Pointer to index structure (nSize at +0x0, pRoot at +0xC)\n- szKey (char*): Key string to search for (case-insensitive, max 32 chars)\n\nReturns:\n- Index value (node+0x20) on match\n- -1 if key not found or tree is empty\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Max key length / offset to value in node\n- 0x24 (36): Offset to left child pointer in node\n- 0x28 (40): Offset to right child pointer in node\n- 0xC (12): Offset to root node pointer in index struct",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:92801ec8e8fb1ee8115b5a09450e8f33",
