      "name": "InsertStringTableEntry",
      "signature": "void InsertStringTableEntry(int * pIndex, char * szKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Inserts a string key into a binary search tree index structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates pIndex is non-NULL\n2. Validates table not already initialized (pIndex[2] == 0)\n3. Allocates 0x2c (44) byte node: char[0x20] key, dword[0x20] value, ptr[0x24] left, ptr[0x28] right\n4. Copies szKey to node (max 0x20 bytes), converts to uppercase\n5. Stores current count as node value at offset 0x20\n6. Inserts node into BST at pIndex[3] using strcmp ordering\n7. Increments entry count at pIndex[0]\n\nParameters:\n- pIndex (int*): String table index structure\n  - [0]: Entry count\n  - [2]: Initialized flag (must be 0)\n  - [3]: BST root pointer\n- szKey (char*): String key to insert (max 32 chars)\n\nReturns:\n- void (asserts on NULL pIndex or initialized table)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2c (44): Node structure size\n- 0x20 (32): Max key length\n- 0x24: Left child pointer offset\n- 0x28: Right child pointer offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
