      "name": "DecodeHuffmanData",
      "signature": "int DecodeHuffmanData(byte * pbDest, int nDestLen, byte * pbSrc, int nSrcLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Decodes Huffman-encoded data using precomputed bit-length and symbol tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each input byte, look up bit length in DAT_6ff822d0 and symbol in DAT_6ffa0198\n2. Extract bits from symbol value based on bit length\n3. Pack decoded bits into output bytes, handling cross-byte boundaries\n4. Flush any remaining partial byte at end of input\n\nParameters:\n- pbDest (byte*): Output buffer for decoded data\n- nDestLen (int): Maximum bytes to write to output buffer\n- pbSrc (byte*): Huffman-encoded input data\n- nSrcLen (int): Number of input bytes to decode\n\nReturns:\n- Number of bytes written to output buffer on success\n- 0 if output buffer would overflow\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: Bits per output byte\n- 0x1f: Bit shift mask (mod 32)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9041b61bdddd3b50e4a9505da45df20e",
