      "name": "DecodeHuffmanStream",
      "signature": "int DecodeHuffmanStream(byte * pbOutBuf, int nOutSize, byte * pbInBuf, int nInSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Decodes Huffman-compressed data from input buffer to output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 32-bit accumulator and bit counter (starts at 32)\n2. Fill accumulator with input bytes while bit counter > 7 and input remains\n3. Use top 8 bits as index into g_apHuffmanTable to get decode table\n4. Extract symbol index using bit length from table entry\n5. If accumulated bits exceed 32, return bytes decoded (end of stream)\n6. If output buffer exhausted, return 0 (incomplete decode)\n7. Write decoded byte to output, shift accumulator, continue loop\n\nParameters:\n- pbOutBuf (byte*): Destination buffer for decoded data (ECX)\n- nOutSize (int): Maximum bytes to decode (EDX)\n- pbInBuf (byte*): Source buffer with Huffman-encoded data\n- nInSize (int): Size of encoded input in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- Number of bytes decoded on success\n- 0 if output buffer exhausted before stream end\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Bit accumulator width\n- 0x18 (24): Shift for top-byte table index\n- 0x8: Bits per input byte",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:3869bc386bdc5337edf1f940dc69e482",
