      "name": "CheckCpuLacksFeatures",
      "signature": "bool CheckCpuLacksFeatures(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Checks if CPU lacks certain features by examining vendor and CPU model.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_wCpuidMaxLevel < 5 (early exit with TRUE if below threshold)\n2. Execute CPUID(0) to get vendor string (12 bytes in EBX:EDX:ECX)\n3. Compare vendor against \"GenuineIntel\", \"AuthenticAMD\", \"CyrixInstead\"\n4. Execute CPUID(1) to get version info, extract type/family/model fields\n5. For Intel: Check specific family 5/6 models that lack features\n6. For AMD: Check family 4 or family 5 models < 6 or 6-7 that lack features\n7. For Cyrix: Always returns TRUE (lacks features)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- TRUE (1): CPU lacks certain features (old/incompatible model)\n- FALSE (0): CPU supports required features\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5: Minimum CPUID support level threshold\n- Family 5, Model 4+ on Intel: Pentium models\n- Family 6, Model < 3 on Intel: Early P6 architecture\n- Family 5 on AMD: K5/K6 processors",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c34ea8482f132a9c60a7a26b6796a34d",
