      "name": "DataArrayClear",
      "signature": "void DataArrayClear(void * pDataArray)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Clears and resets a DataArray structure to initial state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert that pDataArray->fValid is non-zero\n2. Reset state fields: nCurrentIdx=-1, nCount=0, nState=0, wFlags=0x8000\n3. Loop through all elements and clear first word to 0\n\nParameters:\n- pDataArray (void*): Pointer to DataArray structure\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100: Offset to capacity field\n- 0x104: Offset to element stride\n- 0x108: Offset to fValid flag\n- 0x10c: Offset to state field\n- 0x110: Offset to current index (-1 = invalid)\n- 0x114: Offset to count field\n- 0x118: Offset to flags (0x8000 = initial state)\n- 0x11c: Offset to array data pointer",
