      "name": "AssertDataArrayEntryExists",
      "signature": "void AssertDataArrayEntryExists(int nDataArray, int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Asserts that a DataArray entry exists at the given index.\n\nValidates array entry existence and terminates with assertion\nfailure if entry is not found. Used as debug validation wrapper.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call DataArrayGetEntry to retrieve entry at nIndex\n2. If entry is NULL, format assertion message\n3. Call FogAssert with message, source file, line number\n4. Terminate via FUN_6ff71ca1(-1) on failure\n5. Return normally if entry exists\n\nParameters:\n- nDataArray (int): Pointer to DataArray structure (cast to int)\n- nIndex (int): Index/handle to validate (high word=row, low word=id)\n\nReturns:\n- void (terminates on failure via assertion)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xfa (250): Source line number for assertion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:661b7de790810885cc154e260c1878bf",
