      "name": "FogAssert",
      "signature": "void FogAssert(char * szExpr, char * szFile, int nLine)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Handles fatal assertion failures by logging error and cleaning up.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call WSACleanup to release Winsock resources (Ordinal_10002)\n2. Log assertion failure with severity 5 via error handler (Ordinal_10028)\n3. Flush logs and cleanup resources (Ordinal_10040)\n\nParameters:\n- param_1 (char*): Expression string that failed assertion\n- param_2 (char*): Source filename where assertion occurred\n- param_3 (int): Line number in source file\n\nReturns:\n- void (function does not return normally - process may terminate)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10002: WSACleanup wrapper\n- Ordinal_10028: Error logging/crash handler\n- Ordinal_10040: Log flush and cleanup",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:35b8ac74843397f20bd6b7067f1510cc",
