      "name": "GenerateStackTraceReport",
      "signature": "int GenerateStackTraceReport(dword dwUnused, int pExceptionPtrs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Generates a comprehensive stack trace report during exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize symbol handler via Ordinal_423\n2. Check if ImageHelp library is loaded (g_fImageHelpLoaded)\n3. Duplicate current process handle for symbol operations\n4. Build symbol search path from current directory, module path, and environment variables\n   (_NT_SYMBOL_PATH, _NT_ALTERNATE_SYMBOL_PATH, SYSTEMROOT)\n5. Initialize symbol handler with SymInitialize\n6. Enumerate loaded modules via GetCurrentProcessId and internal module list functions\n7. Load symbols for each module via SymLoadModule\n8. Walk the stack using StackWalk and resolve symbols via SymGetSymFromAddr\n9. For each stack frame, log module name, function name, offset, and FPO data\n10. Clean up: release module list, call SymCleanup, close process handle\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnused (dword): Unused parameter\n- pExceptionPtrs (int): Pointer to EXCEPTION_POINTERS structure containing exception context\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (stack trace generated)\n- 0 on failure (symbol handler init failed or ImageHelp not loaded)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x200 (512): Buffer size for paths and directory names\n- 0x17ac (6060): Stack frame allocation size\n- 0x190 (400): Max stack dump iterations\n- 0x1000 (4096): Initial stack dump byte count\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH constant\n- 0x20c (524): Module entry field offsets\n- 0x83 (131): Module list next pointer offset (dword index)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff6f150: Get module list by PID\n- FUN_6ff6f380: Alternative module enumeration\n- FindModuleByAddress: Locate module containing address",
