      "name": "LookupTableEntry",
      "signature": "uint LookupTableEntry(uint dwKey, LookupTable_t * pTable, int * pnOutValue1, int * pnOutValue2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Searches a lookup table for an entry matching the hashed key.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Hash the input key using Ordinal_502 (Storm hash function)\n2. Get entry count from table header at offset +0x4\n3. If count is 0, return EINVAL (0x16)\n4. Iterate through entries starting at offset +0x8\n5. Each entry is 12 bytes: [key:4][value1:4][value2:4]\n6. Compare entry key against hashed key\n7. On match, store value1 and value2 to output pointers\n8. Return 0 on success, 0x16 (EINVAL) if not found\n\nParameters:\n- dwKey (uint): Key to search for (will be hashed)\n- pTable (LookupTable_t*): Pointer to lookup table structure\n- pnOutValue1 (int*): Output for first value from matched entry\n- pnOutValue2 (int*): Output for second value from matched entry\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Entry found, output values populated\n- 0x16 (22/EINVAL): Entry not found in table\n\nTable Structure (LookupTable_t):\n- +0x0: dwReserved (uint)\n- +0x4: dwCount (uint) - number of entries\n- +0x8: entries[] (LookupTableEntry_t[]) - 12-byte stride per entry",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6b33dbbe39fb72291022720cd8aa103e",
