      "name": "UnlinkLogMessageNode",
      "signature": "void UnlinkLogMessageNode(int * pNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Unlinks a log message node from a doubly-linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if node's pNext pointer is valid\n2. Calculate target address using offset field\n3. Patch next node's back-link to skip this node\n4. Clear node's link fields (pNext=0, nOffset=0)\n5. Repeat unlink operation (defensive double-unlink)\n\nParameters:\n- pNode (int*): Pointer to linked list node structure\n  - [0] pNext: Pointer to next node\n  - [4] nOffset: Offset for back-link calculation\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: Offset to nOffset field in node structure",
