      "name": "QueueFormattedLogMessage",
      "signature": "void QueueFormattedLogMessage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Queues a formatted log message to the log manager linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x1008 bytes stack via prologue helper\n2. Check g_dwThreadShutdownFlag==0 and g_fBackgroundThreadActive!=0\n3. Format message via FUN_6ff72fbe into stack buffer (0x1000 bytes)\n4. Get string length via Ordinal_506 (SStrLen)\n5. Enter critical section, allocate LogMessage struct via FUN_6ff70ec0\n6. Copy formatted message to LogMessage+0x3C, append newline if flag set\n7. Copy source name to LogMessage+0x18 (16 chars max)\n8. Store timestamp via GetLocalTime at LogMessage+0x8\n9. Insert LogMessage into linked list at DAT_6ffa076c\n10. Update counters g_dwLogManagerState1, g_dwLogManagerState2\n\nParameters (via registers and stack):\n- IMPLICIT: ECX = szSource (16 char source identifier)\n- IMPLICIT: EDX = nShowTimestamp (1=show timestamp)\n- Stack+0x100C = nAppendNewline (1=append newline to message)\n- Stack+0x1010 = pbFormat (format string pointer)\n- Stack+0x1014 = pVarArgs (pointer to varargs)\n\nReturns:\n- void (cleans 12 bytes from caller stack via RET 0xC)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- LogAppendFormat, QueueLogMessage, AddLogMessage: Callers\n- QueueLogEntry: Similar function without formatting",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:07b5dcabd3278342b7711a8aedc6c39e",
