      "name": "OpenOrGetLogFile",
      "signature": "void OpenOrGetLogFile(char * szFilename, int * pnSlotIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Opens or retrieves an existing log file handle by filename.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current tick count for LRU tracking\n2. Search g_apLogFiles array (12 slots) for matching filename\n3. If found with valid handle, return slot index\n4. If not found, find oldest log file slot (LRU eviction)\n5. Close oldest slot's file handle if open\n6. Copy filename to g_aszLogFilenames at selected slot\n7. Build date-stamped path: path + name + YYMMDD.txt\n8. Open file via FUN_6ff732b6 (fopen wrapper)\n9. Store handle and tick counts for access tracking\n10. Return slot index through output parameter\n\nParameters:\n- szFilename (char*): Log filename to open/find\n- pnSlotIndex (int*): Output - receives slot index (0-11)\n\nReturns:\n- void, slot index returned via pnSlotIndex if successful\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100 (256): Log filename buffer size per slot\n- 0xC (12): Maximum concurrent log files\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH for full path buffer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
