      "name": "ReceiveSocketData",
      "signature": "int ReceiveSocketData(SocketContext * pSocketCtx, char * szBuffer, int nBufferLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Receives data from a socket with critical section synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate socket context pointer is non-NULL\n2. Check error state flag (nErrorState != 0 means error)\n3. Enter critical section for thread safety\n4. Call recv() on socket handle\n5. Leave critical section\n6. On error (recv <= 0), store WSA error and set error code to 4\n\nParameters:\n- pSocketCtx (SocketContext*): Socket context structure\n- szBuffer (char*): Buffer to receive data into\n- nBufferLen (int): Maximum bytes to receive\n\nReturns:\n- Bytes received on success (positive value)\n- 0 if context is NULL or already in error state\n- recv() error code (0 or negative) on socket failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x04: Error code value set on recv failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ef1fc064392fbc5f4e727409aae03040",
