      "name": "CheckSocketReadReady",
      "signature": "void CheckSocketReadReady(int * pSocket)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Checks if a socket is ready for reading or has exception/error.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate socket pointer and check connection state (offset 0x2c=0, offset 0x0!=0)\n2. Set up fd_set for both read and exception monitoring with 100ms timeout\n3. Call select() to check socket status\n4. If select error (-1), store WSA error and set state to 4\n5. Check if socket is in exception set (return 1)\n6. Check if socket is in read set (return 1)\n7. Return 0 if no activity\n\nParameters:\n- pSocket (int*): Socket context structure\n  - [0x0]: Connection valid flag\n  - [0x8]: Socket handle (SOCKET)\n  - [0x2c]: Closing flag\n  - [0x30]: Error state\n  - [0x34]: WSA error code\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Socket ready for read or has error condition\n- 0: Socket not ready or invalid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x186a0 (100000): 100ms timeout in microseconds\n- 0x4: Error state indicating WSA failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:4ca49daac4eedb103111f2311fced028",
