      "signature": "void ComputePowerInternal(int nBaseLo, uint dwBaseHi, int nExpLo, uint dwExpHi)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Computes x^y using FPU logarithm/exponentiation for pow() implementation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check FPU control word, call normalizer if not 0x27F\n2. Extract base exponent bits - if 0x7FF (inf/NaN), handle special case\n3. Load base and exponent to FPU via __fload_withFB\n4. If base is zero, handle 0^y cases (return 0, 1, or inf)\n5. Check sign bit of base - if negative, verify exponent is integer\n6. Compute y * log2(x) via FYL2X instruction\n7. Compute 2^result via FUN_6ff74090 (F2XM1 + FSCALE)\n8. Apply sign correction via FCHS if needed\n9. For edge cases, call FUN_6ff7421c with FSAVE/FRSTOR\n\nParameters:\n- nBaseLo (int): Low 32 bits of base double\n- dwBaseHi (uint): High 32 bits of base double (bits 52-62=exp, bit 63=sign)\n- nExpLo (int): Low 32 bits of exponent double\n- dwExpHi (uint): High 32 bits of exponent double\n\nReturns:\n- void (result returned via FPU ST0 register)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FF00000: IEEE double infinity/NaN exponent mask\n- 0xFFFFF: IEEE double mantissa mask (low 20 bits of high word)\n- 0x80: Sign bit in exponent byte\n- 0x1D (29): Error code for domain error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- 0^0 = 1 (via FLD1)\n- 0^positive = 0 (via FLDZ)\n- inf^y, x^inf: Handled by FUN_6ff7421c\n- negative^non-integer: Returns NaN with domain error\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ComputePowerFromFPU: FPU wrapper caller\n- CheckExponentIntegerParity: Determines if exponent is integer/odd/even\n- FUN_6ff74090: Computes 2^x via F2XM1+FSCALE",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:512beb3274e38dd5f9dc6106693805f5",
