      "name": "CheckExponentIntegerParity",
      "signature": "byte CheckExponentIntegerParity(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Determines integer parity of FPU exponent value for pow() calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Duplicate ST0 and round to integer (FRNDINT)\n2. Compare with original - if equal, value is integer (CL=1)\n3. If not integer, multiply by 0.5 and check if result is integer\n4. If doubled-value is integer, original was odd integer (CL=2)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains the exponent value to check\n\nReturns:\n- CL=0: Not an integer (fractional exponent)\n- CL=1: Even integer exponent\n- CL=2: Odd integer exponent\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0.5 at 0x6ff83d30: Multiplier to check for half-integer (odd)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
