      "name": "CharToUpperSafe",
      "signature": "uint CharToUpperSafe(uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts character to uppercase with thread-safety and locale support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if locale is set (g_dwLocaleId != 0)\n2. If no locale: fast-path ASCII 'a'-'z' (0x61-0x7a) to 'A'-'Z' by subtracting 0x20\n3. If locale set: increment thread counter g_nLocaleRefCount\n4. Check if locale is locked (g_fLocaleLocked != 0)\n5. If locked: decrement counter, acquire critical section 0x13, call FUN_6ff7372d\n6. Call FUN_6ff72226 for locale-aware conversion\n7. Release lock or decrement counter based on lock state\n\nParameters:\n- dwChar (uint): Character to convert (ASCII value or extended code point)\n\nReturns:\n- Uppercase character code, or original character if not lowercase\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x61 (97): ASCII 'a' - start of lowercase range\n- 0x7a (122): ASCII 'z' - end of lowercase range\n- 0x20 (32): ASCII case difference ('a' - 'A')\n- 0x13 (19): Critical section ID for locale lock",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
