      "name": "HeapReallocDispatch",
      "signature": "byte * HeapReallocDispatch(byte * pbBuffer, uint dwNewSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Dispatches memory reallocation across multiple heap modes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pbBuffer is NULL, allocate new memory via malloc\n2. If dwNewSize is 0, free the buffer\n3. Select reallocation strategy based on DAT_6ffa2ca4 heap mode:\n   - Mode 3: Pool allocator with small block optimization\n   - Mode 2: Slab allocator (16-byte aligned, block headers)\n   - Default: Direct HeapReAlloc\n4. Copy data to new allocation and free old block\n5. Retry with new memory handler if allocation fails\n\nParameters:\n- pbBuffer: Existing buffer to reallocate (NULL = malloc)\n- dwNewSize: Requested new size (0 = free)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to reallocated buffer on success\n- NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFFFFFFE1: Maximum valid allocation size\n- 0xF/0x10: 16-byte alignment mask/boundary\n- 0x9: Lock operation type for heap synchronization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:da9fe63256c776da60d8a55e82f34c74",
