      "name": "VsnprintfBounded",
      "signature": "int VsnprintfBounded(char * szBuffer, int nMaxLen, byte * pbFormat, dword * pdwVarArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Formats a string into a bounded buffer using printf-style formatting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize state struct with buffer pointer, max length, and flags (0x42)\n2. Call FUN_6ff74762 (printf engine) to format string into buffer\n3. Decrement remaining length counter\n4. If overflow (negative), call FUN_6ff7464a to flush/finalize\n5. Otherwise, null-terminate buffer at current write position\n6. Return number of characters written\n\nParameters:\n- pszBuffer (char*): Destination buffer for formatted output\n- nMaxLen (int): Maximum buffer size in bytes\n- pbFormat (byte*): Printf-style format string\n- pdwVarArgs (dword*): Pointer to variable arguments\n\nReturns:\n- int: Number of characters written (excluding null terminator)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x42 (66): Internal state flags for printf engine\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff74762: Core printf formatting engine\n- FUN_6ff7464a: Buffer flush/finalize on overflow",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:7d35ed9a72948cae0b0cf3a10f47ee1e",
