      "name": "ReadStreamBuffered",
      "signature": "uint ReadStreamBuffered(byte * pbDst, uint dwElemSize, uint dwCount, int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Reads data from a buffered stream (fread internal worker).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total bytes to read (dwElemSize * dwCount)\n2. Return 0 if total is zero\n3. Determine buffer threshold from stream (default 0x1000)\n4. Loop until all bytes read:\n   a. If buffered data available, copy via memmove\n   b. If request >= threshold, read directly from file\n   c. Otherwise, read char-by-char via putback mechanism\n5. Set error flag (0x20) on read failure or short read\n6. Return number of complete elements read\n\nParameters:\n- pbDst (byte*): Destination buffer for read data\n- dwElemSize (uint): Size of each element in bytes\n- dwCount (uint): Number of elements to read\n- pStream (int*): FILE stream structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n- Number of complete elements successfully read\n- Returns partial count on error/EOF\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000: Default unbuffered read threshold\n- 0x108: Stream buffered mode flags\n- 0x10c: Buffer size configured flag\n- 0x20: Stream error flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b4b6c96f53f9cb01bc83df0c2f2d647f",
