      "name": "ForceDecimalPoint",
      "signature": "void ForceDecimalPoint(char * pszFloatStr)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Forces a decimal point into a floating-point string representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if first char is 'e' or 'E' (exponent marker) via ToLowerChar\n2. If not exponent, skip over digit characters using char type table\n3. Insert decimal point character (from g_cDecimalPoint) at position\n4. Shift all remaining characters right by one position\n\nParameters:\n- pszFloatStr (char*): Null-terminated float string to modify in-place\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies string in-place)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x65 (101): ASCII 'e' (exponent marker, lowercase)\n- 0x4: Character type flag for digits\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Called as g_pfnFptrapHandler2 via function pointer\n- Part of CRT floating-point conversion utilities (cfltcvt)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
