      "name": "FormatFloatAutoSelect",
      "signature": "void FormatFloatAutoSelect(double * pdValue, char * szBuffer, size_t nPrecision, int nUpperCase)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Formats a double to string using %g-style auto-selection between fixed and exponential notation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decompose double into sign, exponent, and digit buffer via FUN_6ff799e8\n2. Round/format digits via FUN_6ff79971 (accounts for negative sign offset)\n3. If exponent < -4 or exponent >= precision, use exponential format (FormatFloatExponential)\n4. Otherwise use fixed decimal format (FormatDecimalString), truncating trailing digit if exponent grew\n\nParameters:\n- pdValue (double*): Pointer to floating-point value to format\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer for formatted string\n- nPrecision (size_t): Number of significant digits\n- nUpperCase (int): Use uppercase 'E' for exponential notation\n\nReturns:\n- void (result written to szBuffer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): ASCII '-' minus sign\n- -4: Lower bound for fixed-point format (exponents >= -4 use decimal)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FormatFloatExponential: Formats in scientific notation (e.g., \"1.23E+05\")\n- FormatDecimalString: Formats in fixed-point notation (e.g., \"123.45\")",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
