      "name": "ComputePowerExponentiation",
      "signature": "void ComputePowerExponentiation(uint dwExpInfo, byte bySignFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Computes power exponentiation (x^y) using FPU instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if exponent high byte is non-zero for special case handling\n2. Call FUN_6ff73df1 to validate exponent type (integer vs fractional)\n3. If validation fails, return NaN via FUN_6ff74006\n4. Compute y*log2(x) using FYL2X instruction\n5. Split result into integer and fractional parts\n6. Compute 2^frac using F2XM1 then add 1\n7. If reciprocal flag set, compute 1/result or use extended precision divide\n8. Scale by integer part using FSCALE\n9. Apply sign via FCHS if sign flag set\n\nParameters:\n- dwExpInfo (uint): Exponent info packed value; high byte indicates special case\n- bySignFlag (byte): Sign flag for result negation\n- IMPLICIT: ST(0) contains base (x), ST(1) contains exponent (y)\n\nReturns:\n- void (result in ST(0) via FPU stack)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFE: Error code stored at [EBP-0x90] for special case\n- 0x40: Bit mask for FSCALE skip condition\n- 0x01: Bit mask for reciprocal operation flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f0a75c57169f7149d74a2236cce98a2e",
