      "name": "ComputeFractionalExp2Minus1",
      "signature": "void ComputeFractionalExp2Minus1(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Computes 2^frac(x) - 1 for the fractional part of x using F2XM1.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if |ST0| exceeds g_ldMaxFracInput threshold\n2. If within range: extract integer part via FRNDINT, compute fractional via subtraction\n3. Apply F2XM1 to |fractional| to get 2^frac - 1\n4. If out of range: handle special case via FUN_6ff73f66\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains the exponent value to process\n\nReturns:\n- ST0 contains 2^frac(x) - 1 result\n- DL contains FPU status flags\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x41: FPU status mask for C0|C3 flags (compare result)\n- 0xA0: Stack offset for FPU status word storage\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff73c50: Caller that computes full 2^x via FSCALE\n- FUN_6ff73f66: Returns 0.0 for out-of-range inputs",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
