      "name": "DispatchFpuClassification",
      "signature": "void DispatchFpuClassification(int nContext, void * pState)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Examines FPU ST0 register and dispatches to handler based on value classification.\nUses FXAM instruction to determine float type then jumps to appropriate handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check state flag at pState+0xe for control word mode\n2. Set FPU control word (0x133f default or custom)\n3. Execute FXAM to classify ST0 floating-point value\n4. Store FPU status word and extract condition codes C0-C3\n5. Use g_abFpuClassLookup to map condition codes to offset\n6. Jump to handler at pState + offset + 0x10\n\nParameters:\n- nContext (int): ECX - FPU context identifier (unused in this function)\n- pState (void*): EDX - Pointer to FPU state structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x0e: Control mode flag (0x05 for custom)\n  - Offset 0x10+: Dispatch handler table\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains floating-point value to classify\n\nReturns:\n- void (exits via indirect jump to classification handler)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x05: State check at offset 0xe triggers custom control word\n- 0x133f: Default FPU control word (round-to-nearest, mask all exceptions)\n- 0x3f: Alternative control word low byte for custom mode\n- 0x10: Base offset of dispatch handler table in state structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1e502191010869fca5d6ea71e353f408",
