      "name": "PopFpuStackSecondValue",
      "signature": "void PopFpuStackSecondValue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleans up FPU stack by discarding the second value (ST1).\n\nUsed after FSCALE and other FPU operations that leave an extra value on the stack.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Exchange ST(0) and ST(1) via FXCH instruction\n2. Pop and discard ST(0) via FSTP ST0 instruction\n3. Result: original ST(1) is discarded, original ST(0) remains as new ST(0)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST(0) and ST(1) contain FPU values; ST(0) is preserved, ST(1) is discarded\n\nReturns:\n- void (FPU stack has one less entry, preserving original top value)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ComputePowerExponentiation: Calls this after FSCALE to clean up stack",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2efd2f634b43779c5726887ddad8796b",
