      "name": "ReturnNaNAndSetErrorFlag",
      "signature": "void ReturnNaNAndSetErrorFlag(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Clears FPU stack and returns NaN for power function error cases.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pop two values from FPU stack (FSTP ST0 twice)\n2. Load NaN constant from g_ldNaN onto ST(0)\n3. If error flag at [EBP-0x90] < 1, set it to 1\n4. Return NaN in ST(0)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: EBP points to caller's stack frame\n- IMPLICIT: ST(0), ST(1) contain values to discard\n\nReturns:\n- NaN value in ST(0) (float10 via FPU stack)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ComputePowerExponentiation: Calls this when exponent validation fails",
