      "name": "__startTwoArgErrorHandling",
      "signature": "float10 __startTwoArgErrorHandling(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__, dword dwFunctionId, dword dwErrorType, word wControlWord, dword dwArg1Hi, dword dwArg1Lo, dword dwArg2Hi, dword dwArg2Lo, dword dwResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Visual Studio CRT two-argument floating-point error handling wrapper.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up stack frame, store function ID at EBP-0x20\n2. Copy second argument (dwArg2Hi/Lo) to local stack slots\n3. Store ST0 as double for error reporting\n4. Copy first argument (dwArg1Hi/Lo) to stack frame\n5. JMP to shared error handler code at 0x6ff74050\n6. Call FUN_6ff7a9eb to process FP exception\n7. Restore original FPU control word and return ST0\n\nParameters:\n- dwFunctionId (dword): Identifies which FP function triggered error (via EAX/__fastcall)\n- dwErrorType (dword): Error type code passed to exception handler\n- wControlWord (word): FPU control word for restoration\n- dwArg1Hi/Lo (dword pair): First double argument high/low dwords\n- dwArg2Hi/Lo (dword pair): Second double argument high/low dwords\n- dwResult (dword): Result placeholder\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains the result value to preserve\n\nReturns:\n- float10 (via ST0): Preserved floating-point result after error handling\n\nRelated Functions:\n- __startOneArgErrorHandling @ 0x6ff74047: Single-argument version\n- FUN_6ff7a9eb: Core FP exception processing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
