      "name": "ClassifyIntegerParity",
      "signature": "uint ClassifyIntegerParity(double dValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Classifies a double value as non-integer, odd integer, or even integer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if value is normal (not NaN/Inf) via FUN_6ff7aabb\n2. Round value and compare to original - if unequal, not an integer\n3. Divide by 2.0 and round - if result equals quotient, value is even\n\nParameters:\n- dValue (double): The floating-point value to classify\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Not a valid integer (special float or has fractional part)\n- 1: Odd integer\n- 2: Even integer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- HandlePowerSpecialCases: Uses result to handle negative base edge cases",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1252459d5bf6fc7fa6bd21d0f60e6017",
