      "name": "PutCharToStream",
      "signature": "int PutCharToStream(int nChar, int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes a single character to a stream (fputc implementation).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check stream flags for valid write state (0x82 mask)\n2. If read mode active (flag 0x1), clear count and reset buffer\n3. Set stream to write mode (flag 0x2), clear read flag (0x10)\n4. If unbuffered (no 0x108 flags), allocate buffer via FUN_6ff7ad53\n5. If buffered, flush existing data via FUN_6ff78085 before writing\n6. Store character at buffer position, update stream pointers\n7. If buffer empty and append mode (0x20), seek to end via FUN_6ff77819\n\nParameters:\n- nChar (int): Character to write (only low byte used)\n- pStream (int*): Pointer to FILE stream structure\n\nReturns:\n- Character written (0-255) on success\n- -1 on error (sets error flag 0x20 in stream)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x82: Read/write mode flags mask\n- 0x40: Error/EOF flag\n- 0x10: Read mode flag\n- 0x108: Buffering flags (0x100=line, 0x8=allocated)\n- 0x20: Error/append flag\n- 0x24 (36): FILE structure entry stride in table\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff78085: Write buffer to file descriptor\n- FUN_6ff7ad53: Allocate stream buffer\n- FUN_6ff77819: Seek file position",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
