      "name": "WritePaddingChars",
      "signature": "void WritePaddingChars(uint dwPadChar, int nCount, int * pStream, int * pnCharCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes a padding character to output stream multiple times for printf format width.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nCount > 0, exit early if not\n2. Loop nCount times (decrementing counter each iteration)\n3. Call WriteCharToBuffer(dwPadChar, pStream, pnCharCount) to output character\n4. After each write, check if *pnCharCount == -1 (write error)\n5. If error detected, exit loop immediately\n6. Continue until count exhausted or error occurs\n\nParameters:\n- dwPadChar (uint): ASCII character code to repeat (typically 0x20 space or 0x30 zero)\n- nCount (int): Number of times to write the character\n- pStream (int*): Pointer to output stream state structure\n- pnCharCount (int*): Pointer to running character count, set to -1 on error\n\nReturns:\n- void (error state communicated via pnCharCount becoming -1)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f7657de81ac8d5d29214c35b4fa6fd17",
