      "name": "WriteStringToBuffer",
      "signature": "void WriteStringToBuffer(char * szSrc, int nLen, int * pnBufPos, int * pnStatus)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes a string of specified length to output buffer character by character.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop through nLen characters from szSrc\n2. For each character, call WriteCharToBuffer to append to output\n3. Exit early if pnStatus becomes -1 (buffer full/error)\n\nParameters:\n- szSrc (char*): Source string to copy from\n- nLen (int): Number of characters to write\n- pnBufPos (int*): Pointer to current buffer write position\n- pnStatus (int*): Pointer to status indicator (-1 = error/full)\n\nReturns:\n- void (status communicated via pnStatus)",
