      "name": "InitSmallBlockHeap",
      "signature": "int InitSmallBlockHeap(uint dwThreshold)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initializes the Small Block Heap (SBH) memory allocator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x140 (320) bytes for heap descriptor via HeapAlloc\n2. Return 0 on allocation failure\n3. Initialize SBH globals: clear reserved fields, set heap pointers\n4. Set granularity to 0x10 (16-byte alignment)\n5. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n- dwThreshold (uint): Maximum block size for SBH allocation\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success, 0 on allocation failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x140 (320): Size of SBH heap descriptor structure\n- 0x10 (16): Block alignment granularity\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitCrtHeap: Parent initializer that calls this function\n- CleanupHeapAllocations: Frees allocated SBH resources",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a57b3ae583e4f6f104245d4da8d3b9fe",
