      "name": "FindSmallBlockHeapEntry",
      "signature": "uint * FindSmallBlockHeapEntry(void * pBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Searches the small block heap array for the entry containing a memory block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Start at g_pHeapEntryArray base pointer\n2. Loop while current entry is within array bounds (g_nHeapEntryCount * 5 dwords)\n3. For each 20-byte (5 dword) entry, compare pBlock against base address at offset 0xc\n4. If (pBlock - entry[3]) < 0x100000, the block falls within this 1MB region\n5. Return entry pointer on match, or NULL if not found\n\nParameters:\n- pBlock (void*): Memory address to locate in the SBH array\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to SBH entry (20 bytes) owning pBlock, or NULL if not found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): SBH entry stride (5 dwords)\n- 0xc (12): Offset to base address within entry (entry[3])\n- 0x100000 (1MB): Maximum block range per SBH entry",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2a0dd1f395da0f8e13609d337843c676",
