      "name": "SbhAllocBlock",
      "signature": "void * SbhAllocBlock(uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates a block from the Small Block Heap (SBH).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute aligned size (16-byte boundary) and bucket index from size\n2. Create bit masks for bucket search based on size class\n3. Search heap regions starting from g_pSbhRegionListEnd for available blocks\n4. If no suitable region found, search from g_pSbhRegionEnd\n5. If still no region, check for regions with commit space or allocate new region\n6. Initialize heap page if needed via InitializeHeapPage()\n7. Find group with free blocks using bit masks on low/high bitmaps\n8. Locate free block in appropriate bucket via linked list\n9. Split block if remainder > 16 bytes, update bucket free lists\n10. Update bitmap counts and region bitmaps when buckets empty/non-empty\n11. Mark allocated block with size+1 sentinel at start and end\n12. Update group allocation counter and cache tracking\n\nParameters:\n- dwSize (uint): Requested allocation size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Pointer to allocated memory (after block header), or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x17 (23): Alignment padding for 16-byte boundary calculation\n- 0xfffffff0: Mask for 16-byte alignment\n- 0x14 (20): Size of SBH region descriptor (5 DWORDs)\n- 0x11 (17): Offset to low bitmap array in page header\n- 0x31 (49): Offset to high bitmap array in page header\n- 0x51 (81): Offset to free list array in page header\n- 0x81 (129): Group stride in page header\n- 0x3f (63): Maximum bucket index\n- 0x80000000: Bit mask for leftmost bit in 32-bit bitmap",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ff64648b3e6e32bc28a5e4bc8d984c1e",
