      "name": "HeapBlockResize",
      "signature": "int HeapBlockResize(uint * pHeapState, byte * pbBlock, int nNewSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Resize a heap block in-place if possible, handling free list management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align new size to 16-byte boundary (+0x17 & 0xFFFFFFF0)\n2. Calculate segment index from block address (>>15, *0x204)\n3. If new size > old size: attempt to coalesce with adjacent free block\n   - Check next block's free flag (bit 0)\n   - Unlink from free list and update size class bitmaps\n4. If new size < old size: split block and return remainder to free list\n   - Insert remainder into appropriate size class bucket\n   - Update segment and global availability bitmaps\n5. Update block headers (size stored at -4 and at end-4)\n\nParameters:\n- pHeapState (uint*): Heap state with bitmaps at [0],[1] and data at [4]\n- pbBlock (byte*): Block data pointer (header at -4)\n- nNewSize (int): Requested new size (will be aligned)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (resize completed)\n- 0 on failure (cannot grow: next block in use or too small)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x17: Alignment pad (round up to 16)\n- 0x3F (63): Max size class index\n- 0x20 (32): Size class split (low vs high bitmap)\n- 0x144: Bucket list base offset\n- 0x204: Segment stride (per-segment bitmap/lists)",
