      "name": "RaiseFloatingPointException",
      "signature": "void RaiseFloatingPointException(uint * pExceptionRecord, uint * pFpuControlWord, uint dwFpuStatusFlags, uint dwPrecisionControl, double * pdSrc, double * pdDst)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Raises a structured exception for floating-point errors.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize exception record fields [+4], [+8], [+0xC] to zero\n2. Map FPU status bits to NTSTATUS codes and exception type flags\n3. Map FPU control word mask bits (inverted) to exception record\n4. Call FUN_6ff7702f to get additional FPU state, map to record[3]\n5. Decode rounding mode from control word bits 10-11 to record[0]\n6. Decode precision control from control word bits 8-9 to record[0]\n7. Store precision control param in bits 5-16 of record[0]\n8. Copy source/dest double values to exception record\n9. Call RaiseException with determined NTSTATUS code\n10. On return, restore FPU control word from modified exception record\n\nParameters:\n- pExceptionRecord (uint*): Output buffer for FP exception record (0x54 bytes)\n- pFpuControlWord (uint*): Pointer to FPU control word to modify\n- dwFpuStatusFlags (uint): FPU status word exception bits\n- dwPrecisionControl (uint): Precision control value (bits 0-11 used)\n- pdSrc (double*): Source operand causing exception\n- pdDst (double*): Destination for result after handler\n\nReturns:\n- void (always raises exception, continues on return)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xC000008F: STATUS_FLOAT_INEXACT_RESULT (bit 0x10)\n- 0xC0000093: STATUS_FLOAT_OVERFLOW (bit 0x02)\n- 0xC0000091: STATUS_FLOAT_UNDERFLOW (bit 0x01)\n- 0xC000008E: STATUS_FLOAT_DIVIDE_BY_ZERO (bit 0x04)\n- 0xC0000090: STATUS_FLOAT_INVALID_OPERATION (bit 0x08)\n- 0xC00/0x400/0x800: Rounding mode control bits\n- 0x300/0x200: Precision control bits",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a4fde7ab66242cc6a0f98892cc769636",
