      "name": "ClassifyDoubleSpecialValue",
      "signature": "int ClassifyDoubleSpecialValue(uint dwLowBits, uint dwHighBits)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Classifies IEEE 754 double-precision special values from raw bit representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if high bits match +infinity pattern (0x7ff00000) with zero low bits\n2. Check if high bits match -infinity pattern (0xfff00000) with zero low bits\n3. Extract exponent bits and check for QNaN pattern (all exp bits + quiet bit set)\n4. Check for SNaN pattern (all exp bits set, non-zero mantissa, quiet bit clear)\n5. Return 0 for finite/normal values\n\nParameters:\n- dwLowBits (uint): Low 32 bits of double (mantissa low part)\n- dwHighBits (uint): High 32 bits of double (sign + exponent + mantissa high)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Finite/normal value\n- 1: Positive infinity (+Inf)\n- 2: Negative infinity (-Inf)\n- 3: Quiet NaN (QNaN)\n- 4: Signaling NaN (SNaN)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7ff00000: +Infinity high bits (exponent=0x7ff, mantissa=0)\n- 0xfff00000: -Infinity high bits (sign=1, exponent=0x7ff, mantissa=0)\n- 0x7ff8: Exponent mask for NaN detection (bits 52-62 shifted)\n- 0x7ffff: Mantissa mask for high word (bits 32-51)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:05d8e97733e4c41533ceefe44bc4bac2",
