      "name": "ExtractMantissaAndExponent",
      "signature": "double ExtractMantissaAndExponent(uint dwDoubleLoBits, uint dwDoubleHiBits, int * pnExponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Extracts normalized mantissa and exponent from IEEE 754 double.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If input is zero, return 0.0 with exponent 0\n2. If denormalized (exponent field 0, mantissa non-zero):\n   - Start with exponent -1021 (0x3FD)\n   - Shift mantissa left until normalized (bit 52 set)\n   - Decrement exponent for each shift\n   - Preserve sign bit\n3. If normalized, extract exponent field minus bias (1022)\n4. Scale result to range [0.5, 1.0) via ScaleDoubleByExponent\n\nParameters:\n- dwDoubleLoBits (uint): Low 32 bits of IEEE 754 double\n- dwDoubleHiBits (uint): High 32 bits of IEEE 754 double\n- pnExponent (int*): Output pointer for binary exponent\n\nReturns:\n- Normalized mantissa m where 0.5 <= |m| < 1.0, input = m * 2^exp\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FF00000: Exponent field mask (bits 52-62)\n- 0xFFFFF: Mantissa field mask (lower 20 bits of high word)\n- 0x3FD (-1021): Initial exponent for denormalized numbers\n- 0x3FE (1022): IEEE 754 double exponent bias minus 1\n- 0x10: Bit 52 position check in high word byte 2\n- 0x80000000: Sign bit / MSB check for carry propagation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:07c53c70ca23fa302c00136544982339",
