      "name": "CleanupFileTableCriticalSections",
      "signature": "void CleanupFileTableCriticalSections(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Frees all allocated file table entries and deletes their critical sections.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate g_apFileTable array (64 entries, 0x6ffa1b60-0x6ffa1c5c)\n2. For each non-NULL entry, iterate 32 file slots (stride 0x24)\n3. If slot's SpinCount field (offset 0x8) is non-zero, delete critical section\n4. Free the entire table entry and NULL the pointer\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480: Total size per table entry (32 slots * 0x24 = 0x480)\n- 0x24 (36): File slot structure stride\n- 0xC: Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION within slot\n- 0x8: Offset to SpinCount check (active indicator)\n- 64: Number of table entries (0x6ffa1c60 - 0x6ffa1b60) / 4\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CRTDllMain: Calls this on DLL_PROCESS_DETACH\n- MemFree: Frees each allocated table entry",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
