      "name": "AllocateStreamSlot",
      "signature": "void * AllocateStreamSlot(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a stream slot from the global stream array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section index 2\n2. Iterate through stream slots searching for available slot\n3. If slot is NULL, allocate 0x38 bytes for new stream structure\n4. Initialize critical section at offset 0x20 within structure\n5. If slot has flags byte at +0xC with bits 0x83 clear, lock and claim it\n6. Initialize claimed stream structure fields to zero/defaults\n7. Release critical section and return pointer\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated/claimed stream structure on success\n- NULL if no slots available or allocation failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x38 (56): Stream structure size\n- 0x83: Busy/locked flag mask at offset +0xC\n- 0x20 (32): Critical section offset in stream structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:22b6fd05e1ae4204b7a816ab266e5408",
