      "name": "CloseFileDescriptorHandle",
      "signature": "int CloseFileDescriptorHandle(uint dwFileDesc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Closes OS handle for a file descriptor and clears its table entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get OS handle for file descriptor via FUN_6ff7bca8\n2. If handle invalid (-1), skip to cleanup\n3. For stdout/stderr (fd 1,2): skip close if both point to same handle\n4. Call CloseHandle on the OS handle\n5. On CloseHandle failure: capture GetLastError\n6. Clear std handle via FUN_6ff7bc29\n7. Clear file descriptor flags at offset 0x4 in table entry (stride 0x24)\n8. Return 0 on success, -1 on error with errno set\n\nParameters:\n- nFileDesc (uint): File descriptor index to close\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on failure, errno set via SetOsErrnoFromDosError\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): File descriptor table entry stride\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for entry index within block (32 entries per block)\n- 5: Right shift for block index (divide by 32)",
