      "name": "FillStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "uint FillStreamBuffer(uint * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Fills stream buffer from file and returns first character.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check stream flags (readable, not EOF/error, not in write mode)\n2. Set read mode flag (0x01)\n3. Allocate buffer if needed (0x1000 bytes) or reset pointer\n4. Call ReadFileLocked to fill buffer from file descriptor\n5. Check file entry flags for text mode marker (0x2000)\n6. Upgrade buffer from 0x200 to 0x1000 if heap-allocated\n7. Decrement count, return first byte, advance pointer\n\nParameters:\n- pStream (uint*): FILE stream structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n- First byte read (0-255) on success\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) on EOF or error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x83: Read mode flags mask\n- 0x40: EOF/error flag\n- 0x02: Write mode flag\n- 0x10c: Buffer allocation flags\n- 0x2000: Text mode translation flag\n- 0x24 (36): File entry structure stride",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
