      "name": "UngetCharIfNotEOF",
      "signature": "void UngetCharIfNotEOF(uint dwChar, int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Conditionally pushes a character back to the input stream.\nWrapper around FUN_6ff7c23f that skips the unget if the\ncharacter is EOF (-1). Used during format parsing to put\nback characters that were read but not consumed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dwChar equals EOF (0xFFFFFFFF)\n2. If dwChar is EOF, return immediately without action\n3. If dwChar is not EOF, call FUN_6ff7c23f(dwChar, pStream)\n\nParameters:\n- dwChar (uint): Character to push back, or EOF (0xFFFFFFFF)\n- pStream (int*): Pointer to stream state structure\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
