      "name": "InitEnvironmentTable",
      "signature": "void InitEnvironmentTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the CRT environment table (_environ) from the raw environment block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Ensure subsystem is initialized via FUN_6ff7c685 if not already\n2. Count valid environment entries (skip entries starting with '=')\n3. Allocate pointer array for (count + 1) entries including NULL terminator\n4. For each valid entry, malloc and copy string to individual buffer\n5. Free original environment block and set g_ppszEnviron\n6. Mark environment as initialized via g_fEnvironInitialized\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- void (calls __amsg_exit(9) on allocation failure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3d (61): ASCII '=' - skip entries starting with this\n- 0x9: Runtime error code for out of memory\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff79161: Gets raw environment block (called before this)\n- FUN_6ff79b00: String copy function\n- FUN_6ff7c685: Subsystem initialization check",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
