      "name": "GetEnvironmentStringsAnsi",
      "signature": "LPSTR GetEnvironmentStringsAnsi(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves environment strings as ANSI, converting from wide if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_nEnvStringMode for cached API preference (0=unset, 1=wide, 2=ANSI)\n2. If unset, try GetEnvironmentStringsW first; cache mode=1 on success\n3. If wide fails, try GetEnvironmentStrings (ANSI); cache mode=2 on success\n4. For wide strings: scan to find total length, call WideCharToMultiByte to get size\n5. Allocate buffer, convert wide to ANSI, free wide strings\n6. For ANSI strings: scan to find total length, allocate and copy buffer\n7. Free original environment block and return ANSI copy\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- LPSTR: Allocated copy of environment strings (caller must free), or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1: Mode flag indicating GetEnvironmentStringsW succeeded\n- 0x2: Mode flag indicating GetEnvironmentStrings (ANSI) succeeded",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
