      "name": "ConvertExtFloatToInt",
      "signature": "int ConvertExtFloatToInt(ushort * pExtFloat, uint * pdwResult, int * pConvParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts 80-bit extended precision float to integer based on conversion parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract sign bit (bit 15 of word 5), exponent (bits 0-14 of word 5), mantissa\n2. Calculate unbiased exponent (exponent - 0x3FFF bias)\n3. If exponent is minimum (-0x3FFF), check for zero mantissa (return 0)\n4. Otherwise, round mantissa based on precision bits, handle overflow/underflow\n5. Shift mantissa right to align with target integer format\n6. Apply sign bit and exponent to result\n\nParameters:\n- pExtFloat (ushort*): 80-bit extended float (12 bytes: 2 words low, 2 words mid, 1 word exp+sign)\n- pdwResult (uint*): Output buffer (4 or 8 bytes based on pConvParams[4])\n- pConvParams (int*): Conversion parameters array:\n  [0] = max exponent, [1] = min exponent, [2] = precision bits,\n  [3] = shift count, [4] = output size (0x20=32-bit, 0x40=64-bit), [5] = exponent bias\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Zero or denormal result\n- 1: Overflow (value too large for target format)\n- 2: Normal conversion completed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3FFF (16383): Extended precision exponent bias\n- 0x7FFF: Exponent mask (15 bits)\n- 0x8000: Sign bit mask\n- 0x20 (32): 32-bit output size\n- 0x40 (64): 64-bit output size",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:7af322ad22a8e231117c7fe6d2adf33c",
