      "name": "BuildRoundedDigitString",
      "signature": "void BuildRoundedDigitString(char * szDest, int nPrecision, int * pCtx)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Builds a rounded digit string from float context for formatted output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Write leading '0' to destination buffer\n2. Copy nPrecision digits from source (pCtx[3]), padding with '0' if source exhausted\n3. Null terminate the result string\n4. If rounding needed (next source digit > '4'):\n   - Propagate carry through '9' digits (replacing with '0')\n   - Increment non-'9' digit\n5. If overflow caused leading '1' (was '0'), increment exponent (pCtx[1])\n6. Otherwise shift buffer left by 1 to remove overflow guard digit\n\nParameters:\n- szDest (char*): Destination buffer for digit string\n- nPrecision (int): Number of digits to copy\n- pCtx (int*): Float context structure where:\n  - pCtx[1]: Exponent value (adjusted if overflow)\n  - pCtx[3]: Source digit string pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void (result written to szDest)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FormatFloatAutoSelect, FormatFloatFixed, FormatDoubleExponential (callers)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:91502dc0968a39359be974ca352b925c",
