      "name": "ProcessFpuError",
      "signature": "void ProcessFpuError(uint dwExceptCode, int * pnFpuState, ushort * pwControlWord)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Processes FPU exception based on error type and exception code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract control word value and error type from FPU state\n2. Map error type to exception flags:\n   - 1,5: Invalid operation (0x08)\n   - 2: Denormal operand (0x04)\n   - 3: Division by zero (0x11)\n   - 4: Overflow (0x12)\n   - 7: Reset error type to 1, skip exception\n   - 8: Precision (0x10)\n3. Call HandleFpuExceptionFlags to process exception\n4. If not handled, modify FPU flags based on exception code:\n   - 0x10,0x16,0x1d: Set precision mode bits\n   - Others: Clear lowest bit\n5. Raise floating point exception if needed\n6. Restore FPU control word\n7. Set errno if appropriate\n\nParameters:\n- dwExceptCode (uint): Exception code (0x10=_DOMAIN, 0x16=_SING, etc.)\n- pnFpuState (int*): Pointer to FPU state structure\n- pwControlWord (ushort*): Pointer to FPU control word\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x08: Invalid operation flag\n- 0x04: Denormal operand flag\n- 0x10: Precision flag\n- 0x11: Division by zero flag\n- 0x12: Overflow flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:fd9902cfddcce5a55494181fb300821e",
