      "name": "IsFileDescTextMode",
      "signature": "byte IsFileDescTextMode(uint dwFileDesc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Checks if a file descriptor is valid and in text mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare descriptor against g_dwMaxFileDesc limit\n2. If out of range, return 0 (invalid)\n3. Lookup FILE entry in g_apFileTable using descriptor\n4. Return text mode flag (0x40 bit) from entry flags byte\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileDesc (uint): File descriptor number to check\n\nReturns:\n- 0x40: File is valid and in text mode\n- 0x00: Invalid descriptor or binary mode\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for table entry index (32 entries per block)\n- 0x5: Right shift to get table block index\n- 0x24 (36): FILE entry stride in table\n- 0x40: Text mode flag bit in FILE flags",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d020e6e6f383c625d5fd112b88b641eb",
