      "name": "ConvertWideCharToMultiByteSingle",
      "signature": "int ConvertWideCharToMultiByteSingle(char * lpszDest, WCHAR wSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts single wide character to multibyte string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return NULL if dest buffer is NULL\n2. If locale ID not set (g_dwLocaleId==0), handle ASCII directly:\n   - If wSrc < 0x100, copy byte directly and return 1\n   - Otherwise fail with EILSEQ\n3. Otherwise call WideCharToMultiByte with flags 0x220\n4. Return byte count on success, -1 on error\n\nParameters:\n- lpszDest (char*): Destination buffer for multibyte output\n- wSrc (WCHAR): Wide character to convert\n\nReturns:\n- Bytes written on success (1 for ASCII)\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) on error, sets errno to EILSEQ (0x2a)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x220: WC_NO_BEST_FIT_CHARS | WC_COMPOSITECHECK flags\n- 0x2a (42): EILSEQ - illegal byte sequence",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:12dead7d93dd2763acf5540fd9895c41",
