      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Internal epilogue fragment of _strchr for the alignment loop match case.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Jumped to from _strchr when character found during byte-by-byte alignment loop\n2. Returns szStr-1 (adjusts for the pre-increment done before compare)\n3. Pops EBX and returns (epilogue shared with main function)\n\nParameters:\n- nUnused (int): ECX register content, unused in this fragment\n- szStr (char*): EDX contains string pointer after INC, needs adjustment\n\nReturns:\n- char*: Pointer to the matched character (szStr - 1)\n\nNote: This is a code fragment, not a standalone function. It exists as a\nseparate function entry due to Ghidra's function detection heuristics.",
