      "name": "IsDateInDaylightSavingTime",
      "signature": "bool IsDateInDaylightSavingTime(int * pDateTime)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Thread-safe wrapper for DST date checking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section 0xb (protects DST transition data)\n2. Call inner DST check function with datetime array\n3. Release critical section 0xb\n4. Return result from inner function\n\nParameters:\n- pDateTime (int*): Array of datetime components [sec, min, hour, day, month, year, dayOfYear, totalDays]\n\nReturns:\n- true: The datetime falls within daylight saving time period\n- false: The datetime is in standard time or DST is disabled\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff7b5c6: Inner function performing actual DST boundary check\n- ConvertDateTimeToTimestamp: Caller that uses DST status for timestamp adjustment",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
