      "name": "CheckDateInDaylightSavingTime",
      "signature": "bool CheckDateInDaylightSavingTime(int * pDateTime)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Checks if a given datetime falls within the DST period.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if DST is disabled (g_fDstEnabled == 0)\n2. If year differs from cached DST transition years, recalculate:\n   - Call FUN_6ff7b772 to compute DST start day-of-year\n   - Call FUN_6ff7b772 to compute DST end day-of-year\n3. Compare input day-of-year against DST range:\n   - If DST start < end (normal case): check if day is between them\n   - If DST start > end (southern hemisphere): check if day is outside range\n4. For boundary days, compute milliseconds since midnight:\n   - Formula: ((hour * 60 + minute) * 60 + second) * 1000\n   - Compare against cached transition times\n\nParameters:\n- pDateTime (int*): Datetime array [sec, min, hour, day, month, year, ?, dayOfYear, ...]\n\nReturns:\n- true if datetime is within DST period, false otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3c (60): Seconds per minute, minutes per hour\n- 0x3e8 (1000): Milliseconds per second\n- 0x14 (20): Offset to year field (index 5)\n- 0x1c (28): Offset to day-of-year field (index 7)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6bb86e2cc8beb9a2c340a0df09e576f1",
