      "name": "LockFileDescriptor",
      "signature": "void LockFileDescriptor(uint dwFileHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Acquires the critical section lock for a file descriptor.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate file table block index (dwFileHandle >> 5) and entry offset ((dwFileHandle & 0x1f) * 0x24)\n2. Check if critical section is initialized (offset 0x8 == 0)\n3. If not initialized, use double-checked locking:\n   a. Lock global critical section 0x11\n   b. Re-check initialization flag\n   c. Initialize CRITICAL_SECTION at offset 0xc\n   d. Set initialization flag to 1\n   e. Release global lock\n4. Enter the per-file critical section\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileHandle (uint): File descriptor handle (bits 0-4 = entry index, bits 5+ = block index)\n\nReturns:\n- void (caller must call corresponding unlock)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for entry index within block\n- 0x24 (36): Stride of file descriptor structure\n- 0x8: Offset of initialization flag in file descriptor\n- 0xc: Offset of CRITICAL_SECTION in file descriptor\n- 0x11 (17): Global critical section index for file table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:89c8ec97483b3d89b792dc7acc8a9af7",
