      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes file descriptor buffers to disk via OS handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file descriptor against g_dwMaxFileDesc\n2. Compute file table index: (dwFileDesc & 0x1f) * 0x24\n3. Check if file is open (flag & 1)\n4. Lock file descriptor\n5. Get OS handle and call FlushFileBuffers\n6. Store error in TLS if flush fails\n7. Unlock and return status\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileDesc (uint): File descriptor index\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success, -1 on error (sets errno to EBADF=9)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for file index within table block\n- 0x24 (36): File descriptor structure stride\n- 9: EBADF (bad file descriptor) errno value",
