      "signature": "int ParseFloatStringToMantissa(void * this, ushort * pMantissaOut, byte * * ppEndPtr, byte * pszInput, int nPrecision, int nExpAdjust, int nFracAdjust, int fAllowSign)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Parses a floating-point string into a 96-bit mantissa structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace (space, tab, newline, CR)\n2. Parse optional sign (+/-), setting dwSign=0x8000 for negative\n3. State machine parses: integer digits, decimal point, fractional digits\n4. Parse exponent if E/e/D/d found with optional sign\n5. Collect up to 25 (0x19) significant digits into abDigits buffer\n6. Convert via AsciiDigitsTo96BitMantissa to 96-bit form\n7. Apply exponent adjustment via FUN_6ff7d73e\n8. Output 12-byte structure: [wMantLow][pbMantMid][wMantHigh|dwSign]\n\nParameters:\n- pMantissaOut (ushort*): Output 12-byte mantissa structure\n- ppEndPtr (byte**): Output pointer past last parsed char\n- pszInput (byte*): Input string to parse\n- nPrecision (int): Precision bits for conversion\n- nExpAdjust (int): Base exponent adjustment\n- nFracAdjust (int): Fraction adjustment factor\n- fAllowSign (int): If 0, treat +/- after digits as terminator\n- IMPLICIT: ECX (this) unused but required by calling convention\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success\n- 1: Underflow (result too small)\n- 2: Overflow (result too large)\n- 4: Parse error (no valid digits found)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x19 (25): Max significant digits collected\n- 0x18 (24): Max digits used in conversion\n- 0x1450 (5200): Max exponent value before overflow\n- 0x8000: Sign bit for negative numbers\n- 0x7FFF: Infinity exponent marker",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ab787578be0f52440df577da55f0ef97",
