      "name": "ConvertExtendedToDecimalString",
      "signature": "int ConvertExtendedToDecimalString(uint dwMantissaLo, uint dwMantissaHi, uint dwExpSign, int nPrecision, byte byFlags, short * psResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts 80-bit extended precision float mantissa and exponent to decimal string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract sign bit (bit 15) and 15-bit exponent from dwExpSign\n2. Handle zero case: if exponent and mantissa both zero, output \"0\"\n3. Handle special exponent 0x7FFF: check mantissa bits for INF/NaN type\n4. Estimate decimal exponent via log10(2) approximation\n5. Scale 96-bit accumulator by negative decimal exponent power of 10\n6. Extract digits via repeated multiply-by-10 and digit extraction\n7. Round last digit using standard rounding (>= 5 rounds up)\n8. Strip trailing zeros and adjust exponent for zero result\n\nParameters:\n- dwMantissaLo (uint): Low 32 bits of 64-bit mantissa\n- dwMantissaHi (uint): High 32 bits of 64-bit mantissa  \n- dwExpSign (uint): Low 15 bits = biased exponent, bit 15 = sign\n- nPrecision (int): Maximum decimal digits to generate\n- byFlags (byte): Bit 0 = adjust precision by adding decimal exponent\n- psResult (short*): Output buffer pointer\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Successful conversion to decimal digits\n- 0: Special value handled (INF, IND, QNAN, SNAN)\n\nOutput Buffer Layout (psResult):\n- Offset 0 (short): Decimal exponent (power of 10)\n- Offset 2 (byte): Sign character (0x20=' ' or 0x2D='-')\n- Offset 3 (byte): Digit count\n- Offset 4+: ASCII decimal digits or special string\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FFF: Mask for 15-bit exponent field\n- 0x8000: Sign bit mask in dwExpSign\n- 0x3FFE: Exponent bias minus 1\n- 0x4D10, 0x4D: Log10(2) approximation constants\n- 0xCCCCCCCC3FFB: Extended precision 1/10 constant",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:caf0293062c4e4caabf207f9f9a0ab4c",
