      "name": "ParseStringToInteger",
      "signature": "int ParseStringToInteger(byte * pbString)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Parses a string to convert it to an integer (atoi-like).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace (character type mask 0x8)\n2. Check for optional +/- sign at position\n3. Parse consecutive digit characters (mask 0x4) into integer\n4. Negate result if sign was minus (0x2d)\n\nParameters:\n- pbString (byte*): Pointer to null-terminated string to parse\n\nReturns:\n- Parsed integer value; 0 if no digits found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): ASCII minus sign '-'\n- 0x2b (43): ASCII plus sign '+'\n- 0x30 (48): ASCII '0' for digit conversion\n- 0x8: Character type mask for whitespace\n- 0x4: Character type mask for digits",
