      "name": "Multiply80BitExtendedPrecision",
      "signature": "void Multiply80BitExtendedPrecision(uint * pdwResult, uint * pdwMultiplier)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Multiplies two 80-bit extended precision floating point values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponents (bits 0-14) and sign bits (bit 15) from both operands\n2. Check for special cases: overflow, underflow, zero operands\n3. Compute result sign as XOR of input sign bits\n4. Add exponents (adjusting for bias)\n5. Perform 96-bit mantissa multiplication via schoolbook method\n6. Normalize result by shifting left/right until MSB is set\n7. Round result and handle carry propagation\n8. Pack sign, exponent, and mantissa into result\n\nParameters:\n- pdwResult (uint*): 12-byte extended precision input/output buffer\n- pdwMultiplier (uint*): 12-byte extended precision multiplicand\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in pdwResult)\n\nStructure Layout (80-bit extended precision):\n| Offset | Size | Field              |\n|--------|------|--------------------|\n| 0      | 8    | 64-bit mantissa    |\n| 8      | 2    | exp[0:14], sign[15]|\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FFF: Max exponent (infinity/NaN)\n- 0x8000: Sign bit mask\n- 0xBFFE: Overflow threshold\n- 0x3FC0: Underflow threshold\n- 0xC002: Exponent bias adjustment (-0x3FFE)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9164e08642353fc9b6a5a942bb4e12cf",
