      "name": "CompareMultiByteStringsWithLocale",
      "signature": "int CompareMultiByteStringsWithLocale(LCID lcid, DWORD dwFlags, byte * pbStr1, int nStr1Len, byte * pbStr2, int nStr2Len, UINT nCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Compares two multi-byte strings using locale-specific collation rules.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Detect system string comparison support (Unicode vs ANSI)\n2. Adjust string lengths via CalcStringLengthBounded if positive\n3. If ANSI-only (mode=2): call CompareStringA directly\n4. If Unicode (mode=1): convert strings to wide chars via MultiByteToWideChar\n5. Handle edge cases for zero-length strings using lead byte checks\n6. Compare wide strings via CompareStringW\n\nParameters:\n- lcid (LCID): Locale identifier for comparison\n- dwFlags (DWORD): Comparison flags passed to CompareString\n- pbStr1 (byte*): First multi-byte string\n- nStr1Len (int): Length of first string (-1 for null-terminated)\n- pbStr2 (byte*): Second multi-byte string\n- nStr2Len (int): Length of second string (-1 for null-terminated)\n- nCodePage (UINT): Code page for conversion (0 = default)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: String 1 < String 2\n- 2: Strings equal\n- 3: String 1 > String 2\n- 0: Error occurred\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x9: MB_PRECOMPOSED|MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS flag for MultiByteToWideChar\n- g_nCompareMode: Cached comparison mode (1=Unicode, 2=ANSI)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
