      "name": "FindCharInStringMB",
      "signature": "byte * FindCharInStringMB(byte * pbStr, uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Multi-byte character-aware strchr. Finds first occurrence of a character in a string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If single-byte code page, delegate to standard strchr\n2. Otherwise acquire critical section 0x19 for thread safety\n3. Loop through string checking each character:\n   - If lead byte of multi-byte char (g_abCharTypeTable & 0x4), combine with next byte\n   - Compare against target character (single or multi-byte)\n4. Return pointer to found char or NULL if not found\n\nParameters:\n- pbStr (byte*): Null-terminated string to search\n- dwChar (uint): Character to find (can be multi-byte combined value)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to first occurrence of dwChar in pbStr, or NULL if not found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x19 (25): Critical section index for multi-byte operations\n- 0x4: Lead byte flag in character type table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:781017f4d855409582a95afe4ce13001",
