      "signature": "uint * AllocateResourcePoolBlock(void * pPoolContext, uint * pPoolConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new resource pool block with virtual memory backing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pool block allocation table capacity needs expansion (count >= capacity)\n2. If expansion needed, increase block table capacity by 0x20 slots\n3. Reallocate pool block table at pPoolContext[0x7a8] with new size * 8 bytes\n4. Return error (0x2ff) if table reallocation fails\n5. Calculate slot array size from pPoolConfig[0x1c] with 32-bit alignment:\n   - Formula: ((capacity + 0x1f) >> 5) << 2 bytes\n6. Allocate memory for pool block header (0x18 bytes) plus slot array via malloc\n7. Allocate virtual memory page via VirtualAlloc with size from pPoolConfig[0x20]\n8. Return error (0x320) if either malloc or VirtualAlloc fails\n9. Initialize pool block header with all zeros at offsets 0x0-0x14 (6 dwords)\n10. Store slot array pointer at block[0x4] = block + 0x18\n11. Zero-fill entire slot array using REP STOSD/STOSB instructions\n12. Store configuration reference at block[0x14] = pPoolConfig\n13. Store virtual memory base address at block[0x0] = pvVirtualMem\n14. Increment allocation counter at pPoolConfig[0x24]\n15. Call InsertPoolBlockSorted to register new block in sorted list\n16. Return pPoolBlock pointer on success\n\nParameters:\npPoolContext - void* pointer to pool management context containing table at offset 0x7a8\npPoolConfig - uint* pointer to pool configuration structure with fields:\n             [0x1c] = slot capacity per block\n             [0x20] = virtual memory size to allocate\n             [0x24] = allocation counter\n\nReturns:\nuint* - Pointer to allocated ResourcePoolBlock structure on success\n        Calls _exit(-1) on failure (memory allocation failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nError 0x2ff - Pool block table allocation overflow, triggers error handler\nError 0x320 - Memory allocation failure (malloc or VirtualAlloc), error code 800 decimal\nBlock structure includes 0x18 byte header plus variable-sized slot array\nSlot count computed as (capacity + 0x1f) >> 5 then masked to 30 bits (& 0x3fffffff)\nVirtual memory allocated with PAGE_COMMIT (0x1000) and PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE (0x4)\n\nStructure Layout (ResourcePoolBlock at returned pointer):\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type     Description\n0x00    4     virtual_memory     void*    Virtual memory base address allocated\n0x04    4     slot_array         uint*    Pointer to slot tracking array\n0x08    4     reserved_0         uint     Zero-initialized reserved field\n0x0c    4     reserved_1         uint     Zero-initialized reserved field\n0x10    4     reserved_2         uint     Zero-initialized reserved field\n0x14    4     config_ref         uint*    Back-reference to pPoolConfig\n0x18    var   slot_array_data    uint[]   Variable-length slot array (32-bit aligned)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:59ad52a59b452669abc0ef2503a759fa",
