      "name": "WaitForObjectHandle",
      "signature": "uint WaitForObjectHandle(void * pObject, uint dwTimeout)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Waits for a synchronization object's HANDLE with optional timeout.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load object pointer from stack parameter (ESP+4)\n2. Validate object pointer - check if NULL\n3. If NULL, return immediately with zero (NULL value in EAX)\n4. Extract HANDLE from object structure at fixed offset +0x114\n5. Prepare parameters: EDX contains handle, ESP+4 still contains timeout\n6. Tail-call to WaitForSingleObject with handle and timeout\n7. Return wait result to caller (WAIT_OBJECT_0, WAIT_TIMEOUT, WAIT_FAILED, etc.)\n\nParameters:\n  pObject - Pointer to object structure containing HANDLE at offset 0x114\n  dwTimeout - Timeout in milliseconds (0 = no wait, 0xFFFFFFFF = infinite)\n\nReturns:\n  DWORD - Result from WaitForSingleObject:\n    WAIT_OBJECT_0 (0) - Object is signaled\n    WAIT_TIMEOUT (258) - Timeout expired before signaling\n    WAIT_ABANDONED (128) - Mutex abandoned\n    WAIT_FAILED (4294967295) - Function call failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer is handled gracefully (returns 0)\n  - Uses fixed object structure offset (+0x114) for handle location\n  - Uses indirect jump through global function pointer at 0x6ff751a8\n  - Calling convention is __stdcall with 2 parameters (8 bytes on stack)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.10",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a17b83e22bf622ac87ecccbc0c3a84eb",
