      "signature": "SOCKET InitializeServerListener(u_short portNumber)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a network server listener socket and registers it with I/O completion port for async operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create I/O completion port for async socket operations via CreateIoCompletionPort()\n2. Check if completion port creation succeeded; on failure, log error and shutdown\n3. Create TCP/IP socket using socket(AF_INET=2, SOCK_STREAM=1, IPPROTO_TCP=0)\n4. Verify socket creation; return 0 (INVALID_SOCKET) if socket creation fails\n5. Configure socket options: SO_REUSEADDR (level 6/opt 1), level 0xffff options 8 and 4 all set to 1\n6. Set socket to non-blocking mode using ioctlsocket() with FIONBIO (0x8004667e)\n7. Build IPv4 sockaddr structure: family=AF_INET(2), convert port to network byte order via htons()\n8. Bind socket to address using bind(socket, sockaddr, 16 bytes)\n9. Check bind result; on failure, log error using szServerBindFailed and return 0\n10. Listen on socket with backlog of 250 (0xfa) using listen()\n11. Check listen result; on failure, log error using szServerListenFailed and return 0\n12. Retrieve socket index from server structure at offset 0xb8c (socket_count field)\n13. Increment socket count and store updated value back at offset 0xb8c\n14. Store I/O completion port handle at [server + 0xc08 + socketIndex*4]\n15. Store port number at [server + 0xba0 + socketIndex*2]\n16. Store socket handle at [server + 0xb90 + socketIndex*4]\n17. Set socket status flag to 1 (active) at [server + 0xba8 + socketIndex*4]\n18. Allocate 8 bytes for worker thread context using AllocateMemoryWithTracking()\n19. Initialize context: [0] = server pointer, [4] = socket index\n20. Create primary worker thread (ProcessServerConnectionIO) via CreateThread()\n21. Store thread handle at [server + 0xbd8 + socketIndex*4] and thread ID at [server + 0xbe8 + socketIndex*4]\n22. Check secondary thread flag at server offset 0xc18\n23. If flag is non-zero, allocate 8-byte context and create secondary worker thread (ReleaseSlotWithCriticalSection)\n24. Store secondary thread handle at [server + 0xc1c + socketIndex*4] and thread ID at [server + 0xc2c + socketIndex*4]\n25. Return socket handle on success\n\nParameters:\nportNumber (u_short): Port number to bind the listener socket to, in host byte order (converted to network byte order internally)\n\nReturns:\nSOCKET: Valid socket handle on success, 0 (INVALID_SOCKET) on any error condition\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- I/O completion port creation failure causes immediate shutdown via ShutdownResourcesAndExit\n- Socket creation failure returns 0 with error logged via ValidateAndInitializeParameter\n- Bind failure returns 0 after logging error message\n- Listen failure returns 0 after logging error message\n- Secondary thread creation is conditional on flag at server offset 0xc18\n- Server context pointer passed via EAX register (implicit __stdcall parameter)",
