      "signature": "void LogResourceAccessToFile(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Logs resource access information to file with optional version header.\n\nType 1 deallocation queue entry handler that records resource access timing\nand content to a log file. Called from ProcessMemoryDeallocQueue when processing\nqueue entries of type 1 (resource logging handler).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate context structure (implicit parameter EDI) has type field = 1\n2. If validation fails: Get return address context, cleanup Windows Sockets,\n   log error message, and shutdown via LogErrorAndShutdown\n3. Extract resource name string pointer from context offset +0x24\n4. Calculate resource name string length using Strlen\n5. Call FindOrCreateLogFile to open/create log file (returns FILE* and fileIndex)\n6. If file opened successfully:\n   a. Check version string flag at context offset +0x10\n   b. If flag set: Write formatted version string using 4 WORD values from\n      context offsets +0x1c, +0x1e, +0x20, +0x22 as major.minor.build.rev\n   c. Calculate pointer to resource data (name + length + 1)\n   d. Get length of resource data string\n   e. Write resource data to file using _fwrite\n7. Record current system tick count (GetTickCount) into timestamp array\n   at [g_dwResourceAccessTimestamps + fileIndex * 4]\n8. Restore registers and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EDI - Pointer to deallocation queue entry context structure\n    +0x0c - Entry type field (must equal 1)\n    +0x10 - Version flag (0=no version, nonzero=write version)\n    +0x1c - Version component 1 (WORD, major)\n    +0x1e - Version component 2 (WORD, minor)\n    +0x20 - Version component 3 (WORD, build)\n    +0x22 - Version component 4 (WORD, revision)\n    +0x24 - Resource name string pointer (null-terminated)\n  IMPLICIT ESP+8 - Stack address to receive fileIndex output from FindOrCreateLogFile\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; performs logging as side effect\n\nCalling Convention:\n  __stdcall - All parameters via registers/stack, callee cleanup\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Type validation failure (EDI+0x0c != 1) triggers shutdown sequence\n  Version string format: \"%02d:%02d:%02d.%03d  \" from szTimeFormatString\n  Resource data pointer calculated as: &name[strlen(name) + 1]\n  Timestamp array indexed by fileIndex from FindOrCreateLogFile\n  File operations may fail silently if log file creation fails\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_szUnrecoverableErrorMessage (0x6ff7850c) - Error message string\n  szTimeFormatString (0x6ff76f34) - Version format template\n  g_dwResourceAccessTimestamps (0x6ff818a8) - Array of access timestamps\n  szSourceFileLocation (0x6ff768ec) - Source location for error logging\n  g_pfnGetTickCount (0x6ff75030) - Function pointer to GetTickCount\n\nStructure Layout (Context at EDI):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name            Type       Description\n  ------  ----  --------------------  ---------  ----------------------\n  +00     4     Flink                 PVOID      Forward link\n  +04     4     Blink                 PVOID      Backward link\n  +08     4     dwMemorySize          DWORD      Entry size\n  +0C     4     dwEntryType           DWORD      Type (1=log)\n  +10     4     dwVersionFlag         DWORD      Write version flag\n  +1C     2     wVersionMajor         WORD       Version major\n  +1E     2     wVersionMinor         WORD       Version minor\n  +20     2     wVersionBuild         WORD       Version build\n  +22     2     wVersionRevision      WORD       Version revision\n  +24     4     pszResourceName       char*      Resource name ptr",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:06690f5318a3c553e5ea099481bc76c2",
