      "signature": "SOCKET AcceptAndInitializeConnectionSocket(uint * pServerIndex, sockaddr * peerAddr, int * pPeerAddrLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Accepts an incoming socket connection on a listening socket and initializes the client connection structure with all necessary endpoint information and I/O completion port registration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate server context base offset by multiplying server index by 0xb0 (struct size)\n2. Initialize 18 DWORD performance counter timestamp buffer at offset +0x91c\n3. Acquire critical section and increment accept attempt counter at +0x964\n4. Call accept() to get connected socket or SOCKET_ERROR (-1)\n5. Record post-accept performance counter timestamp at +0x924\n6. If accept() failed (-1), increment error counter at +0x968 and return -1\n7. Extract peer IP address from sockaddr structure (sin_addr at offset +4)\n8. Validate peer IP address using hash table lookup (FindAndActivateHashTableEntry)\n9. Record IP validation performance counter at +0x92c\n10. Check if IP is valid; if not, set error flag 0x1\n11. Validate peer port and connection timestamp (CheckElementTimestampValid)\n12. If port invalid, handle duplicate attempt and set error flag 0x2\n13. Record port validation performance counter at +0x934\n14. If no validation errors, call TrackAndValidateConnectionUsage to verify connection\n15. Call ValidatePermissionMask to check access permissions\n16. Record permission validation performance counter at +0x93c\n17. If any validation failed (error flag != 0), call HandleDuplicateConnectionAttempt\n18. Log error and close socket if validation fails, return -1\n19. Create new client socket structure via InitializeServerConnection with peer address\n20. Store connection index (parameter 1) in structure field at offset +0x14\n21. Record socket handle registration performance counter at +0x944\n22. Configure socket as non-blocking using ioctlsocket with FIONBIO (0x8004667e)\n23. Get peer endpoint address via getpeername to structure offset +0x88, copy 8 bytes\n24. Get local socket address via getsockname to structure offset +0x78, copy 8 bytes\n25. Verify socket handle in structure matches connection socket; if mismatch, log critical error and exit\n26. Register socket with I/O completion port using connection index as completion key\n27. Record completion port registration performance counter at +0x94c\n28. Call InitiateAsyncDataRead to add socket to active connection pool\n29. If add to pool failed, increment failure counter at +0x970 and return -1\n30. Record socket addition performance counter at +0x954\n31. If custom connection callback is set at offset +0xbc4, invoke it with source location info\n32. Record callback performance counter at +0x95c\n33. Acquire critical section and increment success counter at +0x974\n34. Return client socket handle on success, -1 on any failure\n\nParameters:\n  pServerIndex: uint* - Pointer to server listening socket index (used to identify which listening socket)\n  peerAddr: sockaddr* - Output structure filled with peer socket address by accept() call\n  pPeerAddrLength: int* - Input/output length of peer address (set to 0x10 = 16 bytes on input)\n\nReturns:\n  SOCKET - Connected socket handle on success, or (SOCKET)-1 on any failure condition\n\nError Conditions:\n  - accept() returns SOCKET_ERROR (-1): Listening socket not available\n  - IP validation fails: Peer IP address failed hash table lookup or blacklist check\n  - Port validation fails: Peer port out of valid range or timestamp invalid\n  - Connection tracking fails: TrackAndValidateConnectionUsage returns non-zero\n  - Permission check fails: ValidatePermissionMask returns non-zero\n  - Socket structure creation fails: InitializeServerConnection returns NULL\n  - Socket handle mismatch: Structure handle doesn't match accepted socket\n  - Completion port registration fails: CreateIoCompletionPort fails\n  - Pool add fails: InitiateAsyncDataRead returns 0\n\nPerformance Counters:\n  - +0x91c-0x95c: 9 LARGE_INTEGER performance counter snapshots capture latency at each major step\n  - Enables identification of bottlenecks in accept/validation/initialization pipeline\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic number 0xb0: Server context structure size in bytes\n  - Magic number 0x8004667e: IOCTL_SOCKET_FIONBIO for non-blocking socket configuration\n  - Magic number -0x7ffb9982: Complement of 0x7ffb9982, FIONBIO constant\n  - Error flag 0x1: IP validation failed\n  - Error flag 0x2: Port validation failed\n  - Error flag 0x3: Permission validation failed\n  - Critical section at +0x8b4: Protects counter increments and ensures atomic statistics\n  - Offset +0xbc4: Optional callback function pointer for connection notification\n  - Offset +0xc08: Array of I/O completion port handles indexed by connection index\n\nStructure Layout (Client Socket Context):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name               Type        Description\n  0x00    4     socket_handle            SOCKET      Connected socket handle\n  0x04    4     context_ptr              void*       Pointer to parent context\n  0x10    4     local_address            sockaddr    Local socket address\n  0x14    4     connection_index         uint        Server connection index (set in this function)\n  0x88    4     peer_address             sockaddr    Peer socket address (set by getpeername)\n  0x90    4     peer_address_reserved    byte[8]     Reserved/padding for peer address\n  0x98    4     total_size               -           Context structure ~0x100+ bytes total",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
