      "name": "ProcessCharacterDataWithLock",
      "signature": "int ProcessCharacterDataWithLock(int * pCharData, int nStreamLineOffset, dword dwParamType)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Acquire lock, process character data, and release lock in thread-safe manner.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock on pCharData (or associated global based on address range)\n2. Call ProcessCharacterDataCore with streaming parameters and type parameter\n3. Store return value from processing\n4. Release critical section lock\n5. Return processing result (success/failure code)\n\nParameters:\npCharData - Pointer to character data structure or handle\nnStreamLineOffset - Stream line offset for character data processing\ndwParamType - Parameter type code (0=standard, 1=calculate stream lines, 2=other)\n\nReturns:\n0 on success, -1 on error or invalid parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Lock acquisition uses address range detection to determine lock mechanism\n- Different lock handling for in-range vs out-of-range addresses\n- Return value propagates error/success status from core processing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.10",
