      "name": "ProcessExceptionListNodes",
      "signature": "void ProcessExceptionListNodes(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Processes exception handler linked list nodes for C++ EH cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load node list pointer from implicit context (EBX+8)\n2. Loop while node pointer is positive (>0) indicating valid node\n3. Load data pointer from current node offset +0\n4. If data pointer is null, advance to next node iteration\n5. If data pointer is non-null:\n   a. Load offset value from node offset +4\n   b. Check offset sign (via TEST instruction):\n      - If negative (TEST < 0): compute target as bitwise NOT (~offset)\n      - If non-negative (TEST >= 0): compute target as (pNodePtr + offsetValue - dataPtr[4])\n   c. Store data pointer at computed target address\n   d. Load next node pointer from current data[0]\n   e. Load offset from current data[4]\n   f. Update target[4] with offset value\n   g. Clear pNodePtr[0] to mark node as processed\n   h. Clear pNodePtr[4] to mark node as processed\n6. Jump back to loop_start for next iteration\n7. Exit loop when node pointer <= 0\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionContext (EBX implicit): Provides access to node list at offset +8, contains pointer to exception handler context structure with linked list of nodes to process\n  (No explicit parameters passed on stack)\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function completes linked list processing and returns to caller without return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Negative offsets indicate absolute memory addresses computed via bitwise NOT (~offset)\n  - Non-negative offsets indicate relative addresses calculated from node position\n  - Null data pointers skip processing but continue loop iteration\n  - Node list termination marked by node pointer <= 0\n  - Node structure layout: offset +0 = data pointer, offset +4 = offset value\n  - Implicit EBX context pointer provides access to exception handler state at offset +8",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
