      "name": "CompareFieldLessOrEqual",
      "signature": "bool CompareFieldLessOrEqual(void * this, int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Compares integer fields at offset 0xc from two objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 32-bit field at offset +0xc from the first object (this pointer in ECX)\n2. Load the second object pointer from stack parameter\n3. Subtract the second object's field at +0xc from the first object's field\n4. Set result to true if subtraction result is <= 0 (first <= second)\n5. Return boolean result in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- this: Pointer to first object (implicit in ECX per __thiscall)\n- pSecondObject: Pointer to second object to compare against\n\nReturns:\n- bool: true if this->field_0xc <= pSecondObject->field_0xc, false otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Equal values return true (<=, not just <)\n- Comparison performed on signed 32-bit integers\n- No pointer validation performed\n- Function assumes both objects have valid field at offset 0xc\n\nStructure Layout:\nBoth objects must contain a signed 32-bit comparison field.\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name     | Type | Description\n0x0c   | 4    | compareField   | int  | Signed comparison value\n\nNote:\nThis function cannot be decompiled but documentation is based on disassembly analysis.",
