      "name": "CountVectorBits",
      "signature": "uint CountVectorBits(int pVectorDesc)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Counts the number of set bits in a vector descriptor using Kernighan's algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare input value in EAX against constant 0x40 (64-bit limit)\n2. If input < 0x40: Apply iterative bit clearing using (n-1) & n pattern\n3. Each iteration removes the lowest set bit from the current value\n4. Loop continues while cleared bits remain (JNZ at 0x6fbf3c57)\n5. After loop completes, test if final value is exactly zero\n6. Return 1 if all bits cleared (input was power of 2), else return original value\n7. If input >= 0x40: Store limit constant 0x40 to descriptor[+0xC], return 0x40\n\nParameters:\n- pVectorDesc (int): Vector descriptor pointer, used for writing overflow limit\n- [EAX implicit]: Input bitmask value containing vector bits to analyze\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Returns 1 if input is power of 2 (exactly one bit set), else returns original input value if < 0x40 and not power of 2, or 0x40 constant if input >= 0x40 (capped to limit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nInput value 0 returns 1 (Kernighan's algorithm clears zero bits immediately). Input >= 0x40 triggers descriptor update at offset +0xC and returns max limit. Uses implicit EAX register parameter (not standard calling convention). This is a helper for vector capacity checking (0x40 = 64-bit maximum).\n\nStructure Layout:\nVectorDescriptor:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n------  ----  ----------------  --------  -----------\n0x000C  0x04  dwMaxCapacity     DWORD     Maximum vector capacity limit",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ef01624ba1fdf8f67386976d82d63fb9",
