      "name": "ConvertDoubleToExtendedWithRounding",
      "signature": "float10 * ConvertDoubleToExtendedWithRounding(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__, float10 * pReturnStorage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts double-precision (64-bit) floating point to extended-precision (80-bit) format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check hardware state: verify g_dwFPUControlWord enabled, MXCSR bits[12:4]=0x1f80, FPU control word bits[6:0]=0x7f\n2. If fast path available, load input value into XMM0 from stack parameter\n3. Extract IEEE 754 exponent field by shifting right 52 bits (bits 62:52)\n4. Test exponent sign bit (0x800) to determine positive or negative exponent\n5. For positive exponents (bit clear):\n   - If exponent < 0x3ff: return 0.0 (underflow, value < 1.0)\n   - If exponent 0x3ff-0x432: round mantissa and return normalized value\n   - If exponent >= 0x433: check for NaN/Inf special values\n6. For negative exponents (bit set):\n   - If exponent < 0xbff: apply denormal correction masks\n   - If exponent 0xbff-0xc32: subtract correction term from mantissa\n   - If exponent >= 0xc33: check for NaN/Inf special values\n7. Detect NaN using UCOMISD self-comparison (sets parity flag if NaN)\n8. Call MathOpDispatcher with error code 0x3ed for NaN inputs\n9. Store result to stack and load onto FPU stack (ST0) for return\n10. If fast path unavailable, use fallback: save FPU context with __ctrlfp()\n11. Check exponent 0x7ff0 for special values, call __sptype() classifier\n12. Handle Inf (type 1-2) and QNaN (type 3) with specialized handlers\n13. For normal values, call __frnd() for rounding\n14. If rounding changed value or precision flag set, call HandleMathError\n15. Restore FPU context and return result\n\nParameters:\n  pReturnStorage - Pointer to 10-byte buffer for extended precision result\n  inputValue - Double-precision input value (8 bytes, IEEE 754 binary64)\n  roundingMode - Rounding mode selector (unused in fast SSE2 path)\n\nReturns:\n  ST0 - 80-bit extended precision result loaded onto FPU stack\n  EAX - Pointer to return storage buffer (for ABI compatibility)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  NaN inputs: Delegated to MathOpDispatcher (error code 0x3ed)\n  Infinity: Handled by fallback __sptype() classifier (returns type 1 or 2)\n  Denormalized numbers: Corrected using masks at addresses 0x6ff753c0-0x6ff753f0\n  Underflow (|value| < 1.0): Returns 0.0 via FLDZ instruction\n  Exponent thresholds: 0x3ff (bias 1023), 0x432 (overflow), 0xbff (neg bias), 0xc32 (neg overflow)\n  Magic numbers: 0x1f80 (MXCSR exception masks), 0x7f (FPU precision control), 0x800 (sign bit), 0x7ff0 (Inf/NaN exponent)\n\nGlobal Data:\n  g_dwFPUControlWord - Fast path enable flag (0x6ffa712c)\n  g_dblExponentThresholdTable - Exponent threshold for shift calculation (0x6ff753d0)\n  g_dblMantissaCorrectionMask - Correction mask for negative mantissa (0x6ff753c0)\n  g_dblDenormalCorrectionMask - Final correction for denormals (0x6ff753e0)\n  g_dblDenormalComparisonMask - Comparison mask for denormal detection (0x6ff753f0)\n  g_dblExponentIsolationMask - Isolates exponent bits from mantissa (0x6ff75400)\n  g_dblDenormalizedConstant - Correction constant for denormals (0x6ff79040)\n\nDependencies:\n  MathOpDispatcher (0x6ff579f0) - Handles NaN and exceptional values\n  HandleMathError - Processes rounding errors in fallback path\n  __ctrlfp - FPU control word manipulation (save/restore context)\n  __frnd - Legacy FPU rounding function for fallback path\n  __sptype - Special value classifier (1=Inf, 2=Inf, 3=QNaN)\n  __handle_qnan1 - Quiet NaN handler for QNaN propagation\n\nCalled By:\n  CalculateDateOffsetValue (0x6ff60545, 0x6ff6055b)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
