      "name": "ReleaseLockForFileHandleAllocation",
      "signature": "void ReleaseLockForFileHandleAllocation(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Release critical section lock for file handle allocation\n\nThis is a thin wrapper function that releases a critical section lock\nused during file handle allocation operations. It provides a centralized\nexit point for lock management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push parameter 0xb (critical section index 11) onto stack\n2. Call LeaveCriticalSectionByIndex to release the lock\n3. Pop return address and return to caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Critical section is unlocked after execution.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses hardcoded critical section index 0xb (11)\n- Callee (__stdcall) removes return address from stack\n- Called by __alloc_osfhnd during file handle allocation cleanup\n\nNote:\nThis appears to be part of a runtime library's file handle management\nsystem that uses critical sections to protect allocation/deallocation.",
