      "name": "InitializeModule",
      "signature": "int InitializeModule(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "InitializeModule - Module initialization entry point\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push ECX and EDX to preserve registers\n2. Load 8-byte parameter from caller's stack into initialization context\n3. Prepare initialization context on stack at [ESP+8]\n4. Clear EAX register\n5. Call initialization handler at 0x6ff6b0c0 with context address in ECX\n6. Set return value to 1 (success indicator)\n7. Pop saved registers and return with 8-byte stack cleanup (__stdcall)\n\nParameters:\nvoid - No explicit parameters\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 (success/true) regardless of initialization handler result\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEntry point function called from multiple locations (0x6ff7d9c4 and Entry Point)\nUses __stdcall convention with 8-byte stack parameter cleanup\nThe initialization context is 4 bytes (uint) placed on stack at [ESP+8]\nCallee function at 0x6ff6b0c0 (DeallocateResourcePoolElement) handles actual initialization\nReturn value 1 indicates successful initialization completion\nThis function appears to be a wrapper/dispatcher for module initialization logic",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5fcfe8683d09a8f8b3918e5b0520ca46",
