      "name": "GetOrInitializeDataPointer",
      "signature": "void * GetOrInitializeDataPointer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validate or provide default data pointer\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test EAX register to check if it contains a non-zero (valid) pointer\n2. If EAX is zero (null pointer), load g_pDefaultGameSession address into EAX\n3. Return with the pointer value in EAX (either input or default)\n\nParameters:\n  (implicit) EAX: Input pointer value to validate (or NULL to use default)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: Either the input EAX value if non-zero, or g_pDefaultGameSession if input was null\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If EAX is 0 on entry, returns g_pDefaultGameSession address\n  - If EAX is non-zero on entry, returns EAX unchanged (pass-through behavior)\n  - This is a __stdcall function so callee cleans up stack",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
