      "name": "UpdatePoolNodeListPosition",
      "signature": "void UpdatePoolNodeListPosition(uint dwNewCount, void * pPoolMetadata)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Updates the position of a pool node in a doubly-linked allocation list.\nWhen a resource's allocation changes, this function removes the node from\nits current position in the linked list and reinserts it at the head,\nmaintaining a most-recently-modified ordering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load previous node pointer from poolNode[+0xc]\n2. Validate previous node is not null (early return if unlinked)\n3. Load stride value from prevNode[+0x8] for validation\n4. Validate stride <= metadata[+0x1c] (capacity check)\n5. Unlink node from current position by updating previous->next\n6. If node is not the tail (next != null):\n   - Update next->prev to point to previous node\n7. If node is the tail (next == null):\n   - Update metadata[+0x2c] (tail pointer) to previous node\n8. Load list head from metadata[+0x28]\n9. Insert node at head: node->next = head\n10. Update old head's prev: head->prev = node\n11. Update metadata[+0x28] to point to new head (node)\n12. Clear node's prev pointer (mark as new head)\n13. Return\n\nParameters:\n  newCount (ECX): uint\n    New element count value (used in validation)\n  pPoolMetadata (EDX): void *\n    Pointer to pool metadata structure containing:\n    - [+0x1c]: element count/capacity threshold\n    - [+0x28]: doubly-linked list head pointer\n    - [+0x2c]: doubly-linked list tail pointer\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value; modifies linked list in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Early exit: If poolNode->prev is null (node not in list)\n  Validation failure: If stride > metadata capacity (JL at 0x6ff6ab6e)\n  Tail handling: Updates metadata tail pointer when moving tail node\n  List structure: Doubly-linked list with implicit node passed in EAX\n\nPool Node Structure Layout (inferred from offsets):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type      Description\n  +0x00   4     reserved0     uint      (unknown usage)\n  +0x04   4     reserved1     uint      (unknown usage)\n  +0x08   4     stride        uint      Data element stride/spacing\n  +0x0c   4     prevNode      Node*     Previous node in doubly-linked list\n  +0x10   4     nextNode      Node*     Next node in doubly-linked list\n  Total: 0x14 bytes minimum\n\nPool Metadata Structure Layout (offsets accessed):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type      Description\n  +0x1c   4     capacity      uint      Element count capacity threshold\n  +0x28   4     headNode      Node*     Head of doubly-linked list\n  +0x2c   4     tailNode      Node*     Tail of doubly-linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e8b3be627ae5c77f4b645322abd0e127",
