      "name": "RemoveErrorFromDebugPool",
      "signature": "void RemoveErrorFromDebugPool(int pResourceContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Removes an error node from the debug pool's linked list and releases its memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load error node pointer from EAX and calculate base pointer by subtracting 4 bytes\n2. Calculate hash bucket index: (errorNodeBase) % 0x3ff (1023 buckets)\n3. Extract critical section pointer from resourceContext at offset +4\n4. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity() to validate critical section (log entry 0x3c3)\n5. Enter critical section lock for thread-safe list manipulation\n6. Load first node in hash bucket from resourceContext[0x7ac + bucketIndex*4]\n7. Initialize pCurrentNode to null, pNextNode to first bucket node\n8. Walk linked list: iterate through nodes until matching error node found\n9. If pNextNode is null, node not found in list; proceed to cleanup\n10. If pNextNode matches errorNodeBase, unlink the matching node:\n    - If pCurrentNode is null (head of bucket): replace bucket pointer with next node\n    - If pCurrentNode exists: update pCurrentNode->next to skip errorNode\n11. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity() to exit critical section (log entry 0x3e4)\n12. Leave critical section lock\n13. Call _free() to deallocate error node memory\n14. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pResourceContext: Opaque handle to NetworkResourceContext; contains critical section\n                    pointer at offset +4 and hash bucket array at offset +0x7ac\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value; function always completes cleanup and exits\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Hash bucket calculation: Uses (errorNodePointer - 4) % 0x3ff to determine bucket\n  Linked list removal: Handles both head node and middle node removal correctly\n  Critical section: Protected via ValidateDataStructureIntegrity() entry/exit\n  Memory cleanup: All error nodes freed regardless of bucket location\n  Error node structure: Contains 4-byte header followed by error data (offset -4)\n\nStructure Layout (NetworkResourceContext):\n  Offset   Size   Field Name           Type       Description\n  +0x000   4      unknown_0            pointer    Unknown field 0\n  +0x004   4      pCriticalSection     pointer    Critical section for thread safety\n  +0x7ac   4+     pBucketArray[]       pointer[]  Hash bucket array (1023 buckets)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:6fea067fe7da99204f92ce68713ef2f1",
