      "name": "DeallocateResourcePoolElement",
      "signature": "void DeallocateResourcePoolElement(uint * pResourceAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Deallocate a resource pool element by clearing its allocation bit and decrementing the active count.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate context parameter; use default game context if null (passed in EAX)\n2. Validate resource address is not null; return early if invalid\n3. Call FindResourceByThreshold() to retrieve pool metadata structure\n4. Validate metadata returned successfully; return if null\n5. Validate resource address >= pool base address; return if below range\n6. Load critical section pointer from metadata[5] for thread synchronization\n7. Calculate element index as (resourceAddress - baseAddress) / stride\n8. Validate element index < pool capacity; log error 0x5d2 if out of bounds\n9. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity() to verify critical section state\n10. Enter critical section for thread-safe bit manipulation\n11. Calculate bitmask array offset: baseAddress[1] + (index >> 5) * 4 bytes\n12. Extract bit position within dword: index & 0x1f (bits 0-4)\n13. Test if allocation bit is currently set in bitmask array\n14. If bit is set: clear it using AND with inverted bitmask\n15. Load active element count from metadata[2] and decrement by 1\n16. Store updated count back to metadata[2]\n17. Call UpdatePoolNodeListPosition() with new count and critical section\n18. Log unlock operation with opcode 0x605 via logging callback\n19. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity() again before releasing lock\n20. Leave critical section to release lock\n21. Return from function (caller cleanup 8 bytes of stack)\n\nParameters:\n  pResourceAddress: [ECX] Pointer to resource element within pool; used to calculate the element's index by subtracting pool base address and dividing by element stride\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value; operation result indicated by side effects (count decrement and bit clear)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Resource address validation: Must be non-null and within allocated pool range\n  Bitmask representation: Each DWORD holds 32 element allocation bits; index >> 5 selects DWORD, index & 0x1f selects bit within DWORD\n  Bit already cleared: If allocation bit is not set, logs error 0x609 and skips count decrement; no error propagation\n  Index out of bounds: If calculated index >= pool capacity, logs error 0x5d2 and returns without modifying pool state\n  Critical section semantics: Acquired before bit manipulation and held throughout count update\n  Global lookup tables: g_BitMaskLookupTable[32] for set mask and gdwInvBitMasks[32] for clear mask\n  Active count semantics: Decremented once per element; represents number of currently allocated (non-freed) elements\n  Default context: g_pDefaultGameSession used if context parameter (EAX) is null at entry\n\nStructure Layout - Resource Pool Metadata (from metadata[N] access):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name             Type      Description\n  0x0     4     baseAddress            pointer   Pointer to first pool element (DWORD array)\n  0x4     4     bitmaskArrayBase       pointer   Pointer to allocation bitmask array\n  0x8     4     activeElementCount     uint      Number of currently allocated elements\n  0xc     4     reserved1              uint      Unused/padding field\n  0x10    4     reserved2              uint      Unused/padding field\n  0x14    4     pCriticalSection       pointer   Win32 CRITICAL_SECTION structure (synchronization)\n  0x18    4     elementStride          uint      Byte offset between consecutive elements\n  0x1c    4     totalCapacity          uint      Maximum number of allocatable elements\n  Total Size: 0x20 bytes (32 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:6fea067fe7da99204f92ce68713ef2f1",
