      "name": "InitializeGameStructureWithLocking",
      "signature": "uint InitializeGameStructureWithLocking(GameSessionConfig * pGameStruct)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initializes or validates a game session structure with thread-safe critical section locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameter pGameStruct - if NULL, use default global at 0x6ff9af94\n2. Calculate critical section pointer at offset +0x4 from structure base\n3. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity on critical section\n4. Enter critical section lock via EnterCriticalSection to ensure thread-safe access\n5. Load and cache result value from structure field at offset 0x17a8\n6. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity again on critical section\n7. Leave critical section lock via LeaveCriticalSection\n8. Return the cached result value in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  pGameStruct: Pointer to GameSessionConfig structure (optional)\n    - If NULL: uses global default at 0x6ff9af94 (g_pDefaultGameSession)\n    - Offset +0x4: LPCRITICAL_SECTION for synchronization\n    - Offset +0x17a8: Value field to retrieve and return\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Value retrieved from pGameStruct->field at offset 0x17a8\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Thread-safe design: Both validates before/after critical section entry\n  - Default fallback: NULL parameter automatically uses global game session\n  - Critical section ensures only one thread accesses structure during validation\n  - Structure minimum size requirement: at least 0x17ac bytes (0x17a8 + 4 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:6fea067fe7da99204f92ce68713ef2f1",
