      "name": "AllocateNextPoolNode",
      "signature": "ResourcePoolNode * AllocateNextPoolNode(ResourcePoolNode * * ppAllocatedNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and retrieves the next available slot from a resource pool node, managing a doubly-linked list of pool nodes and handling capacity tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current list head from pool state at offset 0x28\n2. If list is empty (head is null), allocate new node via AllocatePoolBlock\n3. If new node allocation succeeds, initialize as both head and tail and return node\n4. If list not empty, load node capacity threshold from pool state offset 0x1c\n5. Compare current node size at offset 0x8 against capacity threshold\n6. If capacity available, call FindNextSlotInNodeArray to get next available slot ID\n7. If slot ID is valid (>= 0), return current node and slot ID\n8. If capacity exhausted or no valid slot, allocate new node via AllocatePoolBlock\n9. If new node allocated, link into doubly-linked list: new node prev points to old head, old head next points to new node\n10. Update head pointer to new node, return new node address to caller\n\nParameters:\nppAllocatedNode - Pointer to output variable where allocated/current node address is stored\n\nReturns:\nResourcePoolNode * - Address of the allocated or current node (stored via ppAllocatedNode)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list: Creates first node and uses both head and tail pointers\n- Capacity exhausted: Allocates new node and relinks into list maintaining doubly-linked structure\n- Allocation failure: Returns nullptr without updating state\n- Implicit registers: poolContext in EBX, pPoolState in ESI passed by caller (AllocateMemorySlotFromPool)\n\nStructure Layout (ResourcePoolNode at allocated pointer):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type       Description\n0x00    4     prev_node         uint*      Previous node in doubly-linked list\n0x04    4     slot_array        uint*      Array of available slots in this node\n0x08    4     current_size      uint       Current number of allocated slots\n0x0c    4     next_node         uint*      Next node in doubly-linked list\n0x10    4     parent_list       uint*      Back reference to parent list structure\n\nPool State Structure (ESI + offset):\n0x1c    4     capacity_limit    uint       Maximum slots per node before allocation\n0x28    4     list_head         uint*      Pointer to head of node list\n0x2c    4     list_tail         uint*      Pointer to tail of node list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:780fdd1b130dc71a93c61f7ef8fcbb06",
