      "name": "QueueTimedEventIfManagerReady",
      "signature": "int QueueTimedEventIfManagerReady(int eventData2, int eventData1, int delayMs)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Conditionally queues a timed event if the event manager is initialized and ready.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global event manager context pointer from g_pGameEventContext\n2. Check if the event manager pointer is valid (non-null)\n3. If manager is initialized: Call QueueTimedEventInManager with manager context, delay, and event data parameters, and return the result code\n4. If manager not initialized: Return 0xffffffff error code (-1)\n\nParameters:\n- eventData2: Second event data parameter (ECX register, __fastcall)\n- eventData1: First event data parameter (EDX register, __fastcall)\n- delayMs: Delay in milliseconds until the timed event triggers (stack ESP+8)\n\nReturns:\n- int: Result code from QueueTimedEventInManager if manager is ready\n- 0xffffffff (-1) if event manager context not initialized\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns immediately with error code if event manager not yet initialized\n- No memory allocation occurs if manager is null\n- Global g_pGameEventContext is loaded from 0x6ffa6e68\n\nReferences:\n- QueueTimedEventInManager: Performs the actual event queue operation if manager is ready\n- g_pGameEventContext: Global event manager instance pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
