      "name": "ExtractModuleDirectory",
      "signature": "int ExtractModuleDirectory(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Extracts the directory path from a module's full path by truncating after the last path separator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls GetModuleFileNameA to retrieve the module's full file path into pPathBuffer\n2. Scans the buffer byte-by-byte to find the null-terminator and calculate string length\n3. Searches backwards from the string end to locate the last path separator (backslash, forward slash, or colon)\n4. If no separator found, returns 0 (failure) - path must contain directory component\n5. If separator is a colon (drive letter like C:), preserves it in the output\n6. Null-terminates the string at the separator position to create directory-only path\n7. Returns 1 (success) when directory extraction completes\n\nParameters:\n  pszPathBuffer [char *] - Pointer to output buffer for extracted directory path; input contains module path on entry\n  nPathBufferSize [int] - Maximum size of pszPathBuffer in bytes; passed to GetModuleFileNameA\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1 if directory extraction successful, 0 on failure (no separator found or GetModuleFileNameA failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Drive letter paths (e.g., C:\\path\\file.exe) are truncated to C: (includes colon)\n  - UNC paths (e.g., \\\\server\\share\\file.exe) are truncated to \\\\server\\share\n  - If GetModuleFileNameA fails, returns 0 immediately\n  - If no path separators found in string, returns 0 (failure)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:8aaab76887bbbc848a42466b4b78534f",
