      "signature": "void * EnumerateLoadedProcessModules(uint processId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Enumerates all loaded modules for a specified process and returns a sorted linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load kernel32.dll and tlhelp32.dll (in order) to get toolhelp32 API functions\n2. For each DLL, use GetProcAddress to load CreateToolhelp32Snapshot, Module32First, and Module32Next\n3. If all functions load successfully, break; otherwise free library and try next DLL\n4. Call CreateToolhelp32Snapshot(TH32CS_SNAPMODULE=8, processId) to create module snapshot\n5. Validate snapshot handle (must not be 0xFFFFFFFF)\n6. Call Module32First to get first MODULEENTRY32 structure from snapshot\n7. For each module entry:\n   a. Allocate 0x210-byte (528-byte) module node structure from memory pool\n   b. Zero-fill entire structure (0x84 = 132 dwords)\n   c. Copy module file name from stack buffer A (offset +0x104) to allocated structure (+0x104)\n   d. Copy base name from stack buffer B (offset +0x000) to allocated structure (+0x000)\n   e. Store 3 module info fields at offsets +0x204, +0x208, +0x20c (from MODULEENTRY32)\n   f. Insert node into sorted linked list using binary search on offset +0x204 field\n8. Call Module32Next to fetch next module entry\n9. When done, close snapshot handle and free library\n10. Return pointer to head of sorted linked list (or NULL if failed)\n\nParameters:\n  processId (DWORD): Process ID to enumerate modules for (TH32CS_SNAPMODULE scope parameter)\n\nReturns:\n  void *: Pointer to head of sorted linked list of module node structures\n          Each node is 0x210 bytes with next pointer at offset +0x20c\n          Returns NULL (0x0) on error (DLL load failure or snapshot creation failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function attempts to load tlhelp32.dll first, then kernel32.dll (tries 2 DLLs maximum)\n  - Module list is maintained in sorted order by comparing offset +0x204 field (module base name)\n  - Snapshot handle is checked for INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE (0xFFFFFFFF) \n  - All allocated nodes are zero-filled before populating with data\n  - File paths are null-terminated strings copied byte-by-byte from stack buffers\n\nStructure Layout (Module Node - 0x210 bytes):\n  Offset  Size   Field Name            Type         Description\n  0x000   0x104  szModuleBaseName      char[260]    Module base file name path\n  0x104   0x100  szModuleFullPath      char[256]    Module full file path  \n  0x204   0x004  dwBaseAddress         DWORD        Module base address from MODULEENTRY32\n  0x208   0x004  dwModuleSize          DWORD        Module size from MODULEENTRY32\n  0x20c   0x004  pNextModule           void *       Next module in sorted linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
      "method": "STR",
