      "name": "InitializeCleanupForEntryPoint",
      "signature": "void InitializeCleanupForEntryPoint(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize cleanup operation at entry point.\n\nThis wrapper function signals the cleanup subsystem to begin reference counting and\nresource cleanup when called from the program entry point. It passes a cleanup flag\nvia the EDI register to DecrementReferenceCountAndCleanup, which manages a reference\ncounter for symbol handler initialization state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EDI register to stack using PUSH (preserve caller's EDI value)\n2. Set EDI = 1 to signal cleanup operation to called function\n3. Call DecrementReferenceCountAndCleanup() with implicit EDI parameter\n4. Restore original EDI value from stack using POP\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - This is a parameterless entry point wrapper\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Cleanup status is handled internally by DecrementReferenceCountAndCleanup\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called directly from program entry point (EXTERNAL reference)\n- Uses implicit parameter passing via EDI register (non-standard calling convention artifact)\n- Reference count decrement and cleanup logic delegated to DecrementReferenceCountAndCleanup\n- Critical section protection handled in called function\n\nNotes:\n- Thin wrapper for cleanup initialization during process exit sequence\n- EDI register serves as implicit parameter flag (1 = cleanup enabled)\n- Part of symbol handler lifecycle management system",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:60975173380f70991fb49c7cb0345f9a",
