      "name": "WriteCrashDumpFile",
      "signature": "void WriteCrashDumpFile(uint exceptionCode, uint exceptionAddress, uint exceptionFlags, void * exceptionData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Writes exception context and memory data to a crash dump file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize file path buffer to empty string (null-terminated)\n2. Call ExtractModuleDirectory to determine if crash dumps are enabled\n3. If enabled (result != 0):\n   - Append path separator to create directory path\n   - Call CreateDirectoryPathRecursive to create nested directory structure\n4. Append \"Crashdump\" filename to the path\n5. Call OpenFileForCrashDump to open the file for writing\n6. If file opened successfully (handle != NULL):\n   - Load exception context values (code, address, flags) from stack parameters\n   - Calculate total data size: exceptionDataSize * 4 bytes\n   - Copy exception data memory region to stack buffer using CopyMemoryBuffer\n   - Write combined data to file: [context_16_bytes + data_N_bytes]\n   - Close the file handle\n\nParameters:\n- exceptionCode: uint - Exception code identifying the error type\n- exceptionAddress: uint - Memory address where exception occurred\n- exceptionFlags: uint - Exception flags/type information bits\n- exceptionData: void* - Pointer to memory region containing exception data\n\nReturns:\n- void - No return value; performs file I/O silently without error reporting\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If directory creation check returns 0, skips directory creation but still attempts file write\n- If file cannot be opened, silently returns without error notification\n- File path limited to 260 characters (standard MAX_PATH)\n- Data size determined by EDI register at function entry (implicit parameter)\n- Total write size: (exceptionDataSize * 4) + 0x10 bytes (16-byte exception context header)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:ef7bb08bd488857c0f2a7a783c6d4a10",
