      "signature": "void DumpMemoryBlockWithHexEncoding(void * pCallbackContext, BinarySearchTreeNode * pRangeTreeHead)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Dumps memory block in hex format with ASCII and symbol information.\n\nAlgorithm\n1. Search binary search tree for memory range containing target address\n2. Initialize hex and symbol output buffers for formatting\n3. Log \"Annotated stack dump\" header message\n4. For each 16-byte memory block: validate readability with IsBadReadPtr()\n5. Format block as \"              0x%08X:\" address label\n6. For each DWORD: format as \" %02X%02X%02X%02X\" hex bytes\n7. Add padding spaces to align ASCII output column\n8. Convert bytes to ASCII or '.' for non-printable (< 0x20)\n9. Log formatted line with hex and ASCII dump\n10. For pointer DWORDs: search range tree and lookup symbol names\n11. Log pointer info with symbol and offset if pointer is valid\n12. Continue until 0x190 bytes dumped or memory read error\n\nParameters\npCallbackContext: Callback context pointer (void *)\npRangeTreeHead: Binary search tree root node (BinarySearchTreeNode *)\n\nReturns\nvoid",
