      "signature": "void DeallocateModuleListChain(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deallocates all nodes in a linked list of module information structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if list head pointer is NULL\n2. If empty, return without processing\n3. Load next pointer from offset 0x20C of current node\n4. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to deallocate current node\n5. Move to next node and repeat from step 3\n6. Continue until list is exhausted (next pointer is NULL)\n\nParameters:\npListHead (void*): Pointer to head of linked list of module information structures. Each node is 528 bytes (0x210) with the next pointer at offset 0x20C.\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value. All nodes in the list are deallocated.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL list head is handled safely with early return\n- List traversal uses offset 0x20C for next pointer\n- Each node is deallocated via DeallocateResourcePoolElement before processing next",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
      "method": "MNE",
