      "name": "IterateNetworkNodesAndInitialize",
      "signature": "void * IterateNetworkNodesAndInitialize(void * pBaseNodePtr)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Iterates through a linked list of network nodes and initializes connections for each.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Attempt primary node lookup via EnumerateProcessModules (EAX parameter implicit)\n2. If primary lookup returns NULL, call EnumerateProcessModulesWithTracking with baseNodePtr\n3. Store the result node pointer in ESI (will be either primary or fallback result)\n4. Enter loop if node pointer is non-NULL\n5. For each node:\n   - Load field at offset +0x104 (node base address)\n   - Load field at offset +0x204 (parameter 3 to InitializeNetworkConnection)\n   - Load field at offset +0x208 (parameter 4 to InitializeNetworkConnection)\n   - Call InitializeNetworkConnection with format string and source location\n6. Load next node pointer from offset +0x20c (offset 0x83 in DWORD units = 0x20c bytes)\n7. Loop if next node is non-NULL\n8. Return initial node pointer (puVar2/EDI)\n\nParameters:\n- baseNodePtr (ESP+0xc after PUSH): Used as fallback parameter if primary lookup fails\n\nReturns:\n- void *: Pointer to first network node from primary lookup, or fallback result if primary was NULL\n- NULL: If both lookup functions return NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If EnumerateProcessModules succeeds (non-NULL), baseNodePtr is never used\n- Node list may contain single node (next pointer is NULL)\n- Magic offset 0x20c (0x83 * 4) indicates node structure size or linked list field offset\n- Format string \"Base:%08lXh Size:%7lXh Name:%-15.15s Path:%s\" suggests module info structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
