      "name": "InitializeStackWalkContext",
      "signature": "int InitializeStackWalkContext(void * pContext, HANDLE hProcess, void * pStackWalkBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize stack walk context for debugging and diagnostic purposes.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check global initialization lock (g_dwStackWalkLock) to prevent concurrent initialization\\n2. Increment lock counter to prevent recursive initialization\\n3. Get current process handle via GetCurrentProcess() API\\n4. Call InitializeSymbolHandler() to check if stack walking is supported\\n5. Return 0 if stack walking not supported and decrement lock\\n6. Initialize large context structure (0x29 dwords) by clearing all bytes with STOSD.REP\\n7. Copy stack frame parameters from input buffer at offsets +0xb8 (frame type), +0xc4 (frame options), +0xb4 (frame flags)\\n8. Initialize frame walk context fields with required values\\n9. Loop through up to 16 stack frames with frame counter\\n10. For each frame, call g_pfnStackWalk() API with machine type 0x14c\\n11. On API failure, accumulate error counts using 64-bit arithmetic\\n12. On API success, extract frame data and validate via FindValidStackFrameWithRetry()\\n13. Call g_pfnSymGetSymFromAddr() for symbol lookup\\n14. Call g_pfnSymGetModuleInfo() for module information\\n15. Call StripSourcePathPrefix() to process paths\\n16. Call InitializeNetworkConnection() with diagnostic strings\\n17. Increment frame counter and continue if < 0x10\\n18. Call DecrementReferenceCountAndCleanup() for cleanup\\n19. Perform 64-bit division on frame statistics\\n20. Call InitializeNetworkConnection() with final statistics\\n21. Decrement global lock counter\\n22. Return 1 on success\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pContext - Debugging context for diagnostic output\\n  hProcess - Process handle for stack walk and symbol APIs\\n  pStackWalkBuffer - Buffer with frame fields at +0xb8, +0xc4, +0xb4\\n\\nReturns:\\n  1 - Success\\n  0 - Failed (lock held, unsupported, or error)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Global lock prevents re-entrancy\\n  - Uses 64-bit arithmetic for accumulation\\n  - Supports 16 stack frames maximum\\n  - Magic: 0x14c=i386 machine type, 0x29=41 dwords buffer",
