      "name": "InitializeStackWalkContext",
      "signature": "void InitializeStackWalkContext(void * pContextObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a stack walk context structure with current thread information and memory buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 728 bytes of local stack space for data structures and buffers\n2. Initialize stack walk buffer with 179 dwords cleared to zero via REP STOSD loop\n3. Set first element of buffer to magic constant 0x10007 (version/type identifier)\n4. Capture current instruction pointer using CALL/POP return address technique\n5. Preserve captured return address and base pointer values in local stack variables\n6. Obtain current thread handle via Windows GetCurrentThread() API call\n7. Pass initialized context object and buffer to ProcessStackWalkContext() for setup\n8. Return to caller after delegation to ProcessStackWalkContext\n\nParameters:\n  pContextObject - Void pointer to context structure that will be initialized with thread handle and buffer reference information. This pointer is passed through to ProcessStackWalkContext for actual initialization.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; initialization performed through parameter reference\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses CALL/POP instruction sequence to capture return address (CALL 0x6ff663eb; POP [EBP-0xc])\n  - Stack walk buffer size calculated as 179 dwords = 716 bytes (0x2c4 bytes)\n  - Magic constant 0x10007 in first buffer element indicates version or type information\n  - GetCurrentThread() always succeeds when called from valid thread context\n  - Function delegates actual context setup to ProcessStackWalkContext; performs only memory initialization\n  - All local variables stored on stack frame due to __fastcall convention\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name             Type     Description\n  ------  ----  --------------------   -------  ------------------------------------------\n  0x000   0x4   header                 uint     Version/type identifier constant (0x10007)\n  0x004   0x2bc reserved               uint[171] Reserved initialization area for buffer expansion",
