      "name": "InitializeObjectMemory",
      "signature": "void InitializeObjectMemory(void * pBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a 288-byte memory buffer with zeros and calls a resource pool initialization routine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ECX register to stack (callee-preserved)\n2. Copy buffer pointer from EDX (first fastcall parameter) to EDI\n3. Initialize EAX to 0 for zero-fill pattern\n4. Set ECX loop counter to 0x48 (72 iterations for 288 bytes total)\n5. Execute REP STOSD instruction to fill entire buffer with zeros\n6. Push initialization context address 0x6ff78cc4 onto stack\n7. Load buffer pointer from stack offset [ESP + 0xc] into ECX\n8. Store original buffer pointer EDX at [ESP + 0xc]\n9. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement(0x6ff78cc4) to initialize the zeroed buffer\n10. Restore EDI register from stack (callee-preserved)\n11. Restore ECX register from stack\n12. Return to caller via RET instruction\n\nParameters:\n- pBuffer (EDX/ECX via fastcall): Pointer to uninitialized memory buffer to be zeroed and initialized; must be at least 288 bytes in size; no validation performed on size or alignment\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer size is hardcoded to exactly 288 bytes (0x120 bytes or 0x48 dwords)\n- Uses __fastcall calling convention with EDX as implicit first parameter (standard for optimized Win32 functions)\n- Does not validate buffer pointer before use (assumes caller provides valid pointer)\n- Passes magic context address 0x6ff78cc4 to initialization routine as reference data\n- Called during early initialization sequence (referenced from Entry Point)\n\nStructure Layout:\n- Offset 0x00-0x11f: 288 bytes of initialized memory buffer\n- Total Size: 288 bytes (0x120)\n- All bytes zero-filled before initialization routine is called",
