      "name": "AllocatePoolSlot",
      "signature": "uint AllocatePoolSlot(void * pPoolManager)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Allocates a free slot from a pool and initializes it.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Validate that pool manager is initialized (check field at +0x108)\\n2. If pool not initialized, log error, cleanup resources, and exit\\n3. Load pool metadata: slot size (+0x104), current index (+0x10c), max slots (+0x100)\\n4. Calculate offset to current slot using index and slot size\\n5. Search forward through slots for first unoccupied slot (marked with value 0x0000)\\n6. If slot found and within bounds, clear it with memset-style loop (4-byte and 1-byte iterations)\\n7. Assign slot ID from counter (+0x118) and increment counter\\n8. When counter wraps to 0, set to 0x8000 to mark reinitialization\\n9. Update slot usage counters and max index tracker\\n10. Return combined value: slot ID (low 16 bits) | index (high 16 bits)\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pPoolManager (ECX): Pointer to pool manager structure containing:\\n    +0x100: Maximum number of slots (capacity)\\n    +0x104: Size of each slot in bytes (stride)\\n    +0x108: Initialization flag (non-zero if initialized)\\n    +0x10c: Current slot index (write position)\\n    +0x110: Maximum index reached (tracking)\\n    +0x114: Number of allocated slots (count)\\n    +0x118: Next slot ID counter (wraps at 0x8000)\\n    +0x11c: Base pointer to slot array\\n\\nReturns:\\n  EAX: Combined return value with format:\\n    Bits 0-15: Assigned slot ID\\n    Bits 16-31: Slot index\\n    0xFFFFFFFF: Returned when no free slot found or pool not initialized\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Magic value 0x8000: Used to reset slot ID counter to avoid ID 0x0000\\n  - Array search terminates early if reaching max slots without finding free slot\\n  - Memset clearing uses 4-byte word writes followed by 1-byte cleanup for remainder\\n  - Function uses __fastcall: first parameter in ECX register",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:4e2690e85ab304c00638f2a19c048f8a",
