      "name": "PerformNetworkInitValidation",
      "signature": "void PerformNetworkInitValidation(void * pNetworkContext, int nValidationMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates network initialization state and handles validation failures\nPerforms critical network validation before game continues. If validation fails,\ninitiates emergency shutdown to terminate the application safely.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls network validation function with provided context and mode parameters\n2. Tests validation result (0 = failed, non-zero = success)\n3. On validation success: Returns immediately to caller\n4. On validation failure:\n   a. Saves return address for error context tracking\n   b. Cleans up Winsock resources via WSACleanup()\n   c. Logs validation failure with error code 0xfd\n   d. Executes resource cleanup sequence\n   e. Terminates process with exit code -1\n\nParameters:\n- pNetworkContext (ECX): Pointer to network context or state structure passed to validation\n- nValidationMode (EDX): Mode or flags parameter controlling validation behavior\n\nReturns:\n- void: Either returns normally on successful validation or terminates via _exit() on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error code 0xfd (253 decimal) indicates unrecoverable network validation failure\n- WSACleanup() is called before exit to properly shut down Winsock layer\n- Process termination with exit code -1 signals critical initialization failure to OS",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:9d7a192a9dc4655742a7159ac25b11c4",
