      "name": "RemoveSocketQueueItem",
      "signature": "void RemoveSocketQueueItem(void * pSocketQueue, uint itemIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "RemoveSocketQueueItem - Removes an item from a socket queue and compacts queue indices\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Retrieve socket queue item at specified index by calling GetSocketQueueItem (Ordinal_10067)\\n2. If retrieval fails (returns NULL), call GetReturnAddress and trigger error cleanup with WSACleanup and LogErrorAndShutdown\\n3. Mark the retrieved item as inactive by setting its value to 0 (word-sized flag at queue item address)\\n4. Extract queue index from upper 16 bits of itemIndex parameter using SAR EDI, 0x10\\n5. Compare extracted index with minimum queue index (offset +0x10c) and update if new index is smaller\\n6. Check if extracted index equals target index (offset +0x110):\\n   a. If equal, enter backward search loop to compact queue indices\\n   b. Decrement item pointer by stride (offset +0x104 bytes per item)\\n   c. Decrement target index counter (offset +0x110)\\n   d. Continue loop while: target index >= 0 AND current item is inactive (value at item pointer == 0)\\n   e. Exit loop when target index becomes negative or item is active (non-zero)\\n7. Decrement total active queue items counter (offset +0x114)\\n8. Return to caller\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pSocketQueue (ECX, __fastcall): Pointer to socket queue structure\\n  - Offset +0x104: stride (bytes per item in queue, typically 12-16 bytes)\\n  - Offset +0x10c: minimum active queue index (optimization for traversal)\\n  - Offset +0x110: target queue index (search boundary during compaction)\\n  - Offset +0x114: active item counter (total items in use)\\n  - Offset +0x11c: base pointer to queue item array\\n- itemIndex (EDX, __fastcall): Packed 32-bit value with queue index in upper 16 bits (index in bits 16-31)\\n\\nReturns:\\n- None (void function)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- If GetSocketQueueItem returns NULL, function triggers error handling and exits with LogErrorAndShutdown\\n- Queue compaction only occurs when removed index equals target index, indicating front-of-queue removal\\n- Loop skips multiple consecutive inactive items during compaction, advancing backward until first active item found\\n- Function modifies queue control fields directly via memory pointers, no return value",
