      "name": "GetCpuTimestampCounter",
      "signature": "ulonglong GetCpuTimestampCounter(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Reads and returns the CPU's Time Stamp Counter (TSC) register.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 8 bytes on stack for TSC result storage\n2. Execute RDTSC instruction to read CPU timestamp counter into EDX:EAX\n3. Store EAX (low 32 bits of TSC) into [ESP+0]\n4. Store EDX (high 32 bits of TSC) into [ESP+4]\n5. Load low 32 bits from [ESP+0] into EAX\n6. Load high 32 bits from [ESP+4] into EDX\n7. Deallocate 8 bytes of stack space\n8. Return with 64-bit TSC value in EDX:EAX pair\n\nParameters:\n  None - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  ulonglong - 64-bit CPU timestamp counter value in EDX:EAX register pair\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  RDTSC is only available on Pentium and later processors. TSC increments at processor clock frequency. Used by MeasureCpuFrequencyInMHz to measure CPU frequency via cycle delta timing.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e6cc50b84844e2b386c10b8355dc08bc",
