      "name": "GetCpuBrandString",
      "signature": "void GetCpuBrandString(uint dwVendorId, uint dwSignature, char * lpszBrandBuffer, uint dwStepping, uint dwFamily)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "GetCpuBrandString - Retrieves and copies CPU brand string to output buffer based on processor identification\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer with default \"Unknown\" brand string (10 bytes)\n2. Decrement stepping parameter to determine vendor path (stepping-1: 0=Intel/Cyrix, 1=AMD, 2=Other)\n3. Based on stepping value, branch to appropriate CPU vendor/family handler:\n   a. If stepping==1 (Intel/Cyrix): Check signature (EDX) values 1,2,3,4,8,14 for specific models\n   b. If stepping==2 (AMD): Check family values 4,5,6 for 486/K5/K6 processor lines\n   c. If stepping==3: Check EBX variant and family for alternative processor paths\n4. Within each vendor/family branch, match CPU model from EAX against known processor variants\n5. For each matching variant, copy brand string from global data to output buffer at pBrandBuffer\n6. Return void after writing brand string to buffer (all paths end with RET 0xC)\n\nParameters:\nvendorId (ECX, __fastcall unused): Vendor identifier (not used in function)\nsignature (EDX, __fastcall): CPU model/signature bits extracted from CPUID EAX register\npBrandBuffer (ESP+0x8): Pointer to output char buffer (minimum 25 bytes recommended)\nstepping (ESP+0xC): CPU stepping identifier (1=Intel/Cyrix standard, 2=AMD standard, 3=Other)\nfamily (ESP+0x10): CPU family identifier (4=486-era, 5=Pentium/K5, 6=Pentium Pro/K6, 0xF=P4/newer)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - writes null-terminated brand string to pBrandBuffer buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Default brand \"Unknown\" (9 bytes + null) initialized at function entry\n- Model variants with 24+ byte strings use loop-based memory copy (REP MOVSD)\n- Stepping==1 with EDX==14: Outputs 5-byte brand string (4 bytes + 1 byte)\n- Stepping==2, AMD Family==6, Model==6: Uses 6-dword loop for \"Athlon MP/XP/Mobile\"\n- Stepping==1, EBX==0, Family==6, Model>7: Uses 5-dword loop for \"Pentium III (no brand)\"\n- Stepping==1, EBX==0, Family==15: Handles extended family Pentium 4 variants (6 dwords + 1 byte)\n- Unrecognized stepping/family/model combinations leave default \"Unknown\" in buffer\n- All code paths check boundaries: CMP comparisons and conditional jumps to error_exit_return_default\n\nStructure Layout:\nCPU Brand String Buffer (variable length, null-terminated):\nOffset  Size  Field      Type       Description\n0       1+    szBrand    char[]     Null-terminated brand string (e.g., \"Celeron\", \"Pentium III\", \"Athlon\")",
