      "name": "ValidateGameStateRequirements",
      "signature": "int ValidateGameStateRequirements(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates that game state meets requirements for current mode/difficulty/class\n\nSummary:\nChecks whether the current game state configuration (packed difficulty, subtype,\nand class values) satisfies the validation requirements for the active game mode.\nUsed to determine if players can enter a game or if their character meets the\nrequirements for the selected game type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check minimum version requirement (must be >= 5)\n2. Retrieve current game mode from system state (0=SP, 1=BNet, 2=PvP, 3=Custom)\n3. Fetch packed game state value containing mode/difficulty/class bit fields\n4. Extract subtype from bits [13:12], difficulty from [11:8], class from [7:4]\n5. Validate based on mode:\n   - Mode 1 (BNet): Accept subtype 0 + difficulty 5, OR subtype 0 + difficulty 6 + class < 3, OR subtype 1 + difficulty 5\n   - Mode 2 (PvP): Accept difficulty 4, OR difficulty 5 with class <= 8\n   - Mode 3 (Custom): Accept all configurations\n6. Return success (1) if valid, failure (0) if validation fails\n\nParameters:\nNone. Function reads global game state via calls to GetCpuVendorId() and GetCpuVersionInfo().\n\nReturns:\nINT: 1 if game state meets requirements, 0 if validation fails\n\nPacked Game State Structure:\nBits [13:12] = subtype (0-3: difficulty tier, special modes)\nBits [11:8] = difficulty (0-6: normal/nightmare/hell levels, PvP tier)\nBits [7:4] = class or level (0-15: player class ID or level range)\nBits [3:0] = additional mode flags (reserved/unused in validation)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Version check: Returns TRUE (success) if version < 5 to prevent old clients\n- Mode 1 subtype 0: Accepts difficulty 5 unconditionally OR difficulty 6 with class < 3\n- Mode 1 subtype 1: Accepts difficulty 5 with any class value (all results valid)\n- Mode 2: Difficulty 4 always passes; difficulty 5 requires class <= 8",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:54764ec3410ff9e75c5a43631299e873",
