      "name": "MeasureCpuFrequencyInMHz",
      "signature": "ulonglong MeasureCpuFrequencyInMHz(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Measures CPU frequency in MHz using high-resolution performance counters\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current thread priority, restore if valid (not 0x7FFFFFFF)\n2. Capture baseline GetTickCount and QueryPerformanceCounter readings\n3. Call GetCpuTimestampCounter for baseline CPU cycle count\n4. Sleep in calibration loop until 10ms+ elapsed based on GetTickCount\n5. Save thread priority again and restore if valid\n6. Capture end-of-calibration QueryPerformanceCounter and GetCpuTimestampCounter\n7. Query performance counter frequency via QueryPerformanceFrequency\n8. Calculate CPU cycle delta: endCycles - startCycles\n9. Multiply cycle delta by perf counter frequency using __allmul (64-bit multiply)\n10. Divide result by perf counter tick delta using __alldiv (64-bit divide)\n11. Divide by 1,000,000 to convert from Hz to MHz using __alldiv\n12. Return final CPU frequency in MHz as 64-bit unsigned integer\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function measures hardware/OS performance directly\n\nReturns:\nulonglong - CPU frequency in MHz as 64-bit unsigned value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThread priority value 0x7FFFFFFF (INVALID_THREAD_PRIORITY) indicates restoration should be skipped\nMinimum 10ms calibration window ensures stable baseline measurement\nUses high-resolution QueryPerformanceCounter instead of millisecond-precision GetTickCount for actual measurement\nGetCpuTimestampCounter accesses x86 RDTSC instruction for direct CPU cycle counting\n\nStructure Layout:\nLARGE_INTEGER (perf counter types):\n  Offset 0x0 (4 bytes): LowPart - Low 32 bits\n  Offset 0x4 (4 bytes): HighPart - High 32 bits",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
