      "name": "IsStateField0x86cActiveOrBusy",
      "signature": "int IsStateField0x86cActiveOrBusy(void * pObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Checks if an object's state field (offset 0x86c) is in active or busy state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the object pointer from stack parameter\n2. Verify pointer is not NULL\n3. Load the state value from object offset +0x86c\n4. Check if state equals 1 (active) or 2 (busy)\n5. Return 1 (true) if state matches, 0 (false) otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- pObject: Pointer to object structure to check\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (true) if state field at offset 0x86c is 1 or 2\n- 0 (false) if pointer is NULL or state is not 1 or 2\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer check: Returns false for NULL pointers\n- State values: Specifically checks for values 1 and 2",
