      "name": "GetOrSetArrayElement",
      "signature": "uint GetOrSetArrayElement(void * pBaseAddress, uint arrayIndex, uint newValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Reads and optionally updates a dword element in an array at fixed offset 0xba8.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load base address pointer from parameter pBaseAddress\n2. Load array index from parameter arrayIndex\n3. Load array element value: [pBaseAddress + 0xba8 + (arrayIndex * 4)]\n4. Save current element value for return\n5. Load new value parameter newValue from stack\n6. Test if newValue is non-zero (zero indicates read-only mode)\n7. If newValue is non-zero, write newValue to array element at same offset\n8. Restore ESI register (saved earlier for callee-save)\n9. Return previous element value in EAX with stack cleanup\n\nParameters:\npBaseAddress (void *) - Base pointer to data structure containing the array\narrayIndex (uint) - Zero-based index into the dword array (offset = index * 4)\nnewValue (uint) - New value to write; if zero, performs read-only operation\n\nReturns:\nuint - The value that was in the array element before any update\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero sentinel pattern: newValue of 0 disables the write, allowing read-only access\n- Fixed offset 0xba8: Array always located at this offset from structure base\n- Element size: Always 4 bytes per element (dword)\n- Atomic semantics: Caller can check previous value after update\n- Calling convention: __stdcall with 0xc bytes cleaned up by callee\n\nStructure Layout:\nArray base address = pBaseAddress + 0xba8\nElement access formula: (pBaseAddress + 0xba8)[arrayIndex]\nEach element = 4 bytes (dword)\n\nCallers:\nReferenced at 0x6ff7dc00 and Entry Point\nCommon usage: Array-backed data structures like resource pools, state tables, or flags",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f02490aff6864b17a710d4cc7e56fe4b",
