      "name": "DestroyAllLinkedListNodes",
      "signature": "void DestroyAllLinkedListNodes(void * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Destroys all linked list nodes across multiple slots and resets resource counter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate critical section pointer at offset +0x894 from resource manager object\n2. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity to initialize critical section\n3. Enter critical section lock for thread-safe cleanup\n4. Load slot count from offset +0x8b0\n5. If slot count > 0, iterate through each slot (0 to count-1):\n   a. Load array base pointer from offset +0x8ac\n   b. Get first node pointer from array[slotIndex]\n   c. If node pointer is non-null, enter inner node destruction loop:\n      - Load next node pointer from current node + offset 0xc (next pointer field)\n      - Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to destroy current node\n      - Advance to next node and repeat until null\n   d. Clear array[slotIndex] to NULL after processing all nodes\n   e. Increment slot index and continue with next slot\n6. Reset resource counter at offset +0x890 to zero\n7. Leave critical section lock\n8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pResourceManager (EDI): Pointer to resource manager object containing:\n  - Offset +0x8ac: Base address of linked list head pointer array\n  - Offset +0x8b0: Number of linked list slots to process\n  - Offset +0x890: Resource counter to reset\n  - Offset +0x894: Critical section synchronization object\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __thiscall convention with implicit this pointer in EDI register\n- Processes linked list in forward order through array slots\n- Node structure layout: offset +0xc contains next pointer (4 bytes)\n- Thread-safe: Acquires critical section before any modifications\n- Resource counter reset happens after all nodes destroyed\n- Empty slot lists are properly handled (null pointer check at 0x6ff5d74b)\n\nData Structure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field              Type      Description\n------  ----  -----              ----      -----------\n+0x8ac  4     pLinkedListArray   void**    Base address of linked list head pointers\n+0x8b0  4     dwSlotCount        uint      Number of slots in array\n+0x890  4     dwResourceCount    uint      Counter to reset after cleanup\n+0x894  4     hCriticalSection   HANDLE    Critical section for synchronization",
