      "name": "FindHashTableEntry",
      "signature": "uint * FindHashTableEntry(void * pHashTableManager, uint dwSearchKey, void * pOutCriticalSection)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Searches a hash table for an entry matching a given key value. Thread-safe lookup using critical sections.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract hash slot index by masking searchKey with table bitmask (offset +0xc)\n2. Calculate slot's critical section offset as (index * 0x18 bytes)\n3. Get critical section pointer at (base + 0x1c + offset)\n4. Validate critical section structure integrity using ValidateDataStructureIntegrity\n5. Enter critical section to acquire exclusive lock on the hash slot\n6. Retrieve first node pointer from hash slot array (offset +0x14 + index*4)\n7. Loop: Compare node value (at offset +0) with searchKey, advance via next pointer (+4)\n8. On match: Store critical section pointer to output parameter and return node pointer\n9. On NULL/no-match: Release critical section lock and return NULL\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTableManager: Hash table control structure with offsets +0xc (bitmask), +0x14 (list array), +0x1c (crit section array)\n- dwSearchKey: Value to search for in hash table entries (matched against node value at +0)\n- pOutCriticalSection: Output parameter to receive critical section pointer on successful match\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to matched hash table node if entry found\n- NULL pointer if no matching entry exists or list is empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Hash slots indexed via (key & bitmask), supporting variable-size tables (16/32/64 slots)\n- Critical sections are 0x18 bytes each (matches _RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION)\n- Hash table nodes minimum 8 bytes: 4 bytes value + 4 bytes next pointer\n- Caller responsible for releasing critical section via LeaveCriticalSection\n- No modification allowed to critical section pointer after return",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e08518d32f3ae7c7350b06e547a59811",
