      "name": "CheckElementTimestampValid",
      "signature": "bool CheckElementTimestampValid(uint * pElementId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates whether an element's timestamp meets or exceeds the global threshold.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load timestamp threshold from context (ESI + 0x884)\n2. Return false if threshold is negative (invalid state)\n3. Hash the element ID using modulo operation with divisor at ESI + 0x10\n4. Enter critical section to safely access hash table\n5. Search hash bucket chain for matching element ID\n6. If element not found, leave critical section and return false\n7. If element found, extract timestamp from element+4 offset\n8. Leave critical section and compare timestamp >= threshold\n9. Return true if timestamp valid, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\npElementId (uint *): Pointer to element ID to validate\n\nReturns:\nbool: true if element exists and timestamp >= threshold, false otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\nReturns false immediately if threshold is negative\nReturns false if element not found in hash table\nUses critical section (EnterCriticalSection) to prevent race conditions",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:382a3397b2e72163a246122817407b73",
