      "name": "RemoveEntryFromHashTables",
      "signature": "void RemoveEntryFromHashTables(uint entryId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Removes an entry from two independent hash tables (primary and secondary).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire primary hash table critical section\n2. Search first hash table for entry by ID, tracking previous node\n3. If found, acquire secondary hash table critical section\n4. Decrement global entry count\n5. Unlink entry from first hash table (update head or previous node pointer)\n6. Search second hash table for the same entry\n7. Unlink entry from second hash table\n8. Release both critical sections\n\nParameters:\n  entryId (ESP+0x1C): Unsigned 32-bit unique identifier for the entry to remove\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Entry may be the head of hash chain (requires direct head pointer update)\n  - Entry count is stored at global context offset +0x880\n  - Hash tables use separate critical sections at offsets +0xc and +0x854\n  - Uses AND with mask at offset +0xc to calculate hash bucket index\n  - Two separate hash tables with different chain link offsets (+0x4 vs +0x1c)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Context Structure (passed in EAX):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name            | Type      | Description\n  0x0c   | 4    | dwHashMask            | uint      | Hash bucket mask\n  0x14   | 4    | pFirstHashTable       | pointer   | Array of hash chain heads\n  0x1c   | 4    | pCriticalSections     | pointer   | Array of critical section structures\n  0x20   | 4    | pSecondHashTable      | pointer   | Secondary hash table\n  0x854  | 8    | countCriticalSection  | CRITICAL  | Critical section for count access\n  0x880  | 4    | dwEntryCount          | uint      | Total number of entries",
