      "name": "CloseSocketEntryAndCleanup",
      "signature": "void CloseSocketEntryAndCleanup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Closes a socket entry and cleans up associated resources from the hash table.\n\nThis function closes the socket handle contained in a hash table entry and ensures\nproper cleanup when the reference count reaches zero. It is called after transmission\nfailures or when a connection needs to be forcibly terminated.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FindHashTableEntry to retrieve hash entry pointer for current socket key\n2. Check if entry exists (pointer non-NULL check)\n3. Load closed flag field at entry+0xc to check if already marked as closed\n4. If already closed (non-zero), skip closure and branch to cleanup_exit\n5. Load socket handle at entry+0x10 (valid handles are non-negative, -1 is invalid)\n6. Set closed flag at entry+0xc to 1 to prevent duplicate closes\n7. Call CloseSocketImportThunk(handle) to close socket and store result in EDI\n8. Mark socket field as invalid: entry+0x10 = 0xFFFFFFFF\n9. If closesocket returned error (EDI != 0), get error code via WSAGetLastError()\n10. If error, call InitializeNetworkConnection with error string and error code\n11. Call InterlockedDecrement on refcount at entry+0x8 to decrement reference\n12. If refcount becomes zero after decrement (result == 0):\n    a. Load optional cleanup callback at context+0xbc8\n    b. If callback exists, invoke with parameters (szSourceFilePath, 0x374)\n    c. Get entry key from entry+0x0 and call RemoveEntryFromHashTables\n    d. Clean pending socket operations via CleanupPendingSocketOperations()\n13. If closesocket returned -1 (major error), get final error code via WSAGetLastError()\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ESI: Context object pointer (pSocketContext) containing callback at offset 0xbc8 and cleanup data\nIMPLICIT EAX: Socket entry key for hash table lookup (socketKey)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Entry may already be closed (closed flag != 0) - prevents duplicate closes\n- Socket handle -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) indicates invalid/already closed socket\n- Zero refcount triggers hash table removal and full cleanup\n- Callback function may be NULL - checked before invocation at context+0xbc8\n- closesocket error (-1) is distinct from successful close (0)\n- Error logging uses magic value 0x374 as second parameter to callback\n\nStructure Layout:\nHash Table Entry (pSocketEntry) structure offsets:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type        Description\n  0x0     4     socketKey            uint        Hash key for lookup\n  0x8     4     refCount             LONG        Reference count (interlocked)\n  0xc     4     closedFlag           uint        Non-zero if already closed\n  0x10    4     socketHandle         SOCKET      Socket handle (-1 if invalid)\n  \nContext Structure (pSocketContext) offsets:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type        Description\n  0xbc8   4     cleanupCallback      void*       Optional cleanup callback function pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:147162bd175aeb3e4e42b5fa631a66c0",
