      "name": "ClearAllResourcePoolElements",
      "signature": "int ClearAllResourcePoolElements(void * pResourceManager)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Clears all resource elements from a resource manager's pool arrays.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load resource count from offset +0x87c in pResourceManager\n2. Return immediately if count <= 0 (no resources to clear)\n3. For each resource slot (0 to count-1):\n   a. Get critical section address at offset +0x854\n   b. Validate critical section integrity using ValidateDataStructureIntegrity\n   c. Enter critical section for thread-safe access\n   d. Load head element pointer from slot array (offset +0x870 + slotIndex*4)\n   e. Zero both element array entry (offset +0x870) and secondary array entry (offset +0x874)\n   f. Leave critical section\n   g. If head element exists (not NULL):\n      - Loop through linked list of elements starting from head\n      - For each element: load next element pointer from offset +0x5bc\n      - Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to deallocate current element\n      - Continue until no more elements\n4. Return 1 (success status)\n\nParameters:\n  pResourceManager (void *): Pointer to resource manager structure containing:\n    Offset +0x854: CRITICAL_SECTION for synchronization\n    Offset +0x870: Array of element list head pointers (one per slot)\n    Offset +0x874: Array of secondary pointers (one per slot)\n    Offset +0x87c: Count of resource slots\n\nReturns:\n  int: Returns 1 on success (function always succeeds if pResourceManager is valid)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles empty pools gracefully (count <= 0)\n  - Uses critical sections to ensure thread-safe clearing\n  - Deallocates entire linked lists within each slot\n  - No error return value documented (always returns 1)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:aab7e8e30f79729b516eae9a74eba7fb",
