      "name": "SendDataToSocket",
      "signature": "uint SendDataToSocket(void * pConnectionState, void * pSocket)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Sends data to a socket using either wrapped socket handler or direct socket API.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate connection info pointer (EAX) is non-null\n2. Check connection state flag at offset +0xc (0 = normal, non-zero = error state)\n3. If connection state is error, return 0 (failure)\n4. Check if wrapped socket handler is available (pConnectionState check)\n5. If wrapped handler exists, call SendSocketData() with connection, buffer, and size\n6. Otherwise, use raw socket send() API with socket from offset +0x10\n7. For raw send, check if result != -1 (SOCKET_ERROR)\n8. If send succeeded, return 1; if failed or no socket, return 0\n9. Call WSAGetLastError() on send failure (result discarded)\n\nParameters:\n  pConnectionState: Pointer to socket/connection wrapper (may be NULL)\n  pSocket: Raw socket descriptor or connection handle\n  pBuffer: Pointer to data buffer to send\n  bufferSize: Size of data in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  1: Data successfully sent\n  0: Send failed or invalid connection state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pConnectionInfo is NULL on entry, returns 0 (invalid state)\n  - If connection state flag (+0xc) is non-zero, treats as error condition\n  - Fallback from wrapped socket to raw send() if wrapper unavailable\n  - WSAGetLastError() called but result not stored (for error logging)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n  +0x00   4     unknown           uint    (unknown)\n  +0x04   4     unknown           uint    (unknown)\n  +0x08   4     unknown           uint    (unknown)\n  +0x0c   4     connectionState   uint    0=normal, non-zero=error\n  +0x10   4     rawSocket         SOCKET  Direct socket handle",
