      "name": "GetHashTableEntryValue",
      "signature": "uint GetHashTableEntryValue(void * pHashTable, uint dwSearchKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves the value of a hash table entry for a given search key.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate searchKey parameter (must be non-NULL)\n2. Call FindHashTableEntry to locate the hash table entry node\n3. If entry not found, return NULL (zero)\n4. If entry found, extract and return value from offset +0x20 in the entry structure\n\nParameters:\npHashTable - Pointer to hash table manager structure containing bucket array and metadata\ndwSearchKey - Key to search for in hash table\n\nReturns:\nuint - The value stored at offset +0x20 of the matching entry node, or 0 if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if searchKey is NULL (early return path)\n- Returns 0 if FindHashTableEntry fails to locate a matching entry\n- The value extraction loads a DWORD from offset +0x20 in the entry node\n\nNotes:\nThis is a simple wrapper around FindHashTableEntry that extracts a specific field\nfrom the found entry node. The hash table is thread-safe via critical sections\nmanaged by FindHashTableEntry.",
