      "name": "GetHashTableEntryNetworkValue",
      "signature": "u_short GetHashTableEntryNetworkValue(void * pHashTableManager, uint searchKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves a network-byte-order value from a hash table entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FindHashTableEntry with hash table manager and search key\n2. If entry not found, return 0\n3. Extract value from hash entry\n4. Convert value from network byte order to host byte order using ntohs\n5. Leave critical section to release lock\n6. Return converted value\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTableManager: Pointer to hash table structure containing entries\n- searchKey: Key to search for in the hash table\n\nReturns:\n- unsigned short: Network value converted to host byte order\n- Returns 0 if entry not found\n\nNotes:\n- Thread-safe: Uses critical sections to protect hash table access\n- Network byte order conversion: Uses ntohs for proper endianness handling",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:03fc45ba940c3f06774ead3e634dd7db",
