      "name": "RemoveHashTableEntry",
      "signature": "void RemoveHashTableEntry(uint entryId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Removes a hash table entry by ID and logs hacklist state throttled.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if hash table processing is enabled (flag at pContextBlock+0xbd0)\n2. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity with critical section address (pre-lock sync)\n3. Enter critical section to lock hash table access\n4. Calculate hash bucket index: entryId % hash_table_size (at pContextBlock+0x8b0)\n5. Load head pointer from hash bucket array (base at pContextBlock+0x8ac)\n6. Iterate through linked list of hash entries:\n   - Load current entry from head or next.next (offset +0xc)\n   - Compare current entry ID (at offset +0x0) with target entryId\n   - If match found:\n     * If entry is head (pPrevNode == NULL):\n       - Load hash bucket address and its head pointer\n       - Update bucket head to point to next entry\n     * Else (entry in middle or end of list):\n       - Update previous node's next pointer (offset +0xc) to skip current\n     * Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to deallocate matched entry\n     * Decrement entry count at pContextBlock+0x890\n7. Leave critical section to unlock hash table access\n8. Get current tick count via GetTickCount()\n9. Check elapsed time: compare current tick with g_dwLastThrottleTimestamp\n10. If 2000+ milliseconds elapsed:\n    - Call InitializeNetworkConnection with szHackModuleTag and szHacklistFormatString\n    - Update g_dwLastThrottleTimestamp with current tick count\n11. Return (RET 0x4 - callee cleanup of 4-byte parameter)\n\nParameters:\nentryId (on stack at ESP+0x14): 32-bit unsigned entry ID to remove. Matched\nagainst ID field at offset +0x0 in each hash entry. Used to calculate hash\nbucket index via modulo with hash table size.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value. Entry is removed from hash table as side effect.\n\nStructure Layout:\nHashEntry structure (inferred from access patterns):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type     | Description\n0x0    | 4    | dwEntryId       | DWORD    | Entry ID for matching\n0x4    | 4    | pData           | PVOID    | Pointer to entry data\n0x8    | 4    | reserved        | DWORD    | Reserved/unused field\n0xc    | 4    | pNext           | PVOID    | Pointer to next entry in list\nTotal: 16 bytes per entry\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If enabled flag at pContextBlock+0xbd0 is zero, function returns immediately\n- Empty hash bucket (NULL head pointer) skips to critical section exit\n- Only processes single matching entry (breaks after match)\n- Entry count decremented after removal (tracks active entries)\n- Logging throttled to 2000ms minimum interval (prevents log spam)\n- Hash table size must be non-zero (used in modulo calculation)\n- Critical section protects concurrent access during modification\n- Calling context provides implicit pContextBlock pointer in EAX register",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:3a43acad3c00013f73ec709f10a37ffa",
