      "name": "InsertOrUpdateTrackedAddressInHashTable",
      "signature": "void InsertOrUpdateTrackedAddressInHashTable(uint ipAddress, char * pSourceFile, uint lineNumber)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Inserts a new tracked IP address into a hash table or updates timestamp if already exists.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate IP address is initialized by checking state flag at [ESI + 0xBD0]\n2. Call ValidatePermissionMask to check if IP is valid (returns EAX != 0 on error)\n3. If validation callback registered at [ESI + 0xBB8], invoke it with IP, file, and line parameters\n4. Acquire hash table lock using EnterCriticalSection on lock at [ESI + 0x894]\n5. Calculate bucket index using modulo division: EBP / [ESI + 0x8B0] remainder\n6. Load bucket array from [ESI + 0x8AC] and traverse linked list at bucket head\n7. Search for existing entry with matching IP by comparing [EAX] to EBP\n8. If found at entry_exists label: Update timeout field at offset +0x8 to 0x78 (120 seconds) and release lock\n9. If not found: Check free list at [ESI + 0x88C] for available entry to reuse\n10. If free entry available: Pop from free list and link it in\n11. If no free entry: Allocate new entry via AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n12. Initialize new/reused entry: Set IP at offset +0x0, timeout at +0x4 (0x78), flags at +0x8 (0x0)\n13. Link entry into bucket by updating next pointer at +0xC and bucket head at bucket address\n14. Increment entry counter at [ESI + 0x890]\n15. Release hash table lock via LeaveCriticalSection\n16. Call PerformThrottledActionOnTimer with entry count to throttle further operations\n\nParameters:\nipAddress (EBP): 32-bit IP address value to track\npSourceFile (ESP+0xC after PUSH): Pointer to source file path string (filename of caller)\nlineNumber (ESP+0x10 after PUSH): Source code line number where tracking was initiated\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Function modifies hash table state directly.\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x78 (120 decimal): Timeout value in seconds for tracked address entries\n- 0x4A6: Allocation size constant for new entries\n- 0x492: Constant parameter passed to EnterCriticalSection (likely timeout/flags)\nOffset Constants (relative to server context at ESI):\n- 0xBD0: Initialization state flag\n- 0xBB8: Callback function pointer\n- 0x894: Hash table lock object\n- 0x8B0: Bucket count for modulo calculation\n- 0x8AC: Pointer to bucket array\n- 0x88C: Free list head pointer\n- 0x890: Entry count field\nEntry Layout (allocated memory structure):\n- Offset 0x0: IP address (DWORD)\n- Offset 0x4: Timeout counter (DWORD)\n- Offset 0x8: Flags field (DWORD)\n- Offset 0xC: Next pointer (DWORD) - links to next entry in bucket",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:8b2439767f502e8ef29483e438f0839d",
