      "name": "ProcessConnectionTimeouts",
      "signature": "void ProcessConnectionTimeouts(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Periodically processes connection timeout counters across all active client connection slots.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if timeout system initialized (offset 0x888 == -1); initialize with current tick if needed\n2. Query current system tick count (GetTickCount)\n3. Calculate elapsed milliseconds since last check (current_tick - reference_tick)\n4. If elapsed < 1000ms (0x3e8), exit early (not yet time to process)\n5. Convert elapsed milliseconds to seconds via division (multiply by 0x10624dd3, then shift right 6)\n6. Enter critical section at offset 0x894 to protect slot array access\n7. For each slot (0 to count at 0x8b0):\n   a. Get first node in slot's linked list from array at 0x8ac\n   b. For each node in linked list (offset 0xc = next node):\n      - Check first timeout field (offset +8); if non-zero, decrement by elapsed_seconds\n      - When first timeout expires (becomes 0):\n        - Set second timeout to min(0x78 - elapsed_seconds, 0)\n        - Add elapsed_seconds to second timeout\n      - Check second timeout field (offset +4); if non-zero, decrement by elapsed_seconds\n      - When second timeout expires (becomes 0):\n        - Remove node from active list by unlinking\n        - Add node to expired list at 0x88c\n        - Decrement active count at 0x890\n        - Set itemsExpired flag to true\n      - Move to next node in list (offset 0xc)\n8. Leave critical section\n9. If any items expired and last report > 2000ms ago:\n   - Call InitializeNetworkConnection to log expired connections\n   - Update last report timestamp\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT pServerBaseAddr (EAX): Base address of server context structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x888: Last timeout check timestamp (or -1 if uninitialized)\n  - Offset 0x894: Critical section for slot array synchronization\n  - Offset 0x88c: Head of expired connections linked list\n  - Offset 0x890: Count of active connections\n  - Offset 0x8ac: Pointer to array of slot list heads\n  - Offset 0x8b0: Number of slots in array\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First execution initializes reference timestamp to current tick\n- Elapsed time checked as 32-bit unsigned to handle tick count wrapping\n- 1000ms threshold prevents frequent wakeups for this processing\n- Timeout computation uses 2-stage countdown: primary timeout (offset +8) followed by secondary (offset +4)\n- Secondary timeout has minimum 0x78 (120) unit value when set from primary expiry\n- Expired nodes are unlinked from active list and moved to dead list for later cleanup\n- Logging only occurs every 2000ms minimum to avoid spam in high-load scenarios\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type      Description\n0x888   4     lastCheckTimestamp      DWORD     System tick from last execution\n0x894   ~44   criticalSection         CRITICAL_SECTION  Synchronizes slot/list access\n0x8ac   4     slotArrayPointer        void*     Array of linked list heads\n0x8b0   4     slotCount               uint      Number of slots to process\n0x88c   4     expiredListHead         void*     Head of expired connections\n0x890   4     activeConnectionCount   int       Current active connection count",
