      "name": "BroadcastSocketData",
      "signature": "int BroadcastSocketData(int * pResourceManager, byte * pDataBuffer, uint dataSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Broadcasts socket data to all active connections in specified resource manager groups.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify resource manager is valid and contains at least one connection group\n2. Initialize group iteration index and offset (0 to groupCount-1, offset += 0x18 per iteration)\n3. For each connection group:\n   a. Load critical section base pointer from resource manager (+0x1c)\n   b. Add group-specific offset to get group's critical section address\n   c. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity to prepare critical section\n   d. Enter critical section via EnterCriticalSection for thread-safe access\n   e. Load base pointer to connection group array from resource manager (+0x14)\n   f. Load first connection node from array at [arrayBase + groupIndex*4]\n   g. Iterate through connection node linked list:\n      - Load flags from node offset +0xc\n      - Skip node if flags != 0 (uses SendSocketData wrapper instead)\n      - If flags == 0 and resource manager flag (+0x0) == 0: use direct socket send()\n      - If resource manager flag != 0: call SendSocketData wrapper function\n      - Check send result: if -1 (error), call WSAGetLastError for error code\n      - Load next node from current node offset +0x4\n      - Continue until next node is null\n   h. Leave critical section via LeaveCriticalSection\n4. Increment group index and add 0x18 to offset for next group\n5. Continue loop until groupIndex >= groupCount\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pResourceManager: Pointer to resource manager structure\n  * +0x0: DWORD flags (0=use direct socket send, non-0=use SendSocketData wrapper)\n  * +0x8: DWORD groupCount (number of independent connection groups)\n  * +0x14: Pointer to connection group array (array of pointers to connection node lists)\n  * +0x1c: Pointer to critical section base (critical sections at [base + offset])\n- pDataBuffer: Pointer to data buffer to broadcast to all connections\n- dataSize: Size of data buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (always returns success, errors are logged via WSAGetLastError)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If groupCount is 0 or less, function skips all groups and returns success\n- Connections with flags != 0 are skipped (assumed handled by SendSocketData wrapper)\n- Direct send errors (-1) trigger WSAGetLastError call for logging\n- Critical section synchronization prevents race conditions during connection list traversal\n- Group offset calculation: offset = groupIndex * 0x18 bytes per group\n\nStructure Layout - Resource Manager:\nOffset | Size | Field Name           | Type      | Description\n0x0    | 4    | dwUseWrapperFunction | uint      | 0=direct socket send, non-0=use wrapper\n0x8    | 4    | dwGroupCount         | uint      | Number of connection group arrays\n0x14   | 4    | pGroupArray          | uint*     | Pointer to array of group pointers\n0x1c   | 4    | pCriticalSectionBase | CRIT_SEC* | Base address for group critical sections\n\nStructure Layout - Connection Node:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type   | Description\n0x4    | 4    | pNextNode  | void*  | Pointer to next connection node in list\n0xc    | 4    | dwFlags    | uint   | 0=ready for direct send, non-0=skip/use wrapper\n0x10   | 4    | hSocket    | SOCKET | Windows socket handle for direct send()",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:105680f6b3c9f366b6b1354c02bca5a7",
