      "name": "DestroyResourceManager",
      "signature": "int DestroyResourceManager(void * pResourceMgr, void * pDataBuffer, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Destroys and deallocates all resources managed by a resource manager instance.\n\nThis function performs complete cleanup and shutdown of the resource management system,\nincluding socket handles, critical sections, linked list structures, and resource pools.\nThe function validates all data structures before deallocation to ensure integrity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters - pResourceMgr must be non-null, return immediately if null\n2. If pDataBuffer is provided, call BroadcastSocketData to notify clients of shutdown\n3. Load shutdown type from resource manager offset +0x86c\n4. If type is neither 1 nor 2, call InitiateThreadShutdown for graceful termination\n5. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity to verify critical sections before deletion\n6. Call EnterCriticalSection and DeleteCriticalSection on 3 main critical sections\n7. Close all 4 socket handles at offset +0xb90, marking each as 0xffffffff after close\n8. Call WSACleanup for complete Winsock shutdown\n9. Traverse first linked list chain at offset +0x878, follow next pointers at +0x5bc\n10. Deallocate each node using DeallocateResourcePoolElement, update head pointer\n11. Traverse second linked list chain at offset +0x88c, follow next pointers at +0xc\n12. Deallocate each node and update head pointer\n13. Deallocate 6 individual resource pool elements at specific offsets (+0x870, +0x874, +0x40, +0x8ac, +0x20, +0x28)\n14. Iterate through array of critical sections using g_dwGameSessionId as count\n15. Destroy each critical section element (size 0x18 bytes per element)\n16. Deallocate critical section array pointer and resource manager structure itself\n17. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pResourceMgr: void * - Pointer to resource manager structure containing sockets, critical sections, and linked lists\n  pDataBuffer: void * - Optional pointer to data buffer for final broadcast notification (may be null)\n  dwFlags: uint - Flags controlling shutdown behavior\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pResourceMgr is null, function returns immediately without processing\n  - If pDataBuffer is null, broadcast notification is skipped\n  - Shutdown type at +0x86c determines if thread shutdown is needed (types 1 and 2 skip it)\n  - Four socket handles checked against 0xffffffff (invalid marker) before closing\n  - Multiple critical sections must be entered and exited in specific order\n  - Linked list traversal uses next pointers at +0x5bc (first list) and +0xc (second list)\n  - Critical section array element size is 0x18 (24 bytes)\n  - Array iteration count determined by g_dwGameSessionId global variable",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
