      "name": "ProcessNetworkAddressTracking",
      "signature": "void ProcessNetworkAddressTracking(void * pSocketManager, in_addr remoteAddr, char * pDescription, uint flags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Process Network Address Tracking\n\nManages network address tracking within the socket manager infrastructure by validating\nincoming remote addresses, searching the hash table for existing entries, and creating\nor updating tracking records as needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate socket manager is initialized at offset 0xbd0\n2. Load critical section pointer at offset 0xc\n3. Calculate hash bucket index using AND operation\n4. Enter critical section for thread-safe access\n5. Load hash bucket pointer from array at offset 0x20\n6. Iterate through linked list to search for matching address\n7. Compare each entry address field at offset 0x18\n8. If match found, call cleanup handler at 0x6ff5e550\n9. If no match, convert IP to ASCII and log new address detection\n10. Call InsertOrUpdateTrackedAddressInHashTable to create entry\n11. Release critical section via LeaveCriticalSection\n12. Return to caller with stack cleanup via RET 0x10\n\nParameters:\n- pSocketManager: void* pointer to manager structure\n- remoteAddr: in_addr network address to track\n- pDescription: char* descriptive string for logging\n- flags: uint bit flags for hash computation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function has no return value, returns via RET 0x10\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uninitialized manager check at 0xbd0 causes early exit\n- Hash bucket linked list traversal uses offset 0x1c for next",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:e06d368537b03ba9d686ce24b340d779",
