      "signature": "void ProcessClientConnectionData(void * pServerContext, ClientConnection * pConnectionData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Processes incoming client socket data in a continuous loop, dispatching on callback result codes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if server is active (pServerContext[0xbc0] != 0); return if not\n2. Enter main data processing loop that runs while server is active:\n   a. Initialize loop state variables: bytesProcessed=0, bufferAllocated=0, connectionSlotIndex=0\n   b. Acquire critical section lock on connection buffer (pConnectionData[0xb0])\n   c. Invoke callback handler at pServerContext[0xbc0] to perform socket operations and populate\n      bytesProcessed, bufferAllocated, connectionSlotIndex output parameters with results\n   d. Dispatch on callback return code in EAX (high 32 bits in EDX):\n      - Code 2: Data available - process payload below\n      - Code 3: Disconnect - return from function immediately\n      - Code 4: Client banned/hacked - log security event and return\n      - Code 5: Buffer maintenance trigger - skip to compaction phase\n      - Other codes: Continue to buffer compaction\n3. For code 2 (data available):\n   a. If throttle limit enabled (pServerContext[0xbd0]), call ThrottleClientPacketRate with connection\n      info; if throttle rejects (returns false), log ban and return\n   b. Allocate 1472-byte slot from memory pool at pServerContext[0x878], fatal exit if fails\n   c. Calculate payload size: bytesProcessed - bufferAllocated, copy into slot via memmove loop\n   d. Initialize slot metadata: size at offset +0x5b4, GetTickCount() at +0x5b8, next pointer NULL\n      at +0x5bc, copy client connection info to slot[0]\n   e. Verify connectionSlotIndex < pServerContext[0x87c]; fatal exit with error code 6 if >= max\n   f. Acquire critical section on pServerContext[0x854] and link slot into doubly-linked list:\n      - pServerContext[0x870 + slotIndex*4] = head pointer (points to first slot in list)\n      - pServerContext[0x874 + slotIndex*4] = tail pointer (always points to newest slot)\n      - If list is empty (head == NULL), set head = pNewSlot\n      - Else set previous node's next pointer (at offset +0x5bc) = pNewSlot\n      - Always set tail = pNewSlot\n4. After callback dispatch (all codes):\n   a. Acquire connection lock and read remaining buffer bytes: bufferRemaining = bytes_in_buffer - bytesProcessed\n   b. Compact buffer by moving unprocessed data to start: memmove(buffer_base, buffer_base+bytesProcessed, bufferRemaining)\n   c. Verify final size after compaction: bufferRemaining + bytesProcessed <= 1460 bytes (0x5b4);\n      if exceeds, log fatal error code 6 and exit\n   d. Update byte count: bytes_in_buffer = bufferRemaining\n   e. Release connection lock and loop back to step 2a if server still running\n\nParameters:\npServerContext - Server/socket context; contains:\n  +0x854: Critical section for slot pool allocation synchronization\n  +0x870: Array of head pointers for per-connection slot linked lists (indexed by connection slot)\n  +0x874: Array of tail pointers for per-connection slot linked lists (indexed by connection slot)\n  +0x878: Free pool head pointer; non-zero indicates pool allocated, zero means allocate on demand\n  +0x87c: Maximum valid connection slot index (upper bound for connectionSlotIndex)\n  +0xbc0: Callback function pointer for socket operations\n  +0xbd0: Throttle enabled flag (non-zero enables rate limiting)\n\npConnectionData - ClientConnection structure; contains:\n  +0x0: Peer IP address (in_addr format, 4 bytes)\n  +0x8: Peer port number and connection flags\n  +0x18: Peer IP address copy for logging (in_addr format)\n  +0x2c: Receive buffer base address (1460-byte circular buffer for incoming socket data)\n  +0xa8: Bytes currently in receive buffer (read before processing, written after compaction)\n  +0xb0: Critical section lock for receive buffer access synchronization\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function is a server-side event loop that runs until callback returns code 3 (disconnect),\ncode 4 (client banned), or pServerContext[0xbc0] becomes zero (server shutdown)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic constant 0x5c0 (1472) = 1460 (max data) + 12 bytes (header/metadata)\n- Magic constant 0x5b4 (1460) = max receive buffer size after compaction\n- Offsets +0x5b4, +0x5b8, +0x5bc are slot metadata fields within 1472-byte allocation\n- Offset +0x16d, +0x16e, +0x16f are alternate address calculations for metadata (5b4/4=16d, 5b8/4=16e, 5bc/4=16f)\n- Slot linked list is per-connection (per slot index); multiple connections maintain independent lists\n- Buffer overflow (size > 0x5b4 after compaction) is fatal: logs error code 6 and exits process\n- Slot index overflow (connectionSlotIndex >= max slots) is fatal: logs error code 6 and exits process\n- Allocation failure is fatal: logs error code 2 and exits process\n- Throttle rejection (code 2 + throttle enabled) logs ban at offset 0x644 and returns normally",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11b",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:be6569ba552271725c00e1bb8d02b46b",
