      "name": "DeleteFileIfOlderThanThreshold",
      "signature": "void DeleteFileIfOlderThanThreshold(FILETIME * pThresholdTime)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deletes a file if its timestamp embedded in the filename is older than a specified threshold.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate the length of the filename string using Strlen\n2. Subtract 10 to determine the offset to the embedded date portion (format: --DD-MM-YY)\n3. If filename is not long enough to contain date (length < 10 bytes), exit early\n4. Parse the embedded date string using sscanf with format string \"%2d%2d%2d\" to extract year, month, day\n5. Build a SYSTEMTIME structure with parsed date values and time set to 00:00:00.000\n6. Apply century adjustment: if year < 0x5b (91) add 0x7d0 (2000), else add 0x76c (1900)\n7. Convert the SYSTEMTIME to FILETIME format using SystemTimeToFileTime function pointer\n8. Compare the converted FILETIME with threshold timestamp at pThresholdTime + 0x4 (dwHighDateTime)\n9. If threshold timestamp is greater than or equal to converted time, exit without deletion\n10. Calculate age difference: subtract converted FILETIME from threshold timestamp\n11. Compare age difference against threshold value 0x4b7 (1207 units)\n12. If age difference is less than threshold, exit without deletion (file too recent)\n13. If both conditions met (timestamp valid AND age >= threshold), call DeleteFileA to remove the file\n\nParameters:\npThresholdTime: Pointer to FILETIME structure containing comparison threshold timestamp\n                The dwHighDateTime field (offset +0x4) contains the threshold FILETIME value\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function performs deletion as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Date format expected in filename: characters at positions length-10 through length-1\n- Format string: \"%2d%2d%2d\" (dash-separated 2-digit values for year, month, day)\n- Century adjustment threshold: 0x5b (91 decimal); values >= 91 treated as 1900+, < 91 as 2000+\n- Age threshold: 0x4b7 (1207 FILETIME units) represents minimum age before deletion\n- Function exits silently without error if filename format invalid or too short\n- File deletion only occurs when both timestamp parsing succeeds AND age >= threshold\n\nStructure Layout - FILETIME (at pThresholdTime):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type       Description\n+0x0    4     dwLowDateTime     DWORD      Low 32 bits of file time\n+0x4    4     dwHighDateTime    DWORD      High 32 bits of file time (used in comparison)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:a1367c02e1ae1d02d00265a2c610e5cf",
