      "signature": "void WriteRealmStartupInfo(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Writes realm startup information to log file with date/time and computer name.\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. Allocate 68-byte stack frame (0x44 bytes)\n2. Initialize computerNameSize to 0x40 (64 bytes max)\n3. Call GetComputerNameA to retrieve local computer name\n4. If GetComputerNameA fails (EAX=0), null-terminate the buffer (clear first byte)\n5. Write separator line (63 dashes) to log file via WriteFormattedWideStringToFile\n6. Load 7 global game time values (year, month, day, hour, minute, second, millisecond)\n7. Call WriteFormattedWideStringToFile with format string and parameters:\n   - Format: \"%s Realm startup at %04d-%02d-%02d %02d:%02d:%02d.%03u\n\"\n   - computerNameBuffer: Computer name (or empty if GetComputerNameA failed)\n   - g_GameStartTime: Year (4-digit format %04d)\n   - wGameMonth: Month (2-digit zero-padded %02d, range 1-12)\n   - wGameDay: Day (2-digit zero-padded %02d, range 1-31)\n   - wGameHour: Hour (2-digit zero-padded %02d, range 0-23)\n   - wGameMinute: Minute (2-digit zero-padded %02d, range 0-59)\n   - wGameSecond: Second (2-digit zero-padded %02d, range 0-59)\n   - wGameMillisecond: Millisecond (3-digit zero-padded %03u, range 0-999)\n8. Write final separator line (63 dashes) to log file\n9. Return void\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- logFile (ESI, FILE*): Output stream in wide-character mode for logging realm startup\n\nRETURNS:\n- void: No return value, output written to logFile parameter\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n- If GetComputerNameA fails, empty string logged instead of computer name\n- Buffer overflow protection: 64-byte buffer (MAX_COMPUTERNAME_LENGTH + 1)\n- Assumes logFile is valid, open, and in wide-character mode (wchar_t)\n- Date/time values are read from global game time structure at 0x6ff81838+\n\nGLOBAL DATA STRUCTURE (game time, starting at 0x6ff81838):\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type   | Description\n-------|------|------------------|--------|------------------\n  0x00 |  2   | g_GameStartTime  | word   | Year (4-digit, e.g., 2025)\n  0x02 |  2   | wGameMonth       | word   | Month (1-12)\n  0x04 |  2   | (padding)        | word   | Reserved\n  0x06 |  2   | wGameDay         | word   | Day of month (1-31)\n  0x08 |  2   | wGameHour        | word   | Hour (0-23)\n  0x0a |  2   | wGameMinute      | word   | Minute (0-59)\n  0x0c |  2   | wGameSecond      | word   | Second (0-59)\n  0x0e |  2   | wGameMillisecond | word   | Millisecond (0-999)",
