      "name": "CreateCrashDumpLogFile",
      "signature": "void CreateCrashDumpLogFile(char * pBaseFilename)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Creates a timestamped crash dump log file with the current system date and time.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x104 bytes (260 bytes) on stack for filename buffer\n2. Call GetLocalTime() to retrieve current SYSTEMTIME structure\n3. Extract day, month, and year fields from SYSTEMTIME (offsets +0x6, +0x2, +0x0)\n4. Convert year to 2-digit value by dividing by 100 using IDIV instruction\n5. Call sprintf() to format filename as: game_path + base_filename + YY_MM_DD.txt\n6. Test if optional crash config pointer (EDI) is non-null\n7. If config exists and EDI != 0, set flag *EDI = 1\n8. Compare mode byte at [EBX] with 'a' (0x61 ASCII)\n9. If mode != 'a', skip crash dump operations\n10. If mode == 'a', call OpenFileForCrashDump() for crash mode with g_pCurrentCrashDumpFile\n11. Test return value (EAX); if file opened successfully (EAX != 0)\n12. Call _fclose() to close the crash dump file handle\n13. Clear config flag by setting *EDI = 0\n14. Jump to main file open at offset 0x6ff6841a\n15. Call OpenFileForCrashDump() with main filename and EBX parameter (mode flag holder)\n16. Return to caller using RET 0x4 (callee cleanup of 1 parameter)\n\nParameters:\npBaseFilename - Base filename string to use as prefix in timestamped log file\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; file operations managed internally by OpenFileForCrashDump()\n\nSpecial Cases:\nCrash dump mode: When EDI config pointer exists and [EBX] == 'a', opens crash dump file first\n  then immediately closes it after opening main log file. This creates a checkpoint record.\nTimestamp components: Uses only 2-digit year (YY), month (MM), day (DD) in final filename\nImplicit register parameters:\n  - ESI: Pointer to SYSTEMTIME structure from caller context\n  - EBX: Pointer to mode flag byte (checked against 'a' = 0x61)\n  - EDI: Pointer to crash config status dword (set to 1 during crash, 0 after)\nStack allocation: Local buffer at ESP+0 for 0x104 bytes (260 bytes for formatted filename)\n\nStructure Layout (SYSTEMTIME from GetLocalTime):\nOffset  Size  Field   Type    Description\n------  ----  ------  ------  ----------------------------------\n+00     2     wYear   uint16  Year (1601-30827)\n+02     2     wMonth  uint16  Month (1-12)\n+04     2     wDay    uint16  Day (1-31)\n+06     2     wHour   uint16  Hour (0-23)",
