      "name": "InitializeAndBuildPath",
      "signature": "void InitializeAndBuildPath(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize path buffer and conditionally build realm-specific path\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Preserve ESI register for caller (PUSH ESI at entry)\n2. Move first parameter from EAX to ESI (pathBuffer pointer)\n3. Move second parameter from EDI to EAX (realmId)\n4. Clear the path buffer by writing null terminator to buffer[0]\n5. Call ExtractModuleDirectory to validate the realm ID\n6. Test EAX for validation result (non-zero = valid)\n7. Jump to function_exit label (0x6ff60845) if validation failed\n8. If validation succeeded:\n   a. Push realmId onto stack for AppendPathComponent\n   b. Push address of g_szPathSeparator (backslash character at 0x6ff76e9c)\n   c. Push pPathBuffer for modification\n   d. Call AppendPathComponent to build path with separator and realm ID\n   e. Move pPathBuffer pointer to ECX for finalization\n   f. POP ESI (restore caller's register state)\n   g. Jump to 0x6ff67c40 (CreateDirectoryPathRecursive) for path finalization\n9. If validation failed: restore ESI and return immediately\n\nParameters:\npPathBuffer (passed in EAX, stored in ESI): Pointer to character buffer that will be initialized and populated with realm-specific path components. Buffer must be pre-allocated by caller.\nnRealmId (passed in EDI): Unsigned integer realm identifier used to determine which realm-specific path components to append. Validated by ExtractModuleDirectory before use.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies pPathBuffer via side effects and does not return a direct value. Path is finalized by tail-called CreateDirectoryPathRecursive at 0x6ff67c40 if validation succeeds.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid realm: Returns immediately without modifying buffer (early exit at 0x6ff60845)\n- Register preservation: ESI preserved across entire function for caller (PUSH at 0x6ff60820, POP at 0x6ff6083f)\n- Tail call optimization: Uses JMP to 0x6ff67c40 instead of CALL, so path finalization happens in same call stack\n- Buffer initialization: Explicitly sets buffer[0] = 0x00 before any appending operations\n\nData References:\ng_szPathSeparator at 0x6ff76e9c: Single backslash character (0x5C) used as path component separator. Referenced by multiple path-building functions to maintain consistent path format across codebase.",
