      "name": "ShutdownResourcesAndExit",
      "signature": "void ShutdownResourcesAndExit(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Gracefully shut down server resources and exit the application.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if worker thread is ready (g_dwWorkerThreadReady)\n2. If not ready, get return address for error reporting\n3. Perform Windows socket cleanup (WSACleanup)\n4. Log unrecoverable error with source location and return address\n5. Recursively call shutdown to ensure proper cleanup\n6. Perform emergency exit with code -1\n7. If worker thread ready, wait for pending dealloc queue to drain (max 1000ms)\n   - Loop: enter critical section, check queue head, exit section\n   - If queue has items, sleep 10ms and retry\n   - Break when queue is empty (0) or timeout reached\n8. Close all log file pointers in the log file array\n   - Iterate through log file pointer array (g_LogFilePointers to 0x6ff81950)\n   - For each pointer: acquire mutex, close file if non-NULL, zero pointer, release mutex\n9. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(none - this function takes no parameters)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - This function does not return normally; it either recursively exits or terminates via _exit()\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Worker thread not ready (g_dwWorkerThreadReady == 0): Triggers recursive shutdown with error logging\n- Memory dealloc queue drain timeout: Gives 1000ms for pending deallocations before proceeding\n- Log file iteration: Uses array loop with bounds checking (0x6ff81950 is array end)\n- Mutex protection: All file operations protected by g_hCrashDumpMutex\n\nStructure Layout:\nLog file array format:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name                 Type          Description\n  -----   ----  ------------------         -------       -------------------\n  0x00    0x04  LogFilePointer[0]          FILE*         First log file pointer\n  0x04    0x04  LogFilePointer[1]          FILE*         Second log file pointer\n  ...     0x04  LogFilePointer[N]          FILE*         Nth log file pointer\n  0x50    0x00  ARRAY_END                               Array end at 0x6ff81950",
