      "name": "EnqueueLogMessage",
      "signature": "void EnqueueLogMessage(char * pModulePrefix, char * pFunctionName, void * pDataBuffer, uint bufferSize, uint messageType, uint skipDataCopy, uint reserved)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Enqueues a log message to a thread-safe message queue with optional payload.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify initialization by checking g_dwWorkerThreadShutdownFlag (should be 0) and \n   g_dwWorkerThreadReady (should be non-zero); exit immediately if not initialized\n2. If skipDataCopy is 0, validate pDataBuffer readability via IsBadReadPtr; set \n   skipDataCopy to 1 if buffer is unreadable\n3. Calculate total allocation size: sum string lengths of pModulePrefix and \n   pFunctionName, add 0x16 for header, plus bufferSize if skipDataCopy is 0\n4. Enter critical section for thread-safe allocation\n5. Allocate message node from g_MessageQueueHead pool via AllocateMessageNode with \n   calculated totalSize; exit critical section\n6. Initialize message header at node offsets:\n   - Offset +0x8: payload offset = totalSize + 0x24\n   - Offset +0xc: marker value 0x2\n   - Offset +0x10: marker value 0x1\n7. Call GetLocalTime to fill SYSTEMTIME structure at offset +0x14\n8. Store message metadata at offset +0x24:\n   - +0x0: pDataBuffer (original buffer pointer)\n   - +0x4: bufferSize (data size)\n   - +0x8: messageType (message type code)\n   - +0xc: skipDataCopy (copy flag)\n   - +0x10: reserved flag converted to boolean (1 if reserved==0)\n9. If skipDataCopy is 0, copy pDataBuffer into payload area at calculated offset:\n   - Copy DWORD units: bufferSize >> 2 iterations\n   - Copy remainder bytes: bufferSize & 3 individual bytes\n10. Enter critical section for queue manipulation\n11. If message has previous node (pNext != 0), unlink it from temporary list by \n    updating forward/backward pointers\n12. Insert message at queue head g_pCurrentMessageNode:\n    - Set node pNext to current head\n    - Copy head's pPrevOrOffset to new node's pPrevOrOffset\n    - Update old head's pPrevOrOffset to point to new node\n13. Increment g_dwMemoryDeallocEntryCount message counter\n14. Add node size (pListNode[1].pNext = totalSize + 0x24) to \n    g_dwMemoryDeallocTotalBytes total counter\n15. Update g_pCurrentMessageNode to point to new node\n16. Exit critical section and return\n\nParameters:\n  pModulePrefix: Pointer to null-terminated module/component name string (0-256 bytes)\n  pFunctionName: Pointer to null-terminated function name string (0-256 bytes)\n  pDataBuffer: Pointer to optional binary data buffer to include in message; may be NULL\n  bufferSize: Size in bytes of pDataBuffer payload (0 to skip copying)\n  messageType: Message type code/classification (0-0xFFFFFFFF)\n  skipDataCopy: If non-zero, do not copy pDataBuffer into message node (store pointer only)\n  reserved: Flag parameter; converted to boolean (1 if reserved==0, 0 otherwise)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; function always returns via RET instruction\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If initialization flags are not met, function exits immediately without queuing\n  - If skipDataCopy is 0 and IsBadReadPtr returns true, automatically sets skipDataCopy \n    to 1 to prevent reading invalid memory\n  - Message node unlink operation handles both forward and backward pointer updates for\n    nodes in temporary list before queue insertion\n  - All queue operations are protected by g_CriticalSection critical section to ensure\n    thread-safe access to g_pCurrentMessageNode queue head and counters\n  - Total allocation size is totalSize + 0x24 bytes (header + string lengths + payload)\n  - Function uses two critical section enter/exit pairs: one for allocation, one for \n    queue integration\n\nMessage Node Structure (allocated from g_MessageQueueHead pool):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type      Description\n  0x0     4     pNext                ptr       Forward list pointer (to previous node)\n  0x4     4     pPrevOrOffset        int       Backward list pointer or offset adjustment\n  0x8     4     payloadOffset        uint      Offset to payload area (totalSize + 0x24)\n  0xc     4     marker1              uint      Marker value 0x2\n  0x10    4     marker2              uint      Marker value 0x1\n  0x14    16    systemTime           SYSTEMTIME Timestamp structure (wYear, wMonth, wDow, etc)\n  0x24    4     pOriginalBuffer      ptr       Pointer to original data buffer\n  0x28    4     originalSize         uint      Size of original data buffer\n  0x2c    4     messageType          uint      Message type/code\n  0x30    4     skipCopyFlag         uint      Flag: 1 if data not copied (0=copied)\n  0x34    4     reservedFlag         uint      Reserved flag: 1 if reserved param was 0\n  0x38    ...   payloadData          bytes     Copied message data (if skipDataCopy=0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:7d41e7562f7f6856d38421ed21f965a0",
