      "name": "ValidateAndInitializeNetworkConfig",
      "signature": "void ValidateAndInitializeNetworkConfig(void * pGameConfig, char * pConfigString)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Validates network configuration parameters and initializes network settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pConfigString parameter from stack[ESP+8]\n2. Test if pConfigString is NULL - if NULL, trigger fatal error shutdown sequence\n3. On NULL pConfigString: call GetReturnAddress() to capture return address for error logging\n4. Call WSACleanup() to clean up Winsock library resources\n5. Log fatal error with code 6, error message, and location information via LogErrorAndShutdown()\n6. Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit() to clean up remaining game resources\n7. Exit process with status code -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n8. Load pGameConfig parameter from stack[ESP+4] if pConfigString is valid\n9. Test if pGameConfig is NULL - if NULL, substitute default config from address 0x6ff768ec\n10. Calculate return address location at stack[ESP+0xc] for network initialization call\n11. Call network initialization function with pGameConfig, pConfigString, and return address\n\nParameters:\npGameConfig (void *): Pointer to game configuration structure, or NULL to use default config\npConfigString (char *): Network configuration string buffer - MUST NOT be NULL\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return on error path (calls _exit(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL pConfigString: Immediately initiates fatal error shutdown with error code 6\nNULL pGameConfig: Substitutes default config from address 0x6ff768ec\nWSACleanup: Called before shutdown to release Winsock resources\nMultiple paths: Called from 23 locations indicating critical role in network initialization",
