      "name": "InitializeGameState",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the game engine's global state and creates the worker thread\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear worker thread idle flag (g_dwWorkerThreadIdleFlag = 0)\n2. Create worker thread via CreateThread, calling ProcessMemoryDeallocQueue as entry point\n3. Store returned thread handle in g_hWorkerThread for management\n4. Store thread ID in g_dwWorkerThreadId\n5. Set thread ready flag (g_dwWorkerThreadReady = 1) to mark thread as active\n6. Get current system time via GetLocalTime and store in g_GameStartTime\n7. Initialize 20 consecutive game state flag variables (g_dwGameStateFlags[0-19]) to 1\n   - These represent enabled/active states for 20 game subsystems or feature slots\n   - Each flag controls whether a corresponding subsystem is operational\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return a value (initialization routine)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Worker thread creation uses stack-allocated parameter block\n  - Thread handle is stored globally for later CloseHandle cleanup\n  - All 20 state flags are initialized to 1 (enabled state)\n  - GameStartTime captures the exact moment engine initialization completes\n\nCalling Convention:\n  __stdcall - Win32 API calling convention with callee cleanup",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e5fb13e917d36359f8c09e38ee313686",
