      "name": "Decode14BitPackedValue",
      "signature": "int Decode14BitPackedValue(byte * pEncodedBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Decode14BitPackedValue - Decodes a 14-bit value from two 7-bit encoded bytes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer to 2-byte encoded array from stack parameter\n2. Load second byte (byte[1]) which contains high 7 bits\n3. Load first byte (byte[0]) which contains low 7 bits using zero-extend\n4. Mask first byte with 0x7f to remove any bit 7 flag\n5. Mask second byte with 0x7f to remove any bit 7 flag\n6. Shift second byte left 7 bits (multiply by 128) to position high bits\n7. Add masked first byte to shifted second byte\n8. Return combined 14-bit value in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  pEncodedBytes - Pointer to 2-byte array with packed data, each byte uses only lower 7 bits\n\nReturns:\n  int - 14-bit decoded value (range 0-16383)\n    Bit layout: [7 bits from byte[1]] [7 bits from byte[0]]\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Value range is 0-16383 (2^14 - 1, exactly 14 bits)\n  - Bit 7 (0x80) in each byte is masked and ignored\n  - Assumes at least 2 bytes available at pEncodedBytes\n  - Uses __stdcall calling convention (callee cleans 4-byte parameter)\n  - No error checking; assumes valid input",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
