      "name": "SetSocketNonBlocking",
      "signature": "undefined4 SetSocketNonBlocking(void * pSocketContext, u_long enableNonBlocking)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Configures a socket to non-blocking mode using ioctlsocket.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract SOCKET handle from context structure at offset +0x8\n2. Initialize mode buffer with enableNonBlocking parameter\n3. Call ioctlsocket() with FIONBIO command to set non-blocking flag\n4. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n- pSocketContext: Pointer to context structure containing SOCKET at offset +0x8\n- enableNonBlocking: Mode value for ioctlsocket (typically 1 for non-blocking, 0 for blocking)\n\nReturns:\n- Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- FIONBIO (0x8004667e): Windows ioctl command to enable/disable non-blocking mode\n- The mode parameter is passed by value via EDX register (__fastcall convention)\n- Function does not validate socket validity or ioctlsocket return value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
