      "name": "CopyInetNtoaToBuffer",
      "signature": "char * CopyInetNtoaToBuffer(in_addr ipAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Converts an IP address to dotted decimal string and stores in static buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call inet_ntoa() to convert the in_addr parameter to null-terminated string in EAX\n2. Initialize EDX to point to static buffer at 0x6ff819a8\n3. Loop through source string byte-by-byte:\n   - Load char from source [EAX]\n   - Copy to destination [EDX]\n   - Increment both pointers\n   - Test if char is null terminator\n   - Jump back to loop if not null\n4. Return pointer to static buffer (0x6ff819a8)\n\nParameters:\nipAddress (in_addr, ECX): 32-bit IP address in network byte order\n\nReturns:\nchar*: Pointer to static buffer containing dotted decimal representation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses thread-unsafe static buffer (0x6ff819a8), max 15 chars for \"255.255.255.255\"\n- Buffer is shared across all calls, overwritten on each invocation\n- in_addr is 4-byte integer (network byte order)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
