      "name": "InitializeWinsock",
      "signature": "bool InitializeWinsock(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the Windows Sockets 2 (Winsock) API for network communication.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Allocate 400-byte stack buffer for WSADATA structure\\n2. Load address of wsaData buffer into EAX\\n3. Push wsaData address and version 0x0101 (Winsock 1.1) as parameters\\n4. Call WSAStartup() to initialize the Windows Sockets library\\n5. Convert WSAStartup return code to boolean using NEG/SBB/INC pattern\\n6. Clean up stack and return boolean result\\n\\nParameters:\\n(None) - Operates on stack-allocated WSADATA structure\\n\\nReturns:\\n- true (EAX = 1) if WSAStartup succeeded (returned 0)\\n- false (EAX = 0) if WSAStartup failed (returned nonzero error code)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- WSADATA allocation (400 bytes) is sufficient for Winsock 1.1 on all platforms\\n- WSAStartup version 0x0101 requests Winsock 1.1 compatibility\\n- Return value conversion: NEG converts to two's complement, SBB sets sign, INC normalizes to 0 or 1\\n- Function is called at entry point and from function pointer table at 0x6ff7d91c\\n- If WSAStartup fails, network operations will not be initialized",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:3fa12ef2e049bfbacfa74e934975c62c",
