      "name": "SendDataToSocket",
      "signature": "int SendDataToSocket(void * pSocketContext, char * pBuffer, int nBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Sends data to a socket with would-block error handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call send() with socket handle from pSocketContext[8], buffer, and size\n2. Get last Winsock error code via WSAGetLastError()\n3. If error is 0x274c (WSAEWOULDBLOCK), close socket and return 0\n4. Otherwise return the send result (bytes sent or error code)\n\nParameters:\n- pSocketContext: Pointer to context containing SOCKET at offset +8\n- pBuffer: Data buffer to transmit\n- nBufferSize: Size of buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- On success: Number of bytes sent (>0)\n- On WSAEWOULDBLOCK: 0 after closing socket\n- On other errors: -1 (from send()) or WSA error code\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- 0x274c (WSAEWOULDBLOCK): Socket would block, connection closed\n- Caller must be aware that socket is closed when return is 0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:a49f54849f1906bef898b616243e65db",
