      "name": "DecodeBitStream",
      "signature": "int DecodeBitStream(byte * pOutputBuffer, int outputSize, byte * pInputBuffer, int inputSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Decompresses bit-packed data using lookup tables for bit widths and bit patterns.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output pointer, bit counter (8), and partial byte accumulator\n2. For each input byte:\n   - Look up bit width in DAT_6ff7f210 and bit pattern in DAT_6ff80dd0\n   - While bits extracted >= bits remaining in output byte:\n     - Extract bits from input byte and combine with partial byte\n     - Write complete output byte and reset accumulators\n     - Continue with remaining bits\n   - If bits remain: accumulate into partial byte for next iteration\n3. Flush any remaining partial byte if bits were accumulated\n4. Return number of output bytes written\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer: Destination buffer for decompressed data\n- outputSize: Maximum output buffer size in bytes\n- pInputBuffer: Source buffer with bit-packed data\n- inputSize: Number of input bytes to decode\n\nReturns:\n- Number of bytes written to output buffer\n- 0 if output buffer exceeded (early termination)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a66a28d0858034ac9b930abf6c4cd1f4",
