      "comment": "Performs binary search on a sorted array to find an entry matching the search value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load array count and pointer from the search table structure\n2. Initialize low bound (ECX) to 0 and verify count > 0, exit if empty\n3. Loop: Calculate midpoint index between low and high bounds\n4. Load element at midpoint from array using index * 8 byte stride\n5. Compare element value against search value\n6. If element <= search value, set high bound to midpoint (search right half)\n7. If element > search value, set low bound to midpoint + 1 (search left half)\n8. Repeat until low bound >= high bound (convergence)\n9. On convergence: Check final element at midpoint using JNC flag\n10. If found (CF=0): Load and return element ID from offset +4 in element\n11. If not found: Return 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) to indicate no match\n\nParameters:\n- pSearchTable: Pointer to StringSearchTable structure with count and pointer\n  - Offset +0x0: dwCount (DWORD) - number of elements in array\n  - Offset +0x8: pElements (DWORD*) - pointer to array of 8-byte elements\n- searchValue: DWORD search value to find in array elements\n\nReturns:\n- EAX = Element ID (from offset +4) if match found\n- EAX = 0xFFFFFFFF if no match found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty array (count <= 0): Immediately returns -1\n- Array elements are 8 bytes: First 4 bytes = value, offset +4 = ID/index\n- Binary search assumes array is sorted by value in ascending order\n- Search is case-sensitive on value comparison (CMP uses unsigned comparison)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6c007b0113dedf8ec010a2aa0e5d5d39",
