      "name": "ComputeHashByte",
      "signature": "byte ComputeHashByte(void * pReserved, uint dwHashValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Computes a single-byte hash from a 32-bit value using XOR-based bit folding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract bits [8:15] from hashValue using right shift by 8 positions\n2. Copy extracted bits and XOR with original hashValue to combine bit ranges\n3. Extract bits [16:23] from intermediate result using right shift by 16 positions\n4. XOR shifted bits [16:23] with bits [8:15] to fold higher-order bits\n5. XOR all intermediate results with original hashValue [0:7]\n6. Mask final result to single byte using bitwise AND with 0xFF\n7. Return computed hash byte in EAX register\n\nParameters:\n- reserved (ECX): First parameter, unused in computation (allows __fastcall interface usage)\n- hashValue (EDX): 32-bit input value containing bits to fold into hash result\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Single byte hash result derived from XOR of bits at positions [0:7], [8:15], and [16:23]\n\nStructure Layout:\nHash computation operates independently on bit ranges of the 32-bit input:\n  Bits [0:7]   - Included directly in final XOR operation\n  Bits [8:15]  - Extracted via SHR 8 and XORed with lower bits\n  Bits [16:23] - Extracted via SHR 16 and XORed with combined result\n  Bits [24:31] - Implicitly included via unsigned shift operations\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero input (0x00000000) produces zero output (0x00)\n- All bits set (0xFFFFFFFF) produces 0xFF output\n- Function suitable for hash table indexing, checksums, or distributed hash functions\n- Reserved parameter allows this function to serve as callback or interface function pointer\n- No error conditions; always produces valid byte output (0x00-0xFF)",
