      "name": "CopyStringWithSpacePadding",
      "signature": "void CopyStringWithSpacePadding(char * szpSourceString)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Copies up to 4 characters from source string to destination buffer, padding with spaces.\n\nThis function implements a fixed-width 4-character string copy commonly used in game\ndata structures for compact string storage. It reads characters from the source string\nuntil either a null terminator is found or all 4 characters are copied, filling any\nremaining destination bytes with space characters (0x20).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load first character from source string\n2. If null terminator found, fill all 4 destination bytes with spaces and return\n3. Copy first character to destination byte 0\n4. Load second character\n5. If null terminator found, fill bytes 1-3 with spaces and return\n6. Copy second character to destination byte 1\n7. Load third character\n8. If null terminator found, fill bytes 2-3 with spaces and return\n9. Copy third character to destination byte 2\n10. Load fourth character\n11. If null terminator found, fill byte 3 with space and return\n12. Copy fourth character to destination byte 3\n13. Return\n\nParameters:\n  szpSourceString (ECX): Pointer to null-terminated source string\n  szpDestBuffer (EAX): Pointer to 4-byte destination buffer for output\n\nReturns:\n  void - Destination buffer filled with 4-character string (space-padded)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Empty string: All 4 destination bytes filled with spaces (0x20)\n  1-3 character string: Characters copied followed by space padding to 4 bytes\n  4+ character string: Only first 4 characters copied (no null check on 4th)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e6e34a31113a20de49dd6eedb82cd7e0",
