      "name": "SearchTreeWithFallback",
      "signature": "TreeNode * SearchTreeWithFallback(void * pSearchContainer, int nSearchValue, int nReturnFallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Searches a tree structure for a value with optional fallback behavior.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSearchContainer is not NULL\n2. Validate nSearchValue bounds (>= 0 and < container size)\n3. Load tree pointer from container at offset +0xc\n4. Call SearchTreeNodeByValue to search tree for nSearchValue\n5. Load sentinel pointer from g_pNullTreeNodeSentinel\n6. Check if search returned null or sentinel value\n7. If result is null/sentinel and nReturnFallback is true, return sentinel\n8. Otherwise return search result pointer\n\nParameters:\npSearchContainer - Pointer to container structure with tree data\nnSearchValue - Index/value to search for in tree (range validated)\nnReturnFallback - Boolean flag: if true return sentinel on not found\n\nReturns:\nTreeNode pointer: Either found node, sentinel on not found (if fallback enabled), or NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\nReturns sentinel (g_pNullTreeNodeSentinel) if container is NULL or value out of bounds",
