      "name": "InsertNodeInBinarySearchTree",
      "signature": "void InsertNodeInBinarySearchTree(byte * pNewNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Inserts a new node into a binary search tree structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load tree root pointer from EAX (implicit second parameter)\n2. Loop: If tree is empty (root == NULL), insert new node at root and return\n3. For non-empty tree, compare new node data with current node data byte-by-byte\n4. Process two bytes per iteration (optimization for string comparison)\n5. Load first byte from both new node and current node for comparison\n6. If bytes differ, compute comparison result (-1 for less, 1 for greater, 0 for equal)\n7. If new node < current: traverse to left child (offset +0x24) and continue loop\n8. If new node == current: deallocate duplicate node and return (error case)\n9. If new node > current: traverse to right child (offset +0x28) and continue loop\n10. Load second byte and repeat comparison if first bytes matched\n11. If null terminator (0x00) encountered, strings are equal, deallocate duplicate\n12. Continue until empty tree position found, then insert new node\n\nParameters:\npNewNode (Stack[0x4]): Pointer to new node to insert. Node structure:\n  - Offset 0x00-0x1F: Data/key for comparison (32-byte string or binary data)\n  - Offset 0x20: Reserved/padding (4 bytes)\n  - Offset 0x24: Left child pointer (less-than subtree)\n  - Offset 0x28: Right child pointer (greater-than subtree)\n\npTreeRoot (EAX implicit): Pointer to tree root pointer address (address of root variable, not root itself)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (modifies tree structure in-place, no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty tree: Sets root pointer directly to new node\n- Duplicate key: Calls DeallocateResourcePoolElement to free duplicate and returns\n- Comparison uses 2-byte chunks for performance optimization\n- Null terminator (0x00) triggers equality detection\n- Uses single-pass traversal with implicit stack through register parameter\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 32   | data       | byte[32] | Node key/data for comparison (string or binary)\n0x20   | 4    | reserved   | pad  | Padding/reserved space\n0x24   | 4    | left       | ptr  | Left subtree (less-than comparisons)\n0x28   | 4    | right      | ptr  | Right subtree (greater-than comparisons)\n0x2C   | 4    | total      | -    | Structure size (44 bytes per node)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b29068155a2962d849312ac895d1063c",
