      "name": "DeallocateResourcePoolTree",
      "signature": "void DeallocateResourcePoolTree(void * pResourcePool)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deallocates a resource pool tree structure and all its nested components recursively.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameter pResourcePool is non-null\n2. Extract nested pool pointer from offset +0xc in root structure\n3. If nested pool exists, deallocate left subtree node referenced at offset +0x24\n4. If nested pool exists, deallocate right subtree node referenced at offset +0x28\n5. Deallocate the nested pool structure itself using DeallocateResourcePoolElement\n6. Extract child pool pointer from offset +0x8 in root structure\n7. If child pool exists, deallocate it using DeallocateResourcePoolElement\n8. Deallocate the root structure itself using DeallocateResourcePoolElement\n9. Return to caller with stack cleaned up by callee\n\nParameters:\n  pResourcePool (void*): Pointer to root resource pool structure. The structure layout contains:\n    - Offset +0x8: Pointer to child pool element (optional, can be NULL)\n    - Offset +0xc: Pointer to nested resource pool with binary tree structure\n      - Contains left subtree pointer at offset +0x24\n      - Contains right subtree pointer at offset +0x28\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases and Notes:\n  - Handles NULL pointers gracefully at each stage - tests before dereferencing\n  - Implements recursive deallocation through binary tree traversal\n  - Uses __stdcall calling convention with 4-byte parameter (1 DWORD) for cleanup\n  - Magic numbers: Code offsets 0x346, 0x35d, 0x360 passed to deallocation context\n  - Uses LEA instruction to build address context on stack for deallocation calls\n  - Preserves EDI (callee-saved) and uses EDI/ESI for loop/reference preservation\n  - Source file: ..\\\\Source\\\\Fog\\\\Src\\\\Excel\\\\Excel.cpp",
