      "name": "BuildStringIndexTable",
      "signature": "void BuildStringIndexTable(short * pOutputIndices, void * pSearchStrings, void * pEntryArray)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Builds an index table mapping search strings to their positions in an entry array using hash table acceleration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize hash table structures: 1024-byte bucket array (for collision chains) and 3348-byte entry buffer\n2. Validate input: Check that entryArray is not null, count entry records, verify count doesn't exceed limit (0x400)\n3. For each entry in the array, compute string hash: Extract string from searchStrings using ComputeStringHash\n4. Perform hash table collision resolution: Use open addressing with linear probing in hash buckets\n5. For each hash collision, invoke SCompare to determine if strings match exactly\n6. When match found, store the entry index in outputIndices at corresponding string position\n7. If string not found in any entry, call LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown to trigger fatal error\n8. Continue processing all strings until complete or error occurs\n9. Return to caller (ParseFormatStringAndInsertValues) with index table populated\n\nParameters:\n  outputIndices (short*): Output buffer to store matched indices, one short per search string\n  searchStrings (void*): Opaque reference to array/list of strings to search for\n  entryArray (void*): Opaque reference to array of entry records containing searchable strings\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function returns control to caller; does not return a value\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Hash bucket array is indexed by hash % 256 to locate collision chain head\n  Each entry in hashTableEntryBuffer contains reference to entry index and collision chain links\n  Function implements linear probing: if hash[index] occupied, try hash[index+1], hash[index+2], etc.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If entryArray pointer is null, function returns immediately with check at 0x6ff622b4\n  - If entry count exceeds 0x400 (1024), function terminates with error\n  - String mismatch during collision resolution triggers call to SCompare for exact comparison\n  - If search string not found in any entry, LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown called at 0x6ff623f8\n  - Function uses stack-allocated buffers (3348 + 1024 bytes), requires significant stack space",
