      "signature": "void ProcessAndInsertTransformedKey(void * pKeyBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "ProcessAndInsertTransformedKey - Search binary tree for transformed key and insert if not found.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameter (pKeyBuffer must not be null)\n2. Check if transformed key field at offset 0x8 is valid; exit if validation fails\n3. Call SearchBinaryTreeForTransformedKey to search for matching key in tree\n4. If key found or error (return >= 0), exit function\n5. Allocate memory block (0x2c bytes) from memory pool for new tree node\n6. If allocation fails, log error message and exit\n7. Initialize node structure with zero-fill using REP STOSD\n8. Call ApplyCharacterTransformationToBuffer to transform key data\n9. Copy key reference to node at offset 0x20\n10. Insert new node into binary search tree\n11. Increment reference counter at pKeyBuffer+0x0\n12. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pKeyBuffer (void *): Pointer to key data structure containing:\n    - Offset 0x0: Reference count (DWORD, incremented on successful insert)\n    - Offset 0x8: Validation flag (DWORD, must be non-zero to proceed)\n    - Offset 0xC-0x3F: Key data buffer (32 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value; modifies key structure and tree via side effects)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pKeyBuffer is null, logs error and terminates process\n  - If validation field (pKeyBuffer+0x8) is zero, logs error and terminates\n  - If memory allocation fails, logs error and exits\n  - Increments reference counter only after successful tree insertion",
