      "signature": "void ProcessFormatStringData(FormatMetadata * pMetadata, FormatDescriptor * pDescriptors, uint baseOffset, uint validationCheck, uint rowStride)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Parses format descriptor strings and populates data structures with parsed values\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters: validationCheck and rowStride must be non-zero\n2. Build index table of active format positions via BuildStringIndexTable\n3. Scan all format descriptors to detect if complex type processing is needed (types 0x0a-0x12)\n4. If complex formats are detected, execute first pass:\n   a. Iterate through each data row in the source array\n   b. For each format field in the descriptor array:\n      - Skip sentinel values (0x7fff) which mark inactive fields\n      - Parse field-specific data from format string\n      - Process based on descriptor type:\n        * Types 0x0a, 0x0c, 0x0e: Parse numeric value (4-byte buffer), pad with spaces (0x20)\n        * Type 0x0c: Validate parsed value <= 0xff (byte range), store as char\n        * Type 0x0e: Validate parsed value <= 0xffff (word range), store as short\n        * Type 0x10: Copy string to bounded buffer, null-terminate, call InitializeAndInsertBSTNode\n        * Types 0x11-0x12: Copy to temp buffer, call ProcessAndInsertTransformedKey\n   c. Verify each row ends with newline character (0x0a)\n5. Execute second pass processing for remaining format types and validation\n6. Return void\n\nParameters:\npMetadata [FormatMetadata *]: Pointer to metadata structure with fields:\n  offset +0x0: reserved (DWORD)\n  offset +0x4: dataPointer (void *)  - points to source format string array\n  offset +0x8: rowCount (DWORD) - number of rows to process\n  offset +0xc: formatCount (DWORD) - number of format descriptors\n\npDescriptors [FormatDescriptor *]: Pointer to descriptor array (stride = 20 bytes / 5 DWORDs):\n  offset +0x0: type (DWORD) - format type code (0x0a-0x12)\n  offset +0x4: dataOffset (DWORD) - offset into format data\n  offset +0x8: size (DWORD) - max buffer size for string types\n  offset +0xc: valuePointer (void *) - destination storage pointer\n  offset +0x10: searchStructure (void *) - BST or array descriptor pointer\n\nbaseOffset [uint]: Base offset added to all destination pointers before writing\nvalidationCheck [uint]: Validation flag (must be non-zero, calls exit(0xffffffff) if zero)\nrowStride [uint]: Bytes between rows in source data (must be non-zero)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (calls _exit(0xffffffff) on validation failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Sentinel value 0x7fff in formatIndexTable marks inactive format fields to skip\n- Type 0x0a-0x0c: Numeric types require 4-byte value buffer with space padding\n- Type 0x0e: Word type with range validation (0x0000-0xffff)\n- Type 0x10: String type with bounded copy and BST insertion\n- Types 0x11-0x12: Custom data types using transformation function ProcessAndInsertTransformedKey\n- Validation failures trigger error reporting via LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown with error codes:\n  * 0x112: validationCheck is zero\n  * 0x113: rowStride is zero\n  * 0x156: Parsed byte value exceeds 0xff\n  * 0x15a: Parsed word value exceeds 0xffff\n  * 0x185: Row does not end with newline (first pass)\n  * 0x286: Row does not end with newline (second pass)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:187561b12b9133a2fb5b2a6e0cb6c9f4",
