      "name": "DequeueAndProcessPacket",
      "signature": "uint DequeueAndProcessPacket(void * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Dequeues and processes a packet entry from the completion queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock pointer at context offset 0x2c\n2. Call validation function (acquire semantics) with ordinal code 0x53f\n3. Enter critical section to ensure thread-safe access\n4. Load packet entry pointer from context offset 0x74 (queue head)\n5. If packet is non-NULL: Unlink by copying next pointer (offset +4) to queue head\n6. Clear busy flag at offset 0x70 by AND with 0xFFFFFFFB (clears bit 2)\n7. Call validation function (release semantics) with ordinal code 0x552\n8. Leave critical section\n9. If packet exists: Call resource cleanup handler (DeallocateResourcePoolElement)\n10. Return 1 (success/completion status)\n\nParameters:\nImplicit this pointer in EDI - Context structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x2c: CRITICAL_SECTION for queue synchronization\n  - Offset 0x70: Busy/state flags (bit 2 indicates processing state)\n  - Offset 0x74: Pointer to next dequeued packet entry\n\nReturns:\nuint - Always returns 1 (success code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty queue: if (context[0x74] == NULL), no unlink occurs, cleanup skipped\n- Ordinal codes 0x53f (acquire) and 0x552 (release) provide synchronization\n- Packet structure has next pointer at offset +4\n- Bit 2 (0x4) of context[0x70] cleared to mark queue as non-busy\n- Cleanup callback is conditional (only if packet != NULL)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:6fea067fe7da99204f92ce68713ef2f1",
