      "name": "InitiateAsyncWrite",
      "signature": "uint InitiateAsyncWrite(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initiates an asynchronous write operation on a buffered I/O context using WriteFile with OVERLAPPED I/O.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if write buffer exists at context offset +0x74\n2. If buffer empty, return success (no operation needed)\n3. Increment active operation counter at context offset +0x8 using InterlockedIncrement\n4. Load file handle from context offset +0x10\n5. Validate handle against INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE (-1)\n6. If invalid, call GetReturnAddress, log error with LogErrorAndShutdown, and exit\n7. Calculate buffer pointer and size (first DWORD is size, data starts at +8)\n8. Call WriteFile API with OVERLAPPED structure at context offset +0x5c\n9. Get last error code via GetLastError\n10. If WriteFile succeeded (EAX != 0):\n    - If error is not ERROR_IO_PENDING (0x3e5), return success\n    - If error is ERROR_IO_PENDING, set pending flag and return success\n11. If WriteFile failed (EAX == 0):\n    - If error is ERROR_IO_PENDING (0x3e5), set pending flag and return success\n    - If error is not IO_PENDING, call cleanup handlers and return failure\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EDI: Pointer to I/O context structure (IOContextBlock)\n  +0x08: LONG counter for active I/O operations (InterlockedIncrement target)\n  +0x10: HANDLE to file/pipe for WriteFile calls\n  +0x5c: OVERLAPPED structure for async I/O completion tracking\n  +0x70: DWORD flags field (bit 2 set when IO_PENDING operation exists)\n  +0x74: Pointer to write buffer containing size header\n\nReturns:\n1 (EAX=1) - Write operation initiated successfully or IO_PENDING flag set\n0 (EAX=0) - Fatal error occurred, cleanup handlers called\n\nSpecial Cases:\nERROR_IO_PENDING (0x3e5): Expected return value for async writes, sets pending flag\nINVALID_HANDLE_VALUE (-1): Fatal condition triggering application shutdown\nWriteFile Success with IO_PENDING: Asynchronous completion, pending flag set\nWriteFile Failure with IO_PENDING: Normal async completion, treated as success\n\nStructure Layout:\nIOContextBlock structure (relevant fields):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name          Type        Description\n  +0x08   4     dwActiveOpsCounter  LONG        InterlockedIncrement counter\n  +0x10   4     hFileHandle         HANDLE      File/pipe handle for WriteFile\n  +0x5c   32    overlappedIo        OVERLAPPED  Async I/O status and completion event\n  +0x70   4     dwFlags             DWORD       Operational flags (bit 2=IO_PENDING)\n  +0x74   4     pWriteBuffer        void*       Pointer to buffer [size][...data...]",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:4e2690e85ab304c00638f2a19c048f8a",
