      "name": "SendSocketData",
      "signature": "uint SendSocketData(void * this, uint * param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Sends network socket data with thread-safe queuing and error handling.\n\nThis function transmits data packets through an active socket connection while\nmaintaining thread safety through critical section synchronization. It supports\npartial sends by automatically queueing remaining bytes for asynchronous\ntransmission, and gracefully handles socket errors including the non-fatal\nWSAEWOULDBLOCK condition.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock from context at offset +0x2c for thread safety\n2. Get current timestamp via MeasureElapsedTimeInSeconds() and store at context offset +0xa0\n3. Check socket state flag at context offset +0x1d (0 = enabled, non-zero = disabled)\n4. If socket disabled (offset +0x1d non-zero):\n   - Call QueueSocketData() to buffer all bytes for later transmission\n   - Exit with success (return 1)\n5. If socket enabled (offset +0x1d is 0):\n   - Check socket handle validity at context offset +0x10 (compare with -1)\n   - If invalid handle (-1): decrement reference count, cleanup, return 0\n   - If valid: call WinSock send() with socket descriptor at offset +0x10\n6. Handle send() result:\n   - If send returns -1 (error): check error code via WSAGetLastError()\n   - If error is WSAEWOULDBLOCK (0x2733): queue remaining bytes and return 1\n   - If any other error: cleanup via CloseSocketEntryAndCleanup(), return 0\n7. If send returned 0-N bytes < bufferSize (partial send):\n   - Queue remaining bytes (pBuffer + bytesTransferred) via QueueSocketData()\n   - Call WriteDataAsync() to trigger immediate processing\n8. Release critical section lock via LeaveCriticalSection()\n9. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- this: Context/connection object pointer (implicit ECX in __thiscall)\n  Structure offsets used: +0x2c (critical section), +0xa0 (timestamp),\n  +0x1d (socket state flag), +0x10 (socket handle), +0x8 (unknown field)\n- pBuffer: Data buffer containing network packet bytes to transmit\n- bufferSize: Number of bytes in pBuffer to send\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Send succeeded or data queued for later transmission\n- 0: Socket error or handle invalid, connection cleanup initiated\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- WSAEWOULDBLOCK (0x2733): Network buffer full; not an error; data queued\n- Partial sends: When send() returns fewer bytes than requested, remaining\n  bytes automatically queued for asynchronous transmission\n- Socket disabled: When offset +0x1d is non-zero, queues all data without\n  attempting immediate transmission\n- Socket invalid (-1): Triggers immediate connection cleanup and returns 0\n- Reference counting: When socket invalid and refCount hits 0, removes entry\n  from hash tables and initiates full cleanup sequence",
