      "name": "CloseThreadHandlesAndWait",
      "signature": "void CloseThreadHandlesAndWait(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Closes all worker thread handles and waits for their completion with synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock at ESI+0x854 to protect handle access\n2. Load and collect valid handles from multiple context structure fields:\n   - Primary handle from ESI+0xbd8 (unconditional)\n   - Secondary handle from ESI+0xbdc (if non-null)\n   - Tertiary handle from ESI+0xbe0 (if non-null)\n   - Quaternary handle from ESI+0xbe4 (if non-null)\n   - Optional handles from ESI+0xc1c, ESI+0xc20, ESI+0xc24, ESI+0xc28 (if feature flag ESI+0xc18 is set)\n3. Set initialization status flags (value 1) at multiple offsets to signal readiness:\n   - ESI+0xbf8, ESI+0xc3c, ESI+0xbfc, ESI+0xc00, ESI+0xc40, ESI+0xc44, ESI+0xc04, ESI+0xc48\n4. Leave critical section to allow worker threads to proceed\n5. If handles were collected (count > 0), wait for all handles with WaitForMultipleObjects (bWaitAll=1, timeout=1000ms)\n6. Enter close loop: iterate 4 times processing handle groups\n   - For each iteration, close primary handle at [EDI] if non-null, then clear both EDI+0 and EDI+0x10\n   - If feature flag ESI+0xc18 is set, close optional handle at [EDI+0x44] if non-null, then clear both EDI+0x44 and EDI+0x54\n   - Move to next group: add 4 to EDI for next iteration\n7. Return after all handles closed\n\nParameters:\nImplicit context pointer in ESI register - contains:\n  - Critical section at offset 0x854 for thread synchronization\n  - Handle references at multiple offsets (0xbd8, 0xbdc, 0xbe0, 0xbe4, 0xc1c, 0xc20, 0xc24, 0xc28)\n  - Status/initialization flags at offsets 0xbf8, 0xc3c, 0xbfc, 0xc00, 0xc40, 0xc44, 0xc04, 0xc48\n  - Feature flag at offset 0xc18 enabling collection of optional handles\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. All handles are closed and memory is cleaned up.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Feature flag at ESI+0xc18 gates collection and closing of optional handles (0xc1c, 0xc20, 0xc24, 0xc28)\n- Handle pointers are cleared after closing (dual clears at offset and offset+0x10)\n- Optional handles cleared at dual locations offset and offset+0x10 from EDI+0x44\n- WaitForMultipleObjects timeout is 0x3e8 (1000 milliseconds)\n- Loop processes exactly 4 handle groups with stride of 4 bytes between iterations\n- If no handles are collected, WaitForMultipleObjects is skipped\n- Critical section is released before waiting to prevent deadlock with worker threads\n\nContext Structure Fields Used:\nHandle Array Base: ESI+0xbd8 (primary handles)\nOptional Handle Base: ESI+0xc1c (conditional, if feature enabled)\nFeature Flag: ESI+0xc18 (enables optional handle collection)\nStatus Flags: ESI+0xbf8, 0xc3c, 0xbfc, 0xc00, 0xc40, 0xc44, 0xc04, 0xc48\nCritical Section: ESI+0x854",
