      "name": "ProcessActiveSlots",
      "signature": "int ProcessActiveSlots(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Process all active completion status slots in the context.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load context processing status flag from offset +0xc18\\n2. If status is non-zero (context busy), exit immediately with return value 1\\n3. Initialize slot index to 0 and slot pointer to context+0xb90 (slot array base)\\n4. Loop through all 4 slots (0-3):\\n   a. Compare current slot value with -1 (empty sentinel)\\n   b. If slot value equals -1, skip to next slot (jump to loop_increment)\\n   c. If slot is active (non-empty), push slot index to stack\\n   d. Load context and stack frame parameters\\n   e. Call ProcessCompletionStatusWithTimeout to process the slot\\n   f. Increment slot index and advance pointer by 4 bytes (one dword)\\n   g. Compare index with 4 (loop bound check)\\n   h. Jump back to loop_check_slot_valid if index < 4\\n5. Pop callee-saved registers and return 1 (success)\\n\\nParameters:\\nImplicit Context Pointer in EBX\\n- Base pointer to context structure containing slots at offset +0xb90\\n\\nReturns:\\nint - Always returns 1 (success); early exit also returns 1 if context is busy\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Early exit at offset +0xc18: If context status is non-zero, skip all slot processing\\n- Empty slot sentinel: Slots marked with value -1 are skipped\\n- Fixed slot count: Exactly 4 slots are processed per context\\n- Slot stride: Each slot occupies 4 bytes (dword)\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nContext structure (implicit EBX):\\nOffset    Size    Field               Type        Description\\n+0xb90    4       slot[0]             dword       First completion slot value\\n+0xb94    4       slot[1]             dword       Second completion slot value\\n+0xb98    4       slot[2]             dword       Third completion slot value\\n+0xb9c    4       slot[3]             dword       Fourth completion slot value\\n+0xc18    4       processingStatus    dword       Status flag (0=process, non-0=busy)",
