      "name": "IsNTBasedOS",
      "signature": "bool IsNTBasedOS(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Detects if the operating system is NT-based\n\nSummary: Determines whether the current system is running an NT-based Windows OS\n(Windows NT/2000/XP/Vista/7/8/10) by calling GetVersionExA and checking if the\nplatform ID equals 2.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate and zero-initialize OSVERSIONINFOA structure (148 bytes)\n2. Set dwOSVersionInfoSize field to 0x94 (148 bytes)\n3. Call GetVersionExA to populate structure with OS info\n4. Return false if GetVersionExA fails\n5. Load dwPlatformId field from structure\n6. Return true if platform ID equals 2 (NT-based), false otherwise\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nbool - true if NT-based system, false otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\nGetVersionExA failure returns false immediately. Platform ID 2 indicates NT-based.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
