      "name": "InitializeAndQueryMemoryStatus",
      "signature": "void InitializeAndQueryMemoryStatus(LPMEMORYSTATUS pMemStatus)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initializes and populates a Windows MEMORYSTATUS structure with system memory information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer to MEMORYSTATUS structure from stack parameter\n2. Initialize ECX register to zero for zeroing fields\n3. Zero all eight DWORD fields in the structure (dwLength, dwMemoryLoad, dwTotalPhys, dwAvailPhys, dwTotalPageFile, dwAvailPageFile, dwTotalVirtual, dwAvailVirtual)\n4. Set dwLength field to 0x20 (32 bytes - sizeof MEMORYSTATUS structure)\n5. Push structure pointer as parameter for GlobalMemoryStatus API call\n6. Call Windows GlobalMemoryStatus API to populate structure with current system memory statistics\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npMemStatus: Pointer to MEMORYSTATUS structure to be initialized and populated with system memory data\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Structure is populated in-place; no return value used by caller\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The MEMORYSTATUS structure must be at least 32 bytes to hold all fields\n- The dwLength field MUST be set to 0x20 (32) before calling GlobalMemoryStatus or the API call will fail\n- GlobalMemoryStatus modifies all structure fields directly through the pointer parameter\n- All fields are zeroed first before being populated by the API to ensure clean state\n\nStructure Layout (MEMORYSTATUS):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type   Description\n0x0     4     dwLength             DWORD  Structure size (must be 0x20)\n0x4     4     dwMemoryLoad         DWORD  Percentage of memory in use (0-100)\n0x8     4     dwTotalPhys          DWORD  Total physical RAM in bytes\n0xC     4     dwAvailPhys          DWORD  Available physical RAM in bytes\n0x10    4     dwTotalPageFile      DWORD  Total page file size in bytes\n0x14    4     dwAvailPageFile      DWORD  Available page file in bytes\n0x18    4     dwTotalVirtual       DWORD  Total virtual memory in bytes\n0x1C    4     dwAvailVirtual       DWORD  Available virtual memory in bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
