      "name": "InitializeGameValidation",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameValidation(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game validation and security checks on startup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize critical section for synchronization (g_GameInitializationCriticalSection at 0x6ff816d8)\n2. Set up validation data structure with magic number sentinel value 0x29a\n3. Call atomic compare-and-swap to populate initial validation data with system state\n4. Call second validation function to verify the data structure integrity\n5. Check if validation result matches magic number 0x29a AND secondary check passes\n6. On success: capture current Unix timestamp and system tick count, store in g_ValidationTimestampData\n7. On failure: log error with code 0x3c, cleanup resources, terminate process with exit code -1\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters and operates on global validation structures\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function either returns normally on validation success or terminates process on failure via _exit(-1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x29a is sentinel value used to detect data corruption during validation\n- Function contains no-return path on validation failure (calls _exit which never returns)\n- Critical section protects game initialization state from concurrent modification\n- Error code 0x3c indicates unrecoverable validation failure requiring immediate termination\n- Functions called: InitializeCriticalSection, CompareAndSwap64Atomic, ConvertFileTimeToUnixTime32, GetTickCount, GetReturnAddress, WSACleanup, LogErrorAndShutdown, ShutdownResourcesAndExit, _exit\n\nStructure Layout:\nValidation Data Structure (local, 32 bytes on stack):\nOffset | Size | Field Name              | Type     | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwInitData1             | DWORD    | First initialization data element\n0x04   | 4    | dwValidationResult      | DWORD    | Result from validation check (0x29a = success)\n0x08   | 4    | iSecondValidationCheck  | int      | Secondary validation result (0 = success)\n0x0C   | 4    | dwInitData2             | DWORD    | Second initialization data element\n0x10   | 4    | dwMagicValidationNumber | DWORD    | Magic sentinel 0x29a for corruption detection\n0x14   | 4    | dwInitData4             | DWORD    | Fourth initialization data element\n0x18   | 4    | dwCurrentUnixTime       | DWORD    | Current time as Unix timestamp (32-bit)\n0x1C   | 4    | dwSystemTickCount       | DWORD    | System tick count from GetTickCount\nTotal: 32 bytes",
