      "signature": "int InitializeNetworkServerSocket(ushort serverPort)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a TCP server socket for network communication and launches\nthe network acceptance thread.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set network mode flag (0x884) to active (1)\n2. Create TCP socket (AF_INET=2, SOCK_STREAM=1, IPPROTO_TCP=0)\n3. Return failure (0) if socket creation fails\n4. Store socket handle in game context at offset 0xb90\n5. Configure TCP_NODELAY option (disable Nagle buffering for responsiveness)\n6. Configure SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE (prevents socket address reuse conflicts)\n7. Configure SO_REUSEADDR (allows socket to bind after restart)\n8. Set non-blocking mode via FIONBIO ioctl (0x8004667e)\n9. Initialize sockaddr_in structure with AF_INET (2) family\n10. Zero all address bytes (binds to INADDR_ANY = 0.0.0.0)\n11. Convert server port to network byte order via htons()\n12. Store port in sockaddr_in.sin_port (network byte order)\n13. Store port in game context at offset 0xba0\n14. Bind socket to INADDR_ANY:serverPort\n15. Return failure (0) if bind fails\n16. Call ListenOnSocket with backlog of 25 connections\n17. Close socket and return failure (0) if listen fails\n18. Create auto-reset event for thread synchronization\n19. Store event handle in game context at offset 0xbd4\n20. Create network acceptance thread (ServerConnectionHandlerThread)\n21. Store thread handle in game context at offset 0xbd8\n22. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  serverPort (ushort): Port number for server socket to listen on\n\nReturns:\n  1 = Success (socket initialized, thread created)\n  0 = Failure (socket creation, bind, or listen failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic values: 0x19 (25) is backlog queue size, 0x8004667e is FIONBIO ioctl\n  EDI register contains implicit game context pointer (calling convention)\n  Socket options configured in specific order for network initialization\n  Offset 0x884 marks network mode as active\n  Thread is launched with game context (EDI) as parameter\n\nStructure Layout (Game Context):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Type      Description\n  0x884   4     networkModeActive   dword     1=network active, 0=inactive\n  0xb90   4     serverSocket        SOCKET    TCP server socket handle\n  0xba0   2     serverPort          ushort    Server port (host byte order)\n  0xbd4   4     threadEvent         HANDLE    Auto-reset event for thread sync\n  0xbd8   4     connectionThread    HANDLE    Network acceptance thread handle\n  0xbe8   4     threadId            dword     Thread ID output location",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:04be1cb0309df04504b4c514e33c84af",
