      "name": "ValidateConnectionObject",
      "signature": "uint ValidateConnectionObject(void * pConnectionObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates a connection object and returns its connection state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if connection object pointer is NULL (passed in ECX)\n2. If NULL, retrieve calling address, cleanup sockets via WSACleanup\n3. Log error code 0x276 (NULL pointer validation failure) with source location\n4. Shutdown resources and exit with code -1\n5. If pointer valid, load magic type marker from object offset +0x48\n6. AND marker with 0xfffffff0 to isolate type identifier bits\n7. Compare masked marker against expected validation value 0x41737960\n8. If marker matches, jump to return sequence\n9. If marker mismatch, retrieve calling address and cleanup sockets\n10. Log error code 0x277 (invalid marker validation failure) with source location\n11. Shutdown resources and exit with code -1\n12. Load connection state value from object offset +0x40 into EAX\n13. Restore ESI register and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pConnectionObject (ECX): Pointer to connection structure containing:\n  - Offset +0x40: Connection state value (uint, returned to caller)\n  - Offset +0x48: Magic type marker (must equal 0x41737960 when masked with 0xfffffff0)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Connection state value loaded from pConnectionObject+0x40\n- Does not return on validation failure (calls _exit with code -1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer parameter triggers error code 0x276 and immediate shutdown\n- Corrupted magic marker (not matching 0x41737960) triggers error code 0x277\n- Both error paths log source location info and call WSACleanup before exit\n- Function signature uses __fastcall: first parameter in ECX, callee cleanup\n- EBP not used; ESI saved/restored for use as temp storage",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
