      "name": "ManageResourceRefCount",
      "signature": "void ManageResourceRefCount(int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Manages a reference-counted cleanup chain for resource lifecycle management.\nThis function implements a thread-safe reference counting mechanism that queues resource cleanup operations\nwhen the reference count reaches zero. It supports both increment (to acquire a reference) and decrement\n(to release a reference) operations through the bIncrementFlag parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current reference count from g_dwResourceRefCount\n2. If bIncrementFlag is non-zero: increment refCount and return immediately (fast path for acquisitions)\n3. If bIncrementFlag is zero: begin decrement path\n4. Decrement refCount atomically\n5. If refCount becomes zero: process cleanup chain\n   a. Load chain head pointer from g_pResourceCleanupChainHead\n   b. Iterate through intrusive linked list starting at chain head:\n      - Load next pointer from chain element offset +0x50\n      - Compare pending event value (offset +0x44) with applied value (offset +0x4c)\n      - If values differ: signal Windows event handle at offset +0x3c via SetEventWrapper\n      - Clear bit 3 in status flags at offset +0x48 (indicates cleanup complete)\n      - Zero out pending event value at offset +0x4c\n      - Zero out next pointer at offset +0x50\n      - Move to next chain element\n   c. Reset chain head pointer to NULL after processing all elements\n6. If refCount becomes negative: fatal error path\n   a. Retrieve return address via GetReturnAddress() for logging\n   b. Call WSACleanup() for socket cleanup\n   c. Invoke LogErrorAndShutdown with error code 6 and source location 0x216\n   d. Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit()\n   e. Terminate process with _exit(-1)\n\nParameters:\n  bIncrementFlag (ECX): If non-zero, increment reference count; if zero, decrement and check for cleanup\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies global state (reference count and cleanup chain). On fatal error (refCount < 0),\n  terminates the process via _exit(-1) and never returns.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - bIncrementFlag != 0: Fast acquisition path, bypasses all decrement logic\n  - refCount == 0: Triggers full cleanup chain processing (expensive)\n  - refCount < 0: Indicates logic error or race condition, causes fatal shutdown\n  - Intrusive linked list: Each chain element is embedded in larger structure, no separate nodes\n  - Atomic event signaling: Only signals if pending value differs from applied value\n  - Status flags: Bit 3 is cleared during cleanup to mark elements as processed\n\nStructure Layout (Resource Cleanup Chain Element):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name         Type      Description\n  +0x3c   4     hEventHandle       HANDLE    Windows event handle for notifying cleanup completion\n  +0x44   4     dwPendingValue     uint      Pending event notification value (newly queued)\n  +0x48   4     dwStatusFlags      uint      Status bitfield (bit 3 = needs cleanup signal)\n  +0x4c   4     dwAppliedValue     uint      Last applied event notification value\n  +0x50   4     pNextElement       pointer   Pointer to next chain element (0 = end of chain)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:2cb3a92f00444f2f9592ae3ef2897257",
