      "name": "ValidateContextAndWaitHandle",
      "signature": "uint ValidateContextAndWaitHandle(void * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates context structure integrity and waits for associated handle with non-blocking semantics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pContext parameter is NULL; return 0 immediately if null pointer detected\n2. Load context state/flags field from memory offset +0x48 (4-byte DWORD)\n3. Verify context integrity by checking signature bits: (state & 0xfffffff0) == 0x41737960\n4. If signature validation fails: retrieve return address for debugging, cleanup Windows sockets via WSACleanup(), log critical error using LogErrorAndShutdown() with error code 6 and source location 0x1c9, shutdown all resources via ShutdownResourcesAndExit(), and terminate entire process with exit code -1 (0xffffffff) - this indicates critical context corruption\n5. Check if handle is already signaled by testing state LSB: (state & 1) == 1\n6. If handle not yet signaled: load handle pointer from context offset +0x38, dereference pointer to get actual HANDLE value, call WaitForSingleObject() with timeout=0 for non-blocking check\n7. If WaitForSingleObject() returns WAIT_OBJECT_0 (result == 0): call CleanupContextResourceAndReset() to perform additional completion processing\n8. Load final signaled state flag from context offset +0x48, mask LSB to extract handle signal status\n9. Return uint value: non-zero (1) if handle is signaled, zero (0) if not yet signaled\n\nParameters:\npContext (ECX register, __fastcall): void * pointer to context structure containing handle and state information. Offset +0x38 contains HANDLE * (pointer to handle), Offset +0x48 contains DWORD state field with magic sentinel 0x41737960 in upper bits and signaled indicator in LSB.\n\nReturns:\nuint - Handle signaled state indicator. Returns 0x1 if handle is signaled, 0x0 if not yet signaled. Returns 0 for NULL pContext.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:4e2690e85ab304c00638f2a19c048f8a",
