      "name": "CopyValidatedDataBuffer",
      "signature": "uint CopyValidatedDataBuffer(void * pSourceData, void * pDestBuffer, uint * pSizeOut, uint * pSpaceRemaining)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates and copies a sized data buffer with space checking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output size parameter to 0\n2. Load item count from pSourceData[1]\n3. Calculate required size as (itemCount * 12) + 8 bytes\n4. Compare required size against available space in pSpaceRemaining\n5. If required size exceeds available space, return error code 0xE and exit\n6. Store calculated required size in pSizeOut output parameter\n7. Decrement pSpaceRemaining by the bytes that will be copied\n8. Copy requiredSize bytes from pSourceData to pDestBuffer:\n   a. Shift requiredSize right by 2 to get dword count\n   b. Use MOVSD.REP to copy full dwords (4-byte units)\n   c. Mask lowest 2 bits of requiredSize for remaining byte count\n   d. Use MOVSB.REP to copy remaining 0-3 bytes individually\n9. Return success code 0\n\nParameters:\npSourceData: Pointer to source data structure. The value at offset +4 contains\n             the item count which determines total size as (count * 12) + 8.\npDestBuffer: Pointer to destination buffer where data will be copied.\n             Must have at least requiredSize bytes available.\npSizeOut: Output parameter pointer. Receives the total number of bytes copied.\npSpaceRemaining: Input/output parameter pointer. On entry, contains available\n                 space in destination. On success, decremented by bytes copied.\n\nReturns:\n0 (success) if copy completed and space was sufficient\n0xE (14, error) if pSpaceRemaining contained insufficient space for copy\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Size calculation: Each item is 12 bytes (0xC), plus 8-byte header = 0xC*count + 8\n- MOVSD copies complete 32-bit dwords for efficiency\n- MOVSB handles remaining 1-3 bytes after dword copy completes\n- Function uses __fastcall convention with callee cleanup (RET 0x8)\n- Error path immediately returns 0xE without modifying destination\n- Success path completes copy operation and all side effects",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:68373ec2905755e9db585387c5c8d83b",
