      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Virtual method table no-operation stub.\n\nThis function serves as a no-op placeholder in virtual method tables (vtables). It is\nused when a derived class does not override a virtual method, or when an interface\nmethod has no action required.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Simply return immediately with stack cleanup for 7 parameters (0x1c = 28 bytes)\n\nParameters:\nNone. Function signature includes 7 implicit parameters cleaned by __stdcall, but\nthey are not used.\n\nReturns:\nNo meaningful return value. Function performs no operations and returns immediately.\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis stub is referenced from vtable entries at address 0x6ff7dcc8. The RET 0x1c\ninstruction cleans 28 bytes (7 DWORD parameters) from the stack, indicating this\nfunction conforms to the __stdcall calling convention with 7 parameters.",
