      "name": "AppendPathComponentWithNewline",
      "signature": "void AppendPathComponentWithNewline(char * pPathBuffer, char * pComponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Appends a path component followed by a newline to a destination buffer.\n\nThis is a convenience wrapper around AppendPathComponent that automatically appends\na newline sequence after each path component, commonly used for log file formatting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call AppendPathComponent to append pComponent string to pPathBuffer with max length 0x7fffffff\n2. Call AppendPathComponent again to append newline sequence from szNewlineSequence to pPathBuffer\n3. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npPathBuffer (ECX): Pointer to destination character buffer where components are appended\npComponent (EDX): Pointer to null-terminated source string containing path component to append\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No explicit return value; modifies pPathBuffer in-place by appending strings\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Max append length set to 0x7fffffff (2GB), effectively unlimited for practical use\n- Always appends \"\\r\n\" (carriage return + line feed) after each component for log formatting\n- Caller must ensure pPathBuffer has sufficient space for both component and newline strings\n- No bounds checking performed; buffer overflow possible if caller doesn't allocate adequate space\n- Called by BuildDiabloLogHeader for constructing diagnostic log headers",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:433c536f7cabba714b1c8a2bbb677fe7",
