      "name": "TranslateExceptionCodeToMessage",
      "signature": "void TranslateExceptionCodeToMessage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Translates Windows exception and status codes to human-readable error message strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 20-byte stack buffer with default \"Unknown Exception\" message copy\n2. Check if exception code >= 0xc000008e (upper range floating-point exceptions):\n   - If yes: jump to upper_range_switch for floating-point exception lookup\n   - If no: continue to lower range checks\n3. Check if code == 0xc000008d (FLT_DENORMAL_OPERAND):\n   - If exact match: copy FLT_DENORMAL_OPERAND string and return\n   - Otherwise: continue to boundary check\n4. Check if code < 0xc0000007 (lower range):\n   - 0xc0000006: IN_PAGE_ERROR\n   - 0x80000003: BREAKPOINT\n   - 0x80000001: GUARD_PAGE\n   - 0x80000002: DATATYPE_MISALIGNMENT\n   - 0x80000004: SINGLE_STEP\n   - 0xc0000005: ACCESS_VIOLATION\n5. If code >= 0xc0000007 (middle range switch):\n   - 0xc0000008: INVALID_HANDLE\n   - 0xc000001d: ILLEGAL_INSTRUCTION\n   - 0xc0000025: NONCONTINUABLE_EXCEPTION\n   - 0xc0000026: INVALID_DISPOSITION\n   - 0xc000008c: ARRAY_BOUNDS_EXCEEDED\n6. If code >= 0xc000008e (upper range switch):\n   - 0xc000008e-0xc0000093: Floating-point exception variants (divide by zero, underflow, overflow, etc.)\n   - 0xc0000094-0xc0000096: Integer exception variants (divide by zero, overflow, privileged instruction)\n   - 0xc00000fd: STACK_OVERFLOW\n7. If no exact match found: attempt FormatMessageA lookup in NTDLL.DLL system messages\n8. If FormatMessageA fails (returns 0): copy default stack buffer message to output\n9. Return with output buffer filled with error message string\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT REGISTER EAX: Exception code (uint) - Windows NTSTATUS or SEH exception code value\nIMPLICIT REGISTER EBX: Pointer to output buffer (char*) - Destination for error message string\nIMPLICIT REGISTER EDI: Buffer size (size_t) - Maximum number of bytes to write\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Output buffer contains null-terminated error message string (or truncated if buffer too small)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Boundary magic number 0xc000008e separates mid-range from upper-range exceptions\n- Boundary magic number 0xc0000007 separates low-level debug exceptions from status codes\n- Boundary magic number 0x80000004 separates low debug exceptions (0x80000001-0x80000003) from others\n- Stack buffer contains pre-copied default message (18 bytes \"Unknown Exception\" + null + padding)\n- FormatMessageA flags 0xa00 = FORMAT_MESSAGE_FROM_SYSTEM | FORMAT_MESSAGE_ALLOCATE_BUFFER\n- Each matched case calls _strncpy with buffer size to copy predefined exception string\n- Function uses register-based calling convention (EAX, EBX, EDI implicit parameters)",
