      "name": "FormatStringBuffer",
      "signature": "char * FormatStringBuffer(char * szOutputBuffer, char * szFormatString)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Formats a string with variable arguments into a buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load output buffer pointer from stack parameter at [ESP + 0x8]\n2. Load format string pointer from stack parameter at [ESP + 0xC]\n3. Calculate pointer to variable arguments starting at [ESP + 0x10]\n4. Call _vsprintf to perform string formatting with the three parameters\n5. Return the output buffer pointer in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  szOutputBuffer: Pointer to destination buffer for formatted string output\n  szFormatString: Pointer to null-terminated format string with format specifiers (%, d, s, etc.)\n  ...: Variable number of arguments matching the format specifiers in szFormatString\n\nReturns:\n  char*: Pointer to szOutputBuffer (the input output buffer), enabling chaining\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Buffer overflow: Caller is responsible for allocating sufficient buffer space to hold formatted output\n  Format string vulnerabilities: Caller must ensure szFormatString is trusted, not user-controlled\n  Variadic arguments: Arguments on stack must match format specifiers in order and type\n  \nStructure Layout:\n  This function accesses the following stack frame:\n  Offset  Size  Purpose\n  ------  ----  -------\n  +0x04   0x04  Return address\n  +0x08   0x04  szOutputBuffer parameter\n  +0x0C   0x04  szFormatString parameter\n  +0x10   ...   Variable arguments (args[0], args[1], etc.)",
