      "name": "DeleteHistoricalFiles",
      "signature": "void DeleteHistoricalFiles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deletes crash dump files from the previous 10 days based on system date calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current system time via GetLocalTime() into SYSTEMTIME structure\n2. Initialize 260-byte file path buffer to empty string\n3. Call ExtractModuleDirectory() to retrieve module directory path\n4. If extraction successful:\n   - Append pszFilePathComponent to file path using AppendPathComponent()\n   - Create necessary directory structure via CreateDirectoryPathRecursive()\n5. Extract SYSTEMTIME structure fields: wDay, wYear, wMonth into stack variables\n6. Call CalculateDateOffsetValue() to compute offset for current date\n7. Loop 10 times:\n   - Call CalculateJulianDayNumber() to adjust date values backward by one day\n   - Format filename using sprintf() with format \"%s_%s_%02d_%02d_%02d.txt\"\n     (szFilePath, pszFilePathComponent, year%100, month, day)\n   - Attempt DeleteFileA() on formatted filename\n8. Return (callee cleanup: RET 0x4)\n\nParameters:\n  pszFilePathComponent: Pointer to path component string to append to base file path\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - File path buffer is 260 bytes (0x104) - insufficient for very long paths\n  - Year is converted to 2-digit format via modulo 100 (2000->00, 2025->25)\n  - Loop counter decremented twice per iteration (EDI and ESI both decremented at 0x6ff60967-0x6ff60968)\n  - Exactly 10 iterations delete 10 consecutive days of files\n  - DeleteFileA() silently succeeds if file exists, fails silently if missing\n  - Format string at 0x6ff76f4c: \"%s%s%02d%02d%02d.txt\"\n\nStructure Layout (SYSTEMTIME):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name    Type      Description\n  +0x00   WORD  wYear         uint16    4-digit year\n  +0x02   WORD  wMonth        uint16    Month (1-12)\n  +0x04   WORD  wDayOfWeek    uint16    Day of week (0=Sunday)\n  +0x06   WORD  wDay          uint16    Day of month (1-31)\n  +0x08   WORD  wHour         uint16    Hour (0-23)\n  +0x0a   WORD  wMinute       uint16    Minute (0-59)\n  +0x0c   WORD  wSecond       uint16    Second (0-59)\n  +0x0e   WORD  wMilliseconds uint16    Milliseconds (0-999)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
