      "name": "InitializeGameNetworking",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameNetworking(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "InitializeGameNetworking - Initialize network infrastructure and build game logging header\n\nPurpose:\nSets up three network connections and prepares the logging header infrastructure for the game engine.\nThis function serves as the network initialization entry point that establishes communication channels\nbefore game session data can be processed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push first network connection handle (0x6ff768ec) onto stack as parameter\n2. Push second parameter (same handle) for InitializeNetworkConnection\n3. Call InitializeNetworkConnection to initialize first connection\n4. Push first network connection handle again as parameter\n5. Push second parameter for second initialization\n6. Call InitializeNetworkConnection to initialize second connection\n7. Push separator string (0x6ff78a14 \"------\") as parameter\n8. Push connection handle for third initialization\n9. Call InitializeNetworkConnection to initialize third connection\n10. Clean up stack by adding 0x18 (24 bytes) to ESP for three 2-parameter calls\n11. Load log header data address (0x6ff5fd70) into EDX register\n12. Clear ECX register to zero for initialization flag\n13. Perform tail call to BuildDiabloLogHeader to construct the logging header\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters (__stdcall calling convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return normally; control transfers to BuildDiabloLogHeader\n       via unconditional JMP instruction (tail call optimization)\n\nGlobal Data Used:\n- g_pNetworkConnectionHandle (0x6ff768ec): Network connection handle used in initialization\n- szLogHeaderSeparator (0x6ff78a14): Separator string for log header formatting\n- g_LogHeaderData (0x6ff5fd70): Log header structure pointer passed to BuildDiabloLogHeader\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses tail call optimization (JMP instead of CALL/RET) to BuildDiabloLogHeader\n- All three InitializeNetworkConnection calls use 2-parameter __cdecl calling convention\n- EDX is pre-loaded with log header address before tail call\n- ECX is cleared to zero for use by BuildDiabloLogHeader\n- No return instruction present; control flow continues to BuildDiabloLogHeader at 0x6ff60660",
