      "name": "LogErrorContextAndInitiateShutdown",
      "signature": "void LogErrorContextAndInitiateShutdown(void * pErrorContext, void * pThreadContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Logs error context and thread state before application shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize error handler state with stack bytes error label via InitializeNetworkConnection\n2. Queue error context log message containing error context pointer with 0x1000-byte buffer\n3. Initialize code handler state with code bytes error label via InitializeNetworkConnection\n4. Queue thread context log message containing thread context pointer with 0x20-byte buffer\n5. Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit to terminate application and release resources\n6. Return to caller with callee cleanup of 8 bytes for 2 parameters\n\nParameters:\n- pErrorContext (void*): Pointer to exception/error context structure containing error details\n- pThreadContext (void*): Pointer to thread context structure containing thread state and registers\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function does not return normally; initiates application shutdown\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x1000 (4096): Size in bytes of error context buffer for logging\n- Magic number 0x20 (32): Size in bytes of thread context buffer for logging\n- Function always triggers application termination via ShutdownResourcesAndExit\n- Both log messages use caller-provided context pointers passed as parameters\n- Function called from error/exception handlers when critical errors occur (codes 2,5,6,7,10)\n\nGlobal Data Used:\n- g_dwErrorHandlerState (0x6ff768ec): Error handler global state variable\n- szStackBytesErrorLabel (0x6ff78720): String label for error context logging\n- szCodeBytesErrorLabel (0x6ff78714): String label for thread context logging",
