      "name": "TerminateApplicationOnFatalError",
      "signature": "void TerminateApplicationOnFatalError(int nErrorCode, int nUnused1, int nUnused2, int nErrorContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initiates application shutdown after fatal error with socket cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call WSACleanup() to release all Windows Socket API resources\n2. Call LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown() to log error code and context\n3. Transfer control to shutdown_handler_entry via unconditional JMP\n4. Shutdown handler waits for worker threads and closes file handles\n\nParameters:\nerrorCode (EAX): Error/status code indicating reason for shutdown\nunused1 (EDX): Unused parameter (legacy calling convention requirement)\nunused2: Unused parameter (legacy calling convention requirement)\nerrorContext: Additional error context for diagnostic logging\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function never returns; unconditional JMP to shutdown handler ensures control never reaches caller\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __cdecl calling convention with 4 parameters on stack\n- Final JMP instead of RET bypasses normal function epilogue\n- All parameters loaded via MOV from ESP offsets before PUSH/CALL sequence\n- WSACleanup must execute first to ensure sockets released before exit\n- Global szUnrecoverableErrorMessage string used for error reporting\n- Global g_szErrorMessageSourceLocationTable passed to error logger\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset   Size   Description\n0x0      4      Return address (pushed by CALL prologue)\n0x4      4      errorCode parameter\n0x8      4      unused1 parameter\n0xc      4      unused2 parameter\n0x10     4      errorContext parameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
