      "name": "CleanupAndAbort",
      "signature": "void CleanupAndAbort(int nErrorCode, void * pContext, int nLineNumber)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Fatal error handler for unrecoverable runtime errors. Cleans up network resources and initiates shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call WSACleanup() to safely shutdown Windows Sockets subsystem and release resources\n2. Invoke LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown() with error level 6 (fatal severity)\n3. Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit() to terminate application after cleanup\n4. Jump to shutdown_sequence at 0x6ff684a0 for final process termination\n\nParameters:\n- errorCode (int): Numeric code identifying the type of fatal error that occurred\n- pContext (void*): Pointer to optional error context structure (may be NULL)\n- lineNumber (int): Source code line number where the fatal error was detected\n\nReturns:\nNone - Function does not return. Always results in process termination after cleanup.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called from 6 different functions when unrecoverable errors are encountered\n- No error recovery is possible - immediate shutdown is mandatory\n- WSA cleanup must occur before shutdown sequence to prevent socket resource leaks\n- Error level 6 indicates fatal severity to logging system",
