      "name": "CleanupNetworkAndInitiateShutdown",
      "signature": "void CleanupNetworkAndInitiateShutdown(uint errorCode, undefined4 pErrorMessage, uint additionalParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Cleanup Network Resources and Initiate Graceful Shutdown\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Call WSACleanup to release all Winsock 2 network resources\\n2. Load errorCode parameter from stack\\n3. Load pErrorMessage parameter (optional error message string) from stack\\n4. Push parameters to error handler: errorCode, string pointer, severity constant\\n5. Call LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown to log error and begin shutdown sequence\\n6. Clean stack (5 parameters \\u00d7 4 bytes = 0x14)\\n7. Jump to ShutdownResourcesAndExit to complete shutdown\\n\\nParameters:\\n- uint errorCode: Error code value indicating reason for shutdown\\n- char * pErrorMessage: Optional pointer to additional error message string\\n- uint additionalParam: Additional parameter (purpose varies by context)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Function does not return; transfers control to shutdown handler via JMP\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Network cleanup must complete before error handler is called\\n- All three parameters are passed to LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown\\n- Control flow terminates with unconditional jump to shutdown routine\\n\\nThis function serves as a orchestration point between network resource cleanup and the error handling/shutdown system. It ensures that Winsock resources are properly released before logging the error and initiating the shutdown sequence.",
