      "name": "ShutdownAndCleanupSystem",
      "signature": "void ShutdownAndCleanupSystem(uint shutdownFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Performs complete system shutdown and resource cleanup sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global initialization state flag (g_dwGameInitState at 0x6ffa6e78)\n2. Test if state flag is zero - if so, skip cleanup and return (lazy shutdown optimization)\n3. Preserve ESI register by pushing to stack\n4. Close all active event handles via CloseAllEventHandles()\n5. Deinitialize all game resources via DeinitializeGameResources(0)\n6. Clear resource callback state flag (g_pfnErrorShutdownCallback at 0x6ffa6e6c)\n7. Execute game-specific cleanup sequence via CleanupAndReleaseResources()\n8. Shutdown all remaining resources via ShutdownResourcesAndExit()\n9. Validate data structure integrity of g_GameInitializationCriticalSection\n10. Enter critical section for safe cleanup\n11. Delete g_GameInitializationCriticalSection (size: 24 bytes)\n12. Deallocate queue memory and resources via CleanupAndDeallocateQueue()\n13. Clear initialization state flag (g_dwGameInitState = 0)\n14. Delete g_ResourceCleanupCriticalSection (size: 28 bytes at 0x6ff82aec)\n15. Delete g_QueueDeallocationCriticalSection (size: 28 bytes at 0x6ff82c0c)\n16. Restore ESI register by popping from stack\n17. Return from shutdown sequence\n\nParameters:\nshutdownFlags (ECX) - Shutdown control flags; passed by __fastcall convention but not currently used in logic flow\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function performs cleanup and terminates shutdown sequence\n\nSpecial Cases and Edge Cases:\n- If g_dwGameInitState is 0 at entry (offset 0x6ffa6e78), the function exits immediately without performing cleanup, allowing for idempotent shutdown calls\n- Critical sections are deleted in sequence: g_GameInitializationCriticalSection first, then the resource and queue sections\n- ESI register is preserved across all function calls via PUSH/POP to maintain caller state\n- Multiple critical sections indicate multi-threaded cleanup coordination (InitCS, ResourceCS, QueueCS)\n- Function pointer g_pfnErrorShutdownCallback is cleared before shutdown sequence executes\n- Size of critical section structures: 24 bytes (GameInit), 28 bytes each (Resource, Deallocation)\n\nGlobal Data Accessed:\ng_dwGameInitState (0x6ffa6e78) - DWORD initialization state flag, checked at entry and cleared at end\ng_pfnErrorShutdownCallback (0x6ffa6e6c) - DWORD callback pointer, cleared during cleanup\ng_GameInitializationCriticalSection (0x6ff816d8) - CRITICAL_SECTION for init sync, 24 bytes\ng_ResourceCleanupCriticalSection (0x6ff82aec) - CRITICAL_SECTION for resource sync, 28 bytes\ng_QueueDeallocationCriticalSection (0x6ff82c0c) - CRITICAL_SECTION for queue sync, 28 bytes\n\nFunctions Called:\nCloseAllEventHandles() - Closes all system event handles\nDeinitializeGameResources(void*) - Deinitializes game resource structures\nCleanupAndReleaseResources() - Releases general system resources\nShutdownResourcesAndExit() - Shutdown resource manager and exit\nValidateDataStructureIntegrity(ContainerData*) - Validates critical section integrity\nEnterCriticalSection(CRITICAL_SECTION*) - Enters critical section for thread safety\nDeleteCriticalSection(CRITICAL_SECTION*) - Deletes critical section\nCleanupAndDeallocateQueue() - Deallocates queue memory structures",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:8cd9ba288c0333ffeb4670c16e89f464",
