      "name": "ExtractBitsFromStream",
      "signature": "uint ExtractBitsFromStream(BitStreamDecoder * pDecoder)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Extracts a variable-length sequence of bits from a bit-stream decoder context.\n\nThis function decodes N bits from an encoded byte stream by advancing a decoder state\nmachine through byte boundaries as needed. It uses lookup tables to extract and mask\nbits based on the current position within the stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate remaining bits available: (bytesLeft * 8 - byteIndex) + numBits + bitOffset\n2. If remaining space is negative, clamp to 0 and mark overflow flag\n3. Calculate bits to extract in first iteration: min(8 - bitOffset, numBits)\n4. Initialize output accumulator (0) and bit shift position (0)\n5. While bits remain to extract:\n   a. Load current bit offset from pDecoder[3] (0-7 range)\n   b. Determine how many bits available in current byte: (8 - bitOffset)\n   c. Take minimum of available vs remaining bits needed\n   d. Load current byte value from pDecoder[0] pointer\n   e. Index into g_dwBitMaskTable using bit offset to extract mask\n   f. Apply mask to byte, then shift right by bit offset to align\n   g. Index into g_dwWidthMaskTable using bits-to-extract to mask final width\n   h. Shift masked bits left by current output position, accumulate\n   i. Advance bit offset by bits extracted, advance output shift position\n   j. If bit offset reaches 8: advance byte pointer, reset offset, increment word count\n6. Return accumulated output value containing all extracted bits\n\nParameters:\npDecoder [BitStreamDecoder *]: Pointer to bit stream decoder context:\n  +0: pCurrentByte - Pointer to current byte in buffer (incremented at byte boundaries)\n  +4: nByteIndex - Byte index counter (decremented during space calculation)\n  +8: nWordIndex - Word/element counter (incremented after processing 8 bits)\n  +12: nBitOffset - Bit offset within current byte (0-7 range, reset when reaching 8)\n  +16: dwOverflowFlag - Set to 1 if requested bits exceed available space\n\nnumBits [int]: Number of bits to extract (typically 1-8)\n\nReturns:\nuint: Extracted bit value, right-aligned in the 32-bit integer return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If calculated remaining bits go negative, clamped to 0 to prevent extraction\n- Sets pDecoder[16] overflow flag when requested bits exceed available space\n- Lookup tables use specific bit patterns for mask generation\n- Word/element advance (nWordIndex++) happens automatically at byte boundaries\n- Bit offset automatically resets to 0 when it reaches 8\n\nLookup Tables:\ng_dwBitMaskTable (0x6ff768bc): 8 bytes - (0xFF,0xFE,0xFC,0xF8,0xF0,0xE0,0xC0,0x80)\n  Indexed by bit offset (0-7) to create mask for bits starting at that offset\n\ng_dwWidthMaskTable (0x6ff76898): 32 bytes (8 DWORDs) - (0x0,0x1,0x3,0x7,0xF,0x1F,0x3F,0x7F)\n  Indexed by width (0-7) to create mask for extracting that many bits",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
