      "name": "InvertMemoryBlock",
      "signature": "void InvertMemoryBlock(void * pSourceData, uint * pDestBuffer, uint nBitCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Performs bitwise NOT inversion on a contiguous memory block of up to 32 bits.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Round nBitCount up to nearest byte boundary (multiply by 8 via add 7 + rounding)\n2. Calculate byte count by dividing rounded bits by 8 (SAR 0x3)\n3. Calculate DWORD count by dividing bytes by 4 with ceiling rounding\n4. Compute total DWORD size in bytes (multiply DWORD count by 4)\n5. Process all complete 32-bit DWORDs: load from pSourceData, NOT, store to pDestBuffer\n6. Calculate remainder byte count: (total_bytes % 4) yields 0-3 remaining bytes\n7. Process remainder bytes (1-3) based on remainder count using conditional jumps\n\nParameters:\npSourceData (void *): Pointer to source memory block to invert\npDestBuffer (uint *): Pointer to destination buffer for inverted data\nnBitCount (uint): Number of bits to invert (rounded up to byte boundary)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, data written directly to pDestBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nBitCount=0: Function returns immediately without processing\n- nBitCount 1-7: Rounded up to 8 bits (1 byte minimum)\n- Memory must not overlap: assumes pDestBuffer != pSourceData\n- Remainder handling: DEC/JZ cascade (3-byte, 2-byte, 1-byte) processes trailing bytes\n- Uses NOT instruction for true bitwise complement of all bits\n\nPerformance:\n- Processes 4 bytes per iteration in DWORD loop (optimal for 32-bit data)\n- Single-pass algorithm over source memory\n- Minimal register usage allows high cache efficiency",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:784a16cc1d4c15574eb270847b8f571c",
