      "signature": "void BitwiseOrBuffers(byte * srcBuffer1, byte * srcBuffer2, byte * dstBuffer, int bitCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Performs bitwise OR operation combining three byte buffers with bit-field precision.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Round bitCount up to nearest byte boundary and divide by 8 to get total byte count\n2. Round byte count up to nearest 4-byte (dword) boundary for aligned processing\n3. Process full dwords in loop: load from srcBuffer2, OR with srcBuffer1, store to dstBuffer\n4. Calculate remainder bits: bitCount modulo 8 (partial bytes after dword processing)\n5. Handle remainder bytes based on count (1, 2, or 3 bytes) using cascading byte operations\n\nParameters:\nsrcBuffer1: First source buffer (base for offset calculations)\nsrcBuffer2: Second source buffer (reference base for pointer math)\ndstBuffer: Destination buffer (receives bitwise OR result of both sources)\nbitCount: Total number of bits to process (determines byte counts and remainder)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (modifies dstBuffer in place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses register-relative addressing for pointer math (srcBuffer1 - srcBuffer2 offset)\n- Handles non-byte-aligned bit counts by rounding to full bytes then processing remainders\n- Processes remainder bytes in descending order (3 bytes down to 1 byte)\n- EDI register reused after dword loop for bit count calculations and remainder processing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:7280ddc215c629c95437f5e203110faf",
