      "name": "ExtractBitsFromStreamWrapper",
      "signature": "int ExtractBitsFromStreamWrapper(BitStreamDecoder * pDecoder, int numBits)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Wrapper that extracts bits from a bit-stream decoder context.\n\nThis is a thin wrapper function that delegates to ExtractBitsFromStream with proper parameter marshaling and register preservation. It maintains the caller's ESI register while preparing arguments for the underlying extraction function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pDecoder parameter from stack [ESP + 0x8]\n2. Save ESI register (callee-saved, required for restoration)\n3. Load numBits parameter from stack [ESP + 0xC]\n4. Push pDecoder as first argument to ExtractBitsFromStream\n5. Call ExtractBitsFromStream(pDecoder, numBits)\n6. Pop and restore ESI register\n7. Return with __stdcall cleanup (RET 0x8)\n\nParameters:\npDecoder [BitStreamDecoder *]: Pointer to bit-stream decoder context containing current read position and state information\nnumBits [int]: Number of bits to extract from the stream\n\nReturns:\nint: Extracted bits from the stream, typically in range [0, 2^numBits - 1] depending on stream contents\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention with callee-side stack cleanup (RET 0x8)\n- ESI register is preserved across the wrapper call\n- Actual bit extraction logic is implemented in ExtractBitsFromStream\n- This wrapper ensures proper register preservation for calling contexts that depend on ESI",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9777cfb5657a3929cbc455c4d8a0561d",
