      "name": "CleanupResourcePointer",
      "signature": "void CleanupResourcePointer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates and cleans up a resource pointer stored within a context structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate context pointer (ESI) is non-null - if null, skip cleanup\n2. Load resource pointer from context offset 0x110\n3. Validate loaded resource pointer is non-null - if null, skip cleanup\n4. Load validity flag from resource offset 0x24 (4-byte value)\n5. Validate resource validity flag is non-zero - if zero, skip cleanup\n6. Call CloseNetworkResource to perform cleanup with resource pointer\n7. Zero out the resource pointer field at context offset 0x110\n8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nESI (implicit): Pointer to context structure\n  - Type: NetworkResourceContext*\n  - Contains resource pointer at offset 0x110\n  - Resource at offset 0x110 has validity flag at offset 0x24\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function performs side effects only\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles null context pointer gracefully (exits early at 0x6ff6e544)\n- Handles null resource pointer gracefully (exits early at 0x6ff6e544)\n- Validates resource validity flag before cleanup to prevent processing invalid resources\n- Field at offset 0x24 acts as validity indicator (non-zero = valid)\n- All validation checks use TEST + JZ pattern for efficient branching\n\nStructure Layout:\nContext Structure at ESI:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name          Type      Description\n  0x110   4     pResource           dword*    Pointer to NetworkResourceContext, zeroed after cleanup\n  \nResource Structure at [ESI + 0x110]:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name          Type      Description\n  0x24    4     validityFlag        dword     Non-zero if resource is valid",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
