      "name": "InitializeGameThreadState",
      "signature": "HANDLE InitializeGameThreadState(void * pGameState)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize game state structure for threaded subsystem without waiting for thread completion.\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that pGameState is not NULL\n2. Validate that *pGameState equals 0 (uninitialized state)\n3. Clear initialization state flag at offset 0x124 to 0\n4. Create an auto-reset event using CreateEventA() and store handle at offset 0x114\n5. Create a worker thread using CreateThread() with pGameState as context parameter\n6. Store thread handle at offset 0x0 in pGameState\n7. Return thread handle to caller (non-blocking initialization)\nParameters:\npGameState: Pointer to game state structure requiring initialization\nReturns:\nHANDLE - Thread handle created by CreateThread, or NULL if validation fails\nSpecial Cases:\n- Non-blocking initialization suitable for deferred synchronization\n- Thread ID stored via pointer passed as lpThreadId parameter to CreateThread",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
