      "signature": "void EnqueuePacketToQueue(ContainerData * pQueueContext, ushort * pPacketData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "EnqueuePacketToQueue - Thread-safe packet enqueue to linked list queue\n\nPurpose:\nAtomically enqueues a variable-sized packet to a thread-protected queue structure.\nUses critical section synchronization to ensure thread-safe linked list operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate packet size in AX register is non-zero, shutdown if invalid\n2. Load queue context structure pointer from stack parameter\n3. Calculate allocation size = packet size + 8 bytes (2-byte size field + 6-byte padding)\n4. Enter critical section lock at context offset +0x4\n5. Allocate memory block from pool using calculated size\n6. If allocation fails, log error code 0x50 and initiate system shutdown\n7. Store packet size in new node at offset +0x0 (2-byte unsigned short)\n8. Zero-initialize padding fields at offsets +0x4 and +0x6\n9. Copy packet data using optimized DWORD-aligned copy (rep movsd) for full DWORDs\n10. Copy any remaining unaligned bytes using byte copy (rep movsb)\n11. Load head pointer from context offset +0x1C to check if queue empty\n12. If head is NULL (queue empty), initialize both head and tail pointers to new node\n13. If queue has elements, link new node to current tail at tail->offset_4\n14. Update tail pointer to new node (context offset +0x20)\n15. Leave critical section lock and return\n\nParameters:\n  pQueueContext - ContainerData* - Base address of queue control structure\n    Structure Layout:\n      Offset 0x00-0x03: [reserved/context type]\n      Offset 0x04-0x27: CRITICAL_SECTION - Synchronization object for thread safety\n      Offset 0x1C-0x1F: Head pointer - First node in queue (NULL if empty)\n      Offset 0x20-0x23: Tail pointer - Last node in queue (updated on enqueue)\n  \n  pPacketData - unsigned short* - Pointer to packet data buffer to copy\n    Data format: Variable-length byte array, size specified by AX register\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function always returns via RET 0x8 (__stdcall cleanup)\n\nReturn Behavior:\n  Normal path: Returns after queuing completes with critical section released\n  Error path: Calls ShutdownResourcesAndExit() for allocation or validation failures\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Zero-sized packets: Trigger immediate error shutdown with call to LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown\n  Allocation failures: Logged with error code 0x50, system shutdown initiated\n  Empty queue: Both head and tail initialized to new node (self-linked)\n  Non-empty queue: New node appended at tail, tail pointer advanced\n\nData Structures:\n  Queue Node Layout:\n    Offset 0x0: [2 bytes] packet size (unsigned short)\n    Offset 0x2: [2 bytes] reserved/padding\n    Offset 0x4: [4 bytes] next pointer (linked list chain)\n    Offset 0x8: [variable] packet data payload\n  \n  Total node size = packet_size + 8 bytes\n\nThread Safety:\n  CRITICAL_SECTION at offset +0x4 protects all queue modifications\n  EnterCriticalSection called at start, LeaveCriticalSection at all exits\n  Ensures atomic head/tail pointer updates\n\nError Handling:\n  Invalid packet size (0): Calls GetReturnAddress, WSACleanup, LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown(6, ...)\n  Allocation failure: Calls LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown(2, error_code=0x50)\n  Both error paths terminate with ShutdownResourcesAndExit and _exit(-1)\n\nPerformance Notes:\n  Uses rep movsd for DWORD-aligned bulk copy (efficient for large packets)\n  Falls back to rep movsb for unaligned remainder\n  Critical section held only during allocation and pointer updates (minimal contention)\n\nCalled By:\n  ProcessNetworkPackets - Primary caller for network packet queuing\n\nRelated Functions:\n  DequeueAndCopyDataFromLinkedList - Complementary dequeue operation\n  AllocateMemorySlotFromPool - Pool allocator for node memory\n  EnterCriticalSection, LeaveCriticalSection - Synchronization primitives\n  LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown - Error logging and shutdown\n  ValidateDataStructureIntegrity - Pre-lock integrity check",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11b",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:faa8324492fe4cad0fcf206bb80d27ef",
