      "name": "EncodeExpressionTokenStack",
      "signature": "int EncodeExpressionTokenStack(undefined4 nModeFlag, byte * pOutputBuffer, int nMaxOutputSize, undefined4 pTokenProvider, void * pCallbackFunction, undefined4 pContextData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Encodes expression tokens using a stack-based reduction algorithm.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize local state: nEncodingStackDepth=0, nTokenStackIndex=0, bOutputGenerated=0\\n2. Token provider loop: Repeatedly call ParseExpressionToken to fetch tokens from stream\\n3. Token dispatch: For each token type (0x0-0x12), execute corresponding encoding operation\\n   a) PUSH_TOKEN (0x0): Push token onto stack if space available (<0x40), mark with 0x2 end marker\\n   b) POP_TOKEN (0x1): Pop and process stacked tokens with reduction rules, validate stack consistency\\n   c) ENCODE_* (0x2-0xf): Call ProcessTokenEncoding with specific operation codes (0x3, 0x10-0x17)\\n   d) LITERAL_INT (0x10): Encode integer value via EncodeIntegerValue\\n   e) LITERAL_VARLEN (0x11): Encode variable-length integer via EncodeVariableLengthInteger\\n   f) STACK_VALUE (0x12): Push raw value onto internal stack (limited to 0x40 entries)\\n4. Post-loop finalization: Call ProcessTokenEncoding with operation code 0 to finalize\\n5. Optimization pass: If output was generated without special flags, execute bytecode program on result\\n6. Return encoded byte count or 0 on error (buffer overflow, invalid token sequence)\\n\\nParameters:\\n- nModeFlag: Control/mode code passed to helper functions\\n- pOutputBuffer: Target buffer for encoded output bytes\\n- nMaxOutputSize: Maximum bytes available in pOutputBuffer (checked before each write)\\n- pTokenProvider: Callback function pointer to token stream provider\\n- pCallbackFunction: Optional callback for token type 0x1 reduction operations\\n- pContextData: Context parameter passed to token provider callback\\n\\nReturns:\\n- Positive integer: Number of bytes written to pOutputBuffer (final encoded size)\\n- Zero: Error condition (buffer overflow, invalid token sequence, or stack violation)\\n\\nSpecial Cases and Magic Numbers:\\n- Stack size limit: 0x40 (64 decimal) = maximum entries in abyTokenStackBuffer\\n- End marker: 0x2 = marks section boundaries in token stack\\n- Type 1 marker: 0x1 = special token requiring callback invocation\\n- Type 0x15 stack cost: 3 items (special reduction rule for certain operations)\\n- Type 0x16 stack cost: 1 item\\n- Default stack cost: 2 items for most operations\\n- Reduction operation codes: 0x3, 0x10-0x17 map to specific encoding transformations\\n- Well-formed constraint: Token sequences must have matching PUSH/POP pairs with proper nesting\\n\\nStructure Layout (abyTokenStackBuffer):\\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type        Description\\n0       60    abyTokenStackBuffer byte[60]    Local token type stack (LIFO), entries 1/2/0x15/0x16\\n-0x4c   4     auStack_10c         dword[65]   Parallel data values for tokens on stack",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
