      "name": "SetSocketNonBlocking",
      "signature": "void SetSocketNonBlocking(void * pConnectionObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Enables non-blocking mode on a socket within a connection object.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize mode variable to 0 (non-blocking enabled)\n2. Extract socket handle from connection object at offset +8\n3. Call ioctlsocket with FIONBIO (0x8004667e) command to enable non-blocking mode\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pConnectionObject (ECX): Pointer to connection structure containing SOCKET at offset +8\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - FIONBIO constant (0x8004667e) is the Windows socket control code for non-blocking mode\n  - Mode value of 0 enables non-blocking mode; non-zero would disable it\n  - ioctlsocket() return value is not checked or propagated\n  - Socket must be valid; no validation is performed\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field   Type    Description\n  +0x8    4     socket  SOCKET  Network socket handle",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c644f5dcf2e3d26eca019a22b45dae47",
